{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":["vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","vamseeachanta/digitalmodel","vamseeachanta/assetutilities","vamseeachanta/worldenergydata","vamseeachanta/llm-wiki","vamseeachanta/assethold","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-website","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-strategy"],"query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-review\"","topn":50,"sort":"updated","order":"asc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\", \"issue_number\": 2510, \"body\": \"## Context\\nParent: #2507\\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\\n\\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\\n\\n## Proposed scope\\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\\n3. Metadata extraction report.\\n4. Tests and documentation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"display_title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\", \"issue_number\": 2626, \"body\": \"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\\n\\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\\n\\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\\n\\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\\n\\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\\nScenario 3 suggests \\\"temporary lift of interaction limit\\\" \\u2014 globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\\n\\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\\n\\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\\n\\n## Severity\\n\\nMedium \\u2014 the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"display_title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\", \"issue_number\": 2632, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThree llm-wiki issues at `status:plan-approved` (#2368, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125) have been stuck since 2026-04-28 due to a missing/stale approval-binding state. Codex's 10-thread parallel-implementation lanes correctly refused to execute, and the gate has held for 5+ days without remediation. This META issue captures the rot so it can be cleaned up in one pass.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 contract (memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`), `status:plan-approved` GitHub label is necessary but not sufficient \\u2014 execution requires a revision-bound approval marker at `.planning/plan-approved/<n>.md` that names the approved plan SHA + review artifact paths. Otherwise agents can't confirm WHICH version of the plan was approved.\\n\\nThis was specifically designed as a load-bearing user-in-loop gate (memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md`) \\u2014 agents must NOT self-approve by creating the marker themselves.\\n\\nThe gate is doing its job. But the cleanup hasn't happened, and three valuable llm-wiki improvements have been frozen.\\n\\n## Per-issue state (verified 2026-05-03)\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2368.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Local plan `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md`: blob `b391641688` \\u2014 header says `Status: draft` (REGRESSED from v2)\\n- Approved revision per Codex's 2026-04-28 comment: SHA `1c01062d8` \\u2014 header in that SHA says `Status: draft (v2 \\u2014 addresses r1 findings)`, blob `b1df634b3`\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:17:06Z (3 retry passes, all gated)\\n- Likely cause of plan regression: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` pattern during auto-sync\\n\\n**Remediation:**\\n```bash\\ngit checkout 1c01062d8 -- docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md\\n# Then create .planning/plan-approved/2368.md with marker:\\n#   plan_sha: 1c01062d8\\n#   plan_blob: b1df634b3943db8f99888cb120ccf9be6ce245fe\\n#   review_artifacts:\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-claude.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-codex.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-gemini.md\\n#   approved_by: vamseeachanta\\n#   approved_at: <ISO timestamp of human approval>\\ngit add docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md .planning/plan-approved/2368.md\\ngit commit -m \\\"markers(plan-approved): bind vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 to v2 SHA 1c01062d8\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 extend ingestion to Orcina resources/examples/training\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2124.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2124*` exists)\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:18:13Z \\u2014 also flags upstream dependency on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 still being open\\n- Note: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 status as of 2026-05-03 (verify before remediating)\\n\\n**Remediation:** plan needs to be authored or located before binding. May be that the plan was lost to the same merge-race that ate vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22's v2 content.\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 auto-refresh ingestion on Orcina releases\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2125.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2125*` exists)\\n- Codex 2026-04-28T06:15:27Z comment indicates an implementation pass DID complete: branch `codex/10thread-20260428-issue-2125`, commit `e4b6193236a70ed2ec960deb92b3f65b9f876616`. But no merge to main and label still says `status:working`.\\n\\n**Remediation:** check if commit `e4b6193236` is salvageable; either land it or rebind plan + re-execute.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis META issue is for **diagnosis + decision-making**, not implementation:\\n\\n- Confirm the 3 issues' approval-binding state matches what's recorded above (re-verify before acting)\\n- For each: decide rebind / re-plan / archive / continue-as-is\\n- File ONE remediation issue per surviving plan\\n- Update the relevant memory files if the rebinding workflow needs refinement\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- Each of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 reaches one of: (a) properly bound + ready for execution, (b) deferred with explicit ADR, (c) closed as superseded\\n- The meta cleanup commit pattern is documented as a precedent for future \\\"approval-binding rot\\\" sweeps\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Implementation of the 3 issues' actual deliverables (separate downstream work after rebinding)\\n- Codex 10-thread lane reactivation (that's a separate workflow concern)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 (closed) \\u2014 original approval-binding contract; memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`\\n- Memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md` \\u2014 why agents can't self-approve\\n- Memory: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` \\u2014 likely cause of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 plan regression\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 \\u2014 llm-wiki strengthening epic (parent for vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22/#2124/#2125)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2615 (closed 2026-05-03) \\u2014 recent successful approval-binding precedent (Tier C closure)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"display_title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\", \"issue_number\": 2643, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\\n\\n## Context\\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\\n\\nLive prerequisite checks found:\\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\\n\\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\\n\\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\\n\\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\\n\\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\", \"issue_number\": 2528, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\\\"12 skills \\u2192 4-5\\\") is partially complete \\u2014 `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\\n\\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\\n\\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\\n\\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\\n\\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n\\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed \\u2014 no broken references to deleted skills\\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable \\u2014 referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\\\"*.md\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.py\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.yaml\\\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\\n\\n## Complexity\\n\\nT1 (trivial) \\u2014 pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"display_title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\", \"issue_number\": 2551, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\\n\\n## Why\\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\\n\\n## Scope\\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Root hardening: #2546\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"display_title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/387\", \"title\": \"WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration\", \"issue_number\": 387, \"body\": \"## WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** wind\\n\\n**Repo:** ['worldenergydata'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nEvaluate **pyWAsP** (https://docs.wasp.dk/pywasp/latest/) \\u2014 the Python API for the\\nWAsP wind resource assessment flow model (DTU Wind Energy / \\u00d8rsted) \\u2014 for integration\\ninto the worldenergydata ecosystem. pyWAsP covers terrain effects (IBZ model),\\nwind climate generalisation/downscaling, and AEP estimation with wake effects\\n(via PyWake). Built on WindKit, which uses xarray data structures natively.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nWind energy is a core domain for the Tier 3 GTM targets (Orsted, Equinor, Dominion\\nCVOW \\u2014 WRK-148). pyWAsP is the industry-standard tool these companies use daily.\\nAdding wind resource assessment capability to worldenergydata:\\n- Enables AEP \\u2192 field-development economics pipeline (feeds WRK-476 ESG/carbon module)\\n- Creates direct technical credibility with offshore wind prospects\\n- xarray/WindKit structures align with the planned metocean module (NOAA NDBC)\\n- Pairs with existing Arps decline curve (WRK-318) for hybrid fossil/renewables models\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] `pip install pywasp` tested on dev-primary (licence requirement assessed)\\n- [ ] PyWake (open-source companion wake model) installed and smoke-tested separately\\n- [ ] WindKit data structures understood \\u2014 xarray compatibility with worldenergydata\\n- [ ] At least one worked example: wind climate generalisation OR AEP calculation\\n- [ ] Evaluation report written to `specs/data-sources/pywasp-eval.md` covering:\\n- [ ] Decision: integrate (create implementation WRK) | defer | skip\\n- [ ] `specs/data-sources/worldenergydata.yaml` tool entry updated with eval outcome\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/387\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\", \"issue_number\": 2653, \"body\": \"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\\npipeline cleanly.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] New session \\u2192 new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) \\u2192 same log file continues\\n- [ ] Session idle >2h \\u2192 next tool call starts a new log file\\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **19. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **20. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions\", \"issue_number\": 41, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the maritime-law wiki.\\n\\n## Decision source\\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for IMO/ILO convention and code pages.\\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Plan and then implement a bounded metadata-only migration or mirror strategy for eligible maritime-law convention/code pages currently under `wikis/maritime-law/wiki/concepts/`.\\n- Candidate pages include SOLAS, MARPOL, MLC, and ISM Code, subject to duplicate/path review.\\n- Preserve `consolidated_edition` where that is the correct public metadata field.\\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No convention/code text copying.\\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, or source excerpts.\\n- No broad maritime-law schema rewrite beyond the routing implementation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Eligible pages have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\\n- Existing concept links are preserved or redirected/mirrored safely.\\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #15\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing\", \"issue_number\": 42, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the LNG-projects wiki.\\n\\n## Decision source\\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for LNG codes and standards pages.\\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Plan and then implement bounded metadata-only standards pages for LNG codes when public metadata is sufficient.\\n- Candidate families include CSA-Z276, NFPA 59A, and IGC Code, subject to public metadata verification and duplicate/path review.\\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No standard text copying.\\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, project specifications, or source excerpts.\\n- No broad LNG content expansion beyond standards-routing implementation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Eligible LNG standards have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\\n- Any insufficient public metadata is split into follow-up work instead of guessed.\\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #15\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 43, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any SESA LNG corpus extraction can proceed from #14.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #14\\n- Raw/source family: SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa`\\n- Current status: extraction remains blocked until clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist that defines what must exist before extraction starts:\\n- row-level or artifact-level clearance fields required for any proposed first tranche\\n- allowed source evidence types and disallowed source evidence types\\n- public-repo output boundaries for summaries, metadata, and target wiki pages\\n- required approvals for vendor, client/project-sensitive, archive, workbook, and standards-derived materials\\n- validation expectations before any future extraction commit\\n- required separate implementation issue structure after clearance is complete\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa` content into git.\\n- No OCR, text extraction, table extraction, workbook extraction, or PDF summarization.\\n- No vendor standards text, private archive material, credentials, client-sensitive content, or project specifications in this public repo.\\n- No closing #14 until this checklist and a later bounded implementation lane are complete.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored public synthesis, vendor-derived text, client/project-sensitive files, archives, and standards material.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #14 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #14\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 45, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any HSE/safety dataset metadata or wiki promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until dataset clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for HSE/safety dataset material:\\n- dataset-level clearance fields required before promotion\\n- allowed public metadata fields, dataset citations, and aggregate descriptions\\n- disallowed personally identifiable information, incident-sensitive records, raw CSV/TXT rows, and proprietary/private derived data\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules for HSE concepts and source metadata\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/PII/secret scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw dataset extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` content into git.\\n- No CSV/TXT row promotion, ZIP extraction, incident-record summarization, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No PII, private source text, credentials, or raw safety data in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate dataset/artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, aggregate public synthesis, raw rows, PII/sensitive incident records, archives, and derived summaries.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/PII boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 44, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any BSEE/offshore source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for BSEE/offshore candidate material:\\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\\n- handling rules for client/project-sensitive files, permit/activity samples, spreadsheets, document archives, and data descriptions\\n- allowed public metadata fields versus disallowed extracted content\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/client-sensitive boundary scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` content into git.\\n- No OCR, table extraction, workbook extraction, PDF/DOCX summarization, ZIP inspection for promotion, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No client/project-sensitive files, credentials, permit details, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, client/project-sensitive data, proprietary/project material, archives, and authored synthesis.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/client-sensitive boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 46, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations material:\\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\\n- handling rules for magazine/offshore-operation articles, heavy-lift/pipelay source material, images, PDFs, and archives\\n- allowed public bibliographic metadata and authored high-level synthesis\\n- disallowed copied article text, figures, vendor/private material, and raw archive contents\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` content into git.\\n- No OCR, article summarization from raw files, figure extraction, archive extraction, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No copyrighted article text, images, credentials, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored synthesis, copyrighted article text, images/figures, archives, and vendor/private material.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs\", \"issue_number\": 47, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #25 Batch Pack 1 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #25\\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #25: plan branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` at approved SHA `7cc1c0b1a`.\\n- Current blocker: the public spinout repo does not contain the approval-bound plan artifact or the required online-resource registry inputs.\\n\\n## Scope\\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 1 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 1\\n- `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` or an approved public-safe extracted subset sufficient for Batch Pack 1\\n- any overlay/processed input required by the approved plan\\n- provenance notes binding the restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\\n- validation checklist for duplicate checks, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw boundaries\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No Batch Pack 1 promotion execution in this prep issue.\\n- No registry reconstruction from memory.\\n- No source re-download or raw source parsing.\\n- No API/portal wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\\n- No credentials, API keys, private endpoints, private source text, or vendor text in the public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 1 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\\n- [ ] The required registry input or approved subset is available in a public-safe form.\\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\\n- [ ] Future #25 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\\n- [ ] #25 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #25\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs\", \"issue_number\": 48, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #26 Batch Pack 4 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #26\\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #26: plan branch `plan/issue-2373-batch-pack-4` at approved SHA `c516ec853`.\\n- Upstream gate `vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471` is now closed, but the public spinout repo still lacks the approval-bound plan artifact and required data inputs.\\n\\n## Scope\\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 4 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 4\\n- transfer ledger input required for the cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural standards slice\\n- topic-cluster and alias inputs required by the approved plan\\n- any approved summary-backed evidence surface required to avoid raw PDF rereads\\n- provenance notes binding restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\\n- validation checklist for duplicate/extend-vs-create mapping, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw/vendor boundaries\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No Batch Pack 4 promotion execution in this prep issue.\\n- No ledger/cluster reconstruction from memory.\\n- No raw PDF rereads, source extraction, OCR, or standards text summarization.\\n- No standards wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\\n- No credentials, private source text, vendor standards text, formulas, tables, or copied clauses in the public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 4 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\\n- [ ] Required transfer ledger, topic-cluster, and alias inputs are available in a public-safe form.\\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\\n- [ ] Future #26 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\\n- [ ] #26 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #26\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40\", \"title\": \"Research: reservoir engineering literature \\u2014 local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki\", \"issue_number\": 40, \"body\": \"## Goal\\n\\nBuild out the reservoir-engineering substrate of llm-wiki by mining (a) the user's existing local PDF corpus on ace-linux-1 (`/mnt/ace`, 30,499 PDFs) and (b) public online sources, then ingesting the relevant material under llm-wiki's MIT + CC-BY-4.0 license. Drives both the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026) competition (deeper domain literacy \\u2192 better modeling decisions) and longer-term wikis around oil & gas / subsurface engineering.\\n\\nCompanion issue: [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) covers competition-specific *prior art* (datasets + ML papers); this issue covers the broader *educational foundation* (textbooks, coursework, classic papers).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n**In-scope source types**\\n\\n- Textbooks on reservoir engineering, petroleum engineering, formation evaluation, well logging, drilling, geosteering.\\n- University coursework \\u2014 open syllabi, lecture notes, problem sets from Stanford SDSS, Texas A&M, U Texas Austin, Heriot-Watt, IFP, Imperial.\\n- Conference papers \\u2014 SPE, AAPG, SEG, EAGE \\u2014 with care about open-access vs paywalled.\\n- Industry standards / methodology PDFs (DNV, API, ISO).\\n- Theses and dissertations from public university repositories.\\n- ArXiv preprints in petroleum engineering, geophysics, ML-for-geosteering categories.\\n\\n**Out of scope (license / IP risk)**\\n\\n- Pirated or unauthorized copies of paywalled textbooks, even if found locally.\\n- Vendor-derivative material under proprietary license.\\n- The deny-list per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482) governance: nothing under `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/sources/` should be cited; cite the canonical standard or concept page instead.\\n\\n## Sources to mine\\n\\n### Local \\u2014 `/mnt/ace` (ace-linux-1)\\n\\n- `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` \\u2014 top candidate directory by name. First pass: recursively list, classify by filename / metadata, flag candidates.\\n- `/mnt/ace/aceengineer-admin/Reference/` \\u2014 mixed (mostly tax / admin docs in spot-check, but may contain technical references).\\n- Other dirs revealed during initial sweep.\\n- Total PDFs in `/mnt/ace`: ~30,499. Realistic target: 50\\u2013200 ingest-worthy after deduplication and license filtering.\\n\\n### Online (representative starting points)\\n\\n- **Stanford Stanford Doerr School OCW**: open courses on petroleum / energy resources.\\n- **Texas A&M PETE OCW** and **U Texas Austin Petroleum Engineering** open content.\\n- **Heriot-Watt PE** open materials.\\n- **arXiv physics.geo-ph** and **stat.ML** intersection \\u2014 search \\\"well log\\\", \\\"geosteering\\\", \\\"lithology classification\\\".\\n- **OnePetro** free-access entries (SPE / AAPG / SEG; many old papers are now open).\\n- **AAPG Datapages** open-access portion.\\n- **USGS Open-File Reports** in petroleum geology.\\n- **OAPEN** and **Springer Open** for free textbooks.\\n- **MIT OpenCourseWare** earth-and-planetary courses with subsurface relevance.\\n\\n## Output: llm-wiki structure\\n\\nExisting top-level dirs (verified 2026-05-06): `docs/`, `scripts/`, `seeds/`, `tests/`, `wikis/`.\\n\\nProposed additions / extensions (subject to existing wiki conventions; defer final layout to whoever owns llm-wiki structure decisions):\\n\\n- `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` (new, if not present) with:\\n  - `concepts/` \\u2014 fundamentals: porosity, permeability, saturation, capillary pressure, relative permeability, etc.\\n  - `methodology/` \\u2014 geosteering workflow, reservoir characterization, log interpretation, formation evaluation.\\n  - `standards/` \\u2014 DNV / API / ISO references with [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)-shape frontmatter (`code_id`, `publisher`, `revision`).\\n  - `sources/` \\u2014 citation index, NOT ingestion targets per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482).\\n- `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` \\u2014 log of every source examined, decision (ingest / skip / defer), license note.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. **Local sweep.** Inventory `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` and other candidate dirs. Output: a manifest of `(filepath, size, page-count, title-from-metadata, classification)` rows. ~1 hr scripted.\\n2. **Online sweep.** 6\\u201310 best-of-class courses, textbooks (open-access only), and survey papers. Bookmark + brief description. ~1\\u20132 hr.\\n3. **License triage.** Drop everything that's not clearly redistributable. Prefer creative-commons or public-domain (older works > 70 yrs).\\n4. **Wiki page drafts.** Write 5\\u201315 concept pages (`wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/*.md`) in llm-wiki's existing style. Cite sources, never copy. Apply the calc-citation contract (`workspace-hub/.claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md`) where formulas appear.\\n5. **PR with the corpus + wiki pages + citation log.** Reviewer checks license, citation, and that copy is original (not paraphrased > 30-word chunks).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `/mnt/ace` reservoir-engineering inventory at `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` lists at least 50 candidate sources with classification (ingest / skip / defer) and license note.\\n- [ ] At least 5 concept pages drafted under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/` covering core fundamentals (porosity, permeability, gamma-ray log interpretation, dip / azimuth, formation tops).\\n- [ ] At least 2 methodology pages under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/methodology/` covering geosteering workflow + log correlation.\\n- [ ] All cited sources licensed for redistribution OR cited only as reference (no in-page copying).\\n- [ ] PR opened, reviewed, merged with the standard llm-wiki review process.\\n- [ ] Cross-link added to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) when the wiki pages are ready, so Kaggle modeling work can reference them.\\n\\n## Risks and open questions\\n\\n- **Risk:** `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` may contain user-purchased textbooks not licensed for redistribution. Triage carefully \\u2014 local-use-only OK, ingestion-to-public-repo NOT OK.\\n- **Open:** Should reservoir-engineering wiki pages live under a top-level `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` or inside the existing marine/offshore family? Defer to llm-wiki maintainer decision.\\n- **Open:** What citation style \\u2014 IEEE-numeric, APA, or the inline `code_id` style from [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)? Likely match the existing llm-wiki convention.\\n\\n## Time budget\\n\\nA few sessions across 1\\u20132 weeks. Don't disappear into a literature rabbit hole; the 50-source target keeps it bounded.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40\", \"display_title\": \"Research: reservoir engineering literature \\u2014 local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/392\", \"title\": \"feat(data): public well-log datasets for wellbore geology \\u2014 Kaggle ROGII companion ingest\", \"issue_number\": 392, \"body\": \"## Goal\\n\\nIngest the public well-log / wellbore-geology datasets needed to support the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/rogii-wellbore-geology-prediction) competition (deadline 2026-08-05) into worldenergydata's data-collection layer, under a redistribution-clean license posture.\\n\\nThis is the **data-side counterpart** to:\\n- [vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40) \\u2014 reservoir-engineering literature ingest into llm-wiki.\\n- [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) \\u2014 research catalog of public datasets and prior art (kept on the Kaggle side as docs).\\n\\nUser direction 2026-05-06: research + data work is the **gating phase** for the competition's modeling tracks. Planning + thorough execution of this issue (and its companions) precedes any modeling-tail planning ([Phase 3 GBDT](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/4), [Phase 4 sequence](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/7), [Phase 5 ensemble](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/8)).\\n\\n## Scope (well-log + wellbore-geology only)\\n\\n**In-scope datasets (audit candidates):**\\n\\n- **Force 2020 Well-Log Lithology** (Xeek): well logs incl. GR + lithology labels at well-row level. Best-known open analog to the ROGII task.\\n- **Geolink Open North Sea**: ~150 wells with GR and other curves; license needs verification.\\n- **Equinor Volve**: full Norwegian field dataset, well logs incl. GR.\\n- **NLOG (TNO Dutch Subsurface Database)**: well logs, formation tops; established open data.\\n- **USGS Petroleum Atlas / National Geologic Map**: formation-tops references (likely complement existing worldenergydata BSEE work).\\n- **OSDU** open subsets \\u2014 if available under acceptable license.\\n- **BSEE well log subset** \\u2014 already partially in scope under [#365](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/365); this issue's intersection is \\\"the well-log slice with GR / formation labels usable for ML training.\\\"\\n\\n**Out of scope (separate concerns):**\\n\\n- Reservoir-engineering textbooks / coursework / methodology PDFs \\u2192 those go to [llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40).\\n- Cost / economics datasets \\u2192 existing worldenergydata cost track.\\n- Subsea-pipeline material \\u2192 defer to a future \\\\`subsea-engineering\\\\` track.\\n\\n## Deliverable shape\\n\\nFollowing worldenergydata conventions (module-per-domain, schema + data-collection + tests):\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\nsrc/worldenergydata/well_logs/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 schema.py                    # WellLogRecord with GR, lithology, formation, X/Y/Z/MD\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 data_collection/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 force2020_dataset.py     # one module per ingested dataset\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 geolink_dataset.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 volve_dataset.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 nlog_dataset.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 public_dataset.py        # unified loader\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\nPer-dataset module pattern matches existing \\\\`src/worldenergydata/cost/data_collection/public_dataset.py\\\\` style: curated + license-cited + provenance-clean.\\n\\n## License posture (load-bearing)\\n\\n- Cite-only datasets (commercial / paywalled) MUST NOT be ingested as data; they may be referenced in docstrings.\\n- Redistributable datasets (CC-BY, CC0, public-domain, explicit-permission) are eligible for inclusion in the ingest pipeline.\\n- Each dataset module records its license in the docstring header per existing worldenergydata convention.\\n- Adopt [#361](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/361) calc-citation-contract for any standards-derived numerical claim.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria (high-level \\u2014 full plan to follow)\\n\\n- [ ] Per-dataset license audit completed; documented in \\\\`docs/research/well-logs-datasets.md\\\\`.\\n- [ ] At least 2 datasets cleared for redistribution and ingested as worldenergydata modules with full test coverage.\\n- [ ] Public Python query API parity with cost / HSE pattern.\\n- [ ] Cross-link to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) and [vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40).\\n- [ ] Plan posted via worldenergydata's standard \\\\`docs/plans/\\\\` workflow with adversarial review.\\n\\n## Plan tier (proposed)\\n\\n**T3** \\u2014 multiple dataset audits, license-compliance is load-bearing, cross-cutting with [#365](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/365) / [#366](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/366) / [#361](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/361). Plan to follow in a separate session per worldenergydata's normal workflow.\\n\\n## Time budget\\n\\nEstimated 2\\u20134 sessions for the plan + adversarial review. Implementation (per-dataset waves) runs as a multi-week background thread parallel to the Kaggle modeling work, per the [PLANNING-ROADMAP](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/blob/main/docs/plans/PLANNING-ROADMAP.md) revised sequencing.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/392\", \"display_title\": \"feat(data): public well-log datasets for wellbore geology \\u2014 Kaggle ROGII companion ingest\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries","issue_number":2510,"body":"## Context\nParent: #2507\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\n\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\n\n## Proposed scope\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\n\n## Deliverables\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\n3. Metadata extraction report.\n4. Tests and documentation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","display_title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction","issue_number":2626,"body":"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\n\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\n\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\n\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\n\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\nScenario 3 suggests \"temporary lift of interaction limit\" — globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\n\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\n\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\n\n## Severity\n\nMedium — the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","display_title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632","title":"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)","issue_number":2632,"body":"## Summary\n\nThree llm-wiki issues at `status:plan-approved` (#2368, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125) have been stuck since 2026-04-28 due to a missing/stale approval-binding state. Codex's 10-thread parallel-implementation lanes correctly refused to execute, and the gate has held for 5+ days without remediation. This META issue captures the rot so it can be cleaned up in one pass.\n\n## Why\n\nPer the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 contract (memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`), `status:plan-approved` GitHub label is necessary but not sufficient — execution requires a revision-bound approval marker at `.planning/plan-approved/<n>.md` that names the approved plan SHA + review artifact paths. Otherwise agents can't confirm WHICH version of the plan was approved.\n\nThis was specifically designed as a load-bearing user-in-loop gate (memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md`) — agents must NOT self-approve by creating the marker themselves.\n\nThe gate is doing its job. But the cleanup hasn't happened, and three valuable llm-wiki improvements have been frozen.\n\n## Per-issue state (verified 2026-05-03)\n\n### vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2368.md`: **MISSING**\n- Local plan `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md`: blob `b391641688` — header says `Status: draft` (REGRESSED from v2)\n- Approved revision per Codex's 2026-04-28 comment: SHA `1c01062d8` — header in that SHA says `Status: draft (v2 — addresses r1 findings)`, blob `b1df634b3`\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:17:06Z (3 retry passes, all gated)\n- Likely cause of plan regression: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` pattern during auto-sync\n\n**Remediation:**\n```bash\ngit checkout 1c01062d8 -- docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md\n# Then create .planning/plan-approved/2368.md with marker:\n#   plan_sha: 1c01062d8\n#   plan_blob: b1df634b3943db8f99888cb120ccf9be6ce245fe\n#   review_artifacts:\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-claude.md\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-codex.md\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-gemini.md\n#   approved_by: vamseeachanta\n#   approved_at: <ISO timestamp of human approval>\ngit add docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md .planning/plan-approved/2368.md\ngit commit -m \"markers(plan-approved): bind vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 to v2 SHA 1c01062d8\"\n```\n\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 extend ingestion to Orcina resources/examples/training\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2124.md`: **MISSING**\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2124*` exists)\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:18:13Z — also flags upstream dependency on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 still being open\n- Note: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 status as of 2026-05-03 (verify before remediating)\n\n**Remediation:** plan needs to be authored or located before binding. May be that the plan was lost to the same merge-race that ate vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22's v2 content.\n\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 auto-refresh ingestion on Orcina releases\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2125.md`: **MISSING**\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2125*` exists)\n- Codex 2026-04-28T06:15:27Z comment indicates an implementation pass DID complete: branch `codex/10thread-20260428-issue-2125`, commit `e4b6193236a70ed2ec960deb92b3f65b9f876616`. But no merge to main and label still says `status:working`.\n\n**Remediation:** check if commit `e4b6193236` is salvageable; either land it or rebind plan + re-execute.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis META issue is for **diagnosis + decision-making**, not implementation:\n\n- Confirm the 3 issues' approval-binding state matches what's recorded above (re-verify before acting)\n- For each: decide rebind / re-plan / archive / continue-as-is\n- File ONE remediation issue per surviving plan\n- Update the relevant memory files if the rebinding workflow needs refinement\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Each of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 reaches one of: (a) properly bound + ready for execution, (b) deferred with explicit ADR, (c) closed as superseded\n- The meta cleanup commit pattern is documented as a precedent for future \"approval-binding rot\" sweeps\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Implementation of the 3 issues' actual deliverables (separate downstream work after rebinding)\n- Codex 10-thread lane reactivation (that's a separate workflow concern)\n\n## References\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 (closed) — original approval-binding contract; memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`\n- Memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md` — why agents can't self-approve\n- Memory: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` — likely cause of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 plan regression\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 — llm-wiki strengthening epic (parent for vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22/#2124/#2125)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2615 (closed 2026-05-03) — recent successful approval-binding precedent (Tier C closure)\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632","display_title":"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage","issue_number":2643,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\n\n## Context\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\n\nLive prerequisite checks found:\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\n\n## Problem\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\n\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\n\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\n\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\n\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model","issue_number":2528,"body":"## Context\n\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\"12 skills → 4-5\") is partially complete — `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\n\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\n\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\n\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\n\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed — no broken references to deleted skills\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable — referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\"*.md\"` `--include=\"*.py\"` `--include=\"*.yaml\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\n\n## Complexity\n\nT1 (trivial) — pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\n\n## References\n\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","display_title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown","issue_number":2551,"body":"## Summary\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\n\n## Why\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\n\n## Scope\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\n\n## Related\n- Root hardening: #2546\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","display_title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/387","title":"WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration","issue_number":387,"body":"## WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** wind\n\n**Repo:** ['worldenergydata'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nEvaluate **pyWAsP** (https://docs.wasp.dk/pywasp/latest/) — the Python API for the\nWAsP wind resource assessment flow model (DTU Wind Energy / Ørsted) — for integration\ninto the worldenergydata ecosystem. pyWAsP covers terrain effects (IBZ model),\nwind climate generalisation/downscaling, and AEP estimation with wake effects\n(via PyWake). Built on WindKit, which uses xarray data structures natively.\n\n### Why\n\nWind energy is a core domain for the Tier 3 GTM targets (Orsted, Equinor, Dominion\nCVOW — WRK-148). pyWAsP is the industry-standard tool these companies use daily.\nAdding wind resource assessment capability to worldenergydata:\n- Enables AEP → field-development economics pipeline (feeds WRK-476 ESG/carbon module)\n- Creates direct technical credibility with offshore wind prospects\n- xarray/WindKit structures align with the planned metocean module (NOAA NDBC)\n- Pairs with existing Arps decline curve (WRK-318) for hybrid fossil/renewables models\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] `pip install pywasp` tested on dev-primary (licence requirement assessed)\n- [ ] PyWake (open-source companion wake model) installed and smoke-tested separately\n- [ ] WindKit data structures understood — xarray compatibility with worldenergydata\n- [ ] At least one worked example: wind climate generalisation OR AEP calculation\n- [ ] Evaluation report written to `specs/data-sources/pywasp-eval.md` covering:\n- [ ] Decision: integrate (create implementation WRK) | defer | skip\n- [ ] `specs/data-sources/worldenergydata.yaml` tool entry updated with eval outcome\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/387","display_title":"WRK-688: eval(worldenergydata): evaluate pyWAsP for wind resource assessment integration"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh","issue_number":2653,"body":"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\n\n### Why\n\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\npipeline cleanly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] New session → new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) → same log file continues\n- [ ] Session idle >2h → next tool call starts a new log file\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** — done\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **19. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **20. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","display_title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41","title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions","issue_number":41,"body":"## Summary\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the maritime-law wiki.\n\n## Decision source\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for IMO/ILO convention and code pages.\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\n\n## Scope\n- Plan and then implement a bounded metadata-only migration or mirror strategy for eligible maritime-law convention/code pages currently under `wikis/maritime-law/wiki/concepts/`.\n- Candidate pages include SOLAS, MARPOL, MLC, and ISM Code, subject to duplicate/path review.\n- Preserve `consolidated_edition` where that is the correct public metadata field.\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No convention/code text copying.\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, or source excerpts.\n- No broad maritime-law schema rewrite beyond the routing implementation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Eligible pages have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\n- Existing concept links are preserved or redirected/mirrored safely.\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\n\n## Related\n- #15\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42","title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing","issue_number":42,"body":"## Summary\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the LNG-projects wiki.\n\n## Decision source\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for LNG codes and standards pages.\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\n\n## Scope\n- Plan and then implement bounded metadata-only standards pages for LNG codes when public metadata is sufficient.\n- Candidate families include CSA-Z276, NFPA 59A, and IGC Code, subject to public metadata verification and duplicate/path review.\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No standard text copying.\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, project specifications, or source excerpts.\n- No broad LNG content expansion beyond standards-routing implementation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Eligible LNG standards have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\n- Any insufficient public metadata is split into follow-up work instead of guessed.\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\n\n## Related\n- #15\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist","issue_number":43,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any SESA LNG corpus extraction can proceed from #14.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #14\n- Raw/source family: SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa`\n- Current status: extraction remains blocked until clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist that defines what must exist before extraction starts:\n- row-level or artifact-level clearance fields required for any proposed first tranche\n- allowed source evidence types and disallowed source evidence types\n- public-repo output boundaries for summaries, metadata, and target wiki pages\n- required approvals for vendor, client/project-sensitive, archive, workbook, and standards-derived materials\n- validation expectations before any future extraction commit\n- required separate implementation issue structure after clearance is complete\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa` content into git.\n- No OCR, text extraction, table extraction, workbook extraction, or PDF summarization.\n- No vendor standards text, private archive material, credentials, client-sensitive content, or project specifications in this public repo.\n- No closing #14 until this checklist and a later bounded implementation lane are complete.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored public synthesis, vendor-derived text, client/project-sensitive files, archives, and standards material.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #14 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #14","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":45,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any HSE/safety dataset metadata or wiki promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until dataset clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for HSE/safety dataset material:\n- dataset-level clearance fields required before promotion\n- allowed public metadata fields, dataset citations, and aggregate descriptions\n- disallowed personally identifiable information, incident-sensitive records, raw CSV/TXT rows, and proprietary/private derived data\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules for HSE concepts and source metadata\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/PII/secret scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw dataset extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` content into git.\n- No CSV/TXT row promotion, ZIP extraction, incident-record summarization, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No PII, private source text, credentials, or raw safety data in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate dataset/artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, aggregate public synthesis, raw rows, PII/sensitive incident records, archives, and derived summaries.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/PII boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":44,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any BSEE/offshore source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for BSEE/offshore candidate material:\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\n- handling rules for client/project-sensitive files, permit/activity samples, spreadsheets, document archives, and data descriptions\n- allowed public metadata fields versus disallowed extracted content\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/client-sensitive boundary scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` content into git.\n- No OCR, table extraction, workbook extraction, PDF/DOCX summarization, ZIP inspection for promotion, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No client/project-sensitive files, credentials, permit details, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, client/project-sensitive data, proprietary/project material, archives, and authored synthesis.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/client-sensitive boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":46,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations material:\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\n- handling rules for magazine/offshore-operation articles, heavy-lift/pipelay source material, images, PDFs, and archives\n- allowed public bibliographic metadata and authored high-level synthesis\n- disallowed copied article text, figures, vendor/private material, and raw archive contents\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` content into git.\n- No OCR, article summarization from raw files, figure extraction, archive extraction, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No copyrighted article text, images, credentials, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored synthesis, copyrighted article text, images/figures, archives, and vendor/private material.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47","title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs","issue_number":47,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #25 Batch Pack 1 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #25\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #25: plan branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` at approved SHA `7cc1c0b1a`.\n- Current blocker: the public spinout repo does not contain the approval-bound plan artifact or the required online-resource registry inputs.\n\n## Scope\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 1 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 1\n- `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` or an approved public-safe extracted subset sufficient for Batch Pack 1\n- any overlay/processed input required by the approved plan\n- provenance notes binding the restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\n- validation checklist for duplicate checks, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw boundaries\n\n## Out of scope\n- No Batch Pack 1 promotion execution in this prep issue.\n- No registry reconstruction from memory.\n- No source re-download or raw source parsing.\n- No API/portal wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\n- No credentials, API keys, private endpoints, private source text, or vendor text in the public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 1 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\n- [ ] The required registry input or approved subset is available in a public-safe form.\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\n- [ ] Future #25 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\n- [ ] #25 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\n\n## Related\n- #25\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48","title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs","issue_number":48,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #26 Batch Pack 4 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #26\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #26: plan branch `plan/issue-2373-batch-pack-4` at approved SHA `c516ec853`.\n- Upstream gate `vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471` is now closed, but the public spinout repo still lacks the approval-bound plan artifact and required data inputs.\n\n## Scope\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 4 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 4\n- transfer ledger input required for the cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural standards slice\n- topic-cluster and alias inputs required by the approved plan\n- any approved summary-backed evidence surface required to avoid raw PDF rereads\n- provenance notes binding restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\n- validation checklist for duplicate/extend-vs-create mapping, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw/vendor boundaries\n\n## Out of scope\n- No Batch Pack 4 promotion execution in this prep issue.\n- No ledger/cluster reconstruction from memory.\n- No raw PDF rereads, source extraction, OCR, or standards text summarization.\n- No standards wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\n- No credentials, private source text, vendor standards text, formulas, tables, or copied clauses in the public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 4 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\n- [ ] Required transfer ledger, topic-cluster, and alias inputs are available in a public-safe form.\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\n- [ ] Future #26 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\n- [ ] #26 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\n\n## Related\n- #26\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40","title":"Research: reservoir engineering literature — local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki","issue_number":40,"body":"## Goal\n\nBuild out the reservoir-engineering substrate of llm-wiki by mining (a) the user's existing local PDF corpus on ace-linux-1 (`/mnt/ace`, 30,499 PDFs) and (b) public online sources, then ingesting the relevant material under llm-wiki's MIT + CC-BY-4.0 license. Drives both the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026) competition (deeper domain literacy → better modeling decisions) and longer-term wikis around oil & gas / subsurface engineering.\n\nCompanion issue: [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) covers competition-specific *prior art* (datasets + ML papers); this issue covers the broader *educational foundation* (textbooks, coursework, classic papers).\n\n## Scope\n\n**In-scope source types**\n\n- Textbooks on reservoir engineering, petroleum engineering, formation evaluation, well logging, drilling, geosteering.\n- University coursework — open syllabi, lecture notes, problem sets from Stanford SDSS, Texas A&M, U Texas Austin, Heriot-Watt, IFP, Imperial.\n- Conference papers — SPE, AAPG, SEG, EAGE — with care about open-access vs paywalled.\n- Industry standards / methodology PDFs (DNV, API, ISO).\n- Theses and dissertations from public university repositories.\n- ArXiv preprints in petroleum engineering, geophysics, ML-for-geosteering categories.\n\n**Out of scope (license / IP risk)**\n\n- Pirated or unauthorized copies of paywalled textbooks, even if found locally.\n- Vendor-derivative material under proprietary license.\n- The deny-list per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482) governance: nothing under `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/sources/` should be cited; cite the canonical standard or concept page instead.\n\n## Sources to mine\n\n### Local — `/mnt/ace` (ace-linux-1)\n\n- `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` — top candidate directory by name. First pass: recursively list, classify by filename / metadata, flag candidates.\n- `/mnt/ace/aceengineer-admin/Reference/` — mixed (mostly tax / admin docs in spot-check, but may contain technical references).\n- Other dirs revealed during initial sweep.\n- Total PDFs in `/mnt/ace`: ~30,499. Realistic target: 50–200 ingest-worthy after deduplication and license filtering.\n\n### Online (representative starting points)\n\n- **Stanford Stanford Doerr School OCW**: open courses on petroleum / energy resources.\n- **Texas A&M PETE OCW** and **U Texas Austin Petroleum Engineering** open content.\n- **Heriot-Watt PE** open materials.\n- **arXiv physics.geo-ph** and **stat.ML** intersection — search \"well log\", \"geosteering\", \"lithology classification\".\n- **OnePetro** free-access entries (SPE / AAPG / SEG; many old papers are now open).\n- **AAPG Datapages** open-access portion.\n- **USGS Open-File Reports** in petroleum geology.\n- **OAPEN** and **Springer Open** for free textbooks.\n- **MIT OpenCourseWare** earth-and-planetary courses with subsurface relevance.\n\n## Output: llm-wiki structure\n\nExisting top-level dirs (verified 2026-05-06): `docs/`, `scripts/`, `seeds/`, `tests/`, `wikis/`.\n\nProposed additions / extensions (subject to existing wiki conventions; defer final layout to whoever owns llm-wiki structure decisions):\n\n- `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` (new, if not present) with:\n  - `concepts/` — fundamentals: porosity, permeability, saturation, capillary pressure, relative permeability, etc.\n  - `methodology/` — geosteering workflow, reservoir characterization, log interpretation, formation evaluation.\n  - `standards/` — DNV / API / ISO references with [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)-shape frontmatter (`code_id`, `publisher`, `revision`).\n  - `sources/` — citation index, NOT ingestion targets per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482).\n- `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` — log of every source examined, decision (ingest / skip / defer), license note.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Local sweep.** Inventory `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` and other candidate dirs. Output: a manifest of `(filepath, size, page-count, title-from-metadata, classification)` rows. ~1 hr scripted.\n2. **Online sweep.** 6–10 best-of-class courses, textbooks (open-access only), and survey papers. Bookmark + brief description. ~1–2 hr.\n3. **License triage.** Drop everything that's not clearly redistributable. Prefer creative-commons or public-domain (older works > 70 yrs).\n4. **Wiki page drafts.** Write 5–15 concept pages (`wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/*.md`) in llm-wiki's existing style. Cite sources, never copy. Apply the calc-citation contract (`workspace-hub/.claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md`) where formulas appear.\n5. **PR with the corpus + wiki pages + citation log.** Reviewer checks license, citation, and that copy is original (not paraphrased > 30-word chunks).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `/mnt/ace` reservoir-engineering inventory at `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` lists at least 50 candidate sources with classification (ingest / skip / defer) and license note.\n- [ ] At least 5 concept pages drafted under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/` covering core fundamentals (porosity, permeability, gamma-ray log interpretation, dip / azimuth, formation tops).\n- [ ] At least 2 methodology pages under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/methodology/` covering geosteering workflow + log correlation.\n- [ ] All cited sources licensed for redistribution OR cited only as reference (no in-page copying).\n- [ ] PR opened, reviewed, merged with the standard llm-wiki review process.\n- [ ] Cross-link added to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) when the wiki pages are ready, so Kaggle modeling work can reference them.\n\n## Risks and open questions\n\n- **Risk:** `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` may contain user-purchased textbooks not licensed for redistribution. Triage carefully — local-use-only OK, ingestion-to-public-repo NOT OK.\n- **Open:** Should reservoir-engineering wiki pages live under a top-level `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` or inside the existing marine/offshore family? Defer to llm-wiki maintainer decision.\n- **Open:** What citation style — IEEE-numeric, APA, or the inline `code_id` style from [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)? Likely match the existing llm-wiki convention.\n\n## Time budget\n\nA few sessions across 1–2 weeks. Don't disappear into a literature rabbit hole; the 50-source target keeps it bounded.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40","display_title":"Research: reservoir engineering literature — local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/392","title":"feat(data): public well-log datasets for wellbore geology — Kaggle ROGII companion ingest","issue_number":392,"body":"## Goal\n\nIngest the public well-log / wellbore-geology datasets needed to support the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/rogii-wellbore-geology-prediction) competition (deadline 2026-08-05) into worldenergydata's data-collection layer, under a redistribution-clean license posture.\n\nThis is the **data-side counterpart** to:\n- [vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40) — reservoir-engineering literature ingest into llm-wiki.\n- [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) — research catalog of public datasets and prior art (kept on the Kaggle side as docs).\n\nUser direction 2026-05-06: research + data work is the **gating phase** for the competition's modeling tracks. Planning + thorough execution of this issue (and its companions) precedes any modeling-tail planning ([Phase 3 GBDT](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/4), [Phase 4 sequence](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/7), [Phase 5 ensemble](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/8)).\n\n## Scope (well-log + wellbore-geology only)\n\n**In-scope datasets (audit candidates):**\n\n- **Force 2020 Well-Log Lithology** (Xeek): well logs incl. GR + lithology labels at well-row level. Best-known open analog to the ROGII task.\n- **Geolink Open North Sea**: ~150 wells with GR and other curves; license needs verification.\n- **Equinor Volve**: full Norwegian field dataset, well logs incl. GR.\n- **NLOG (TNO Dutch Subsurface Database)**: well logs, formation tops; established open data.\n- **USGS Petroleum Atlas / National Geologic Map**: formation-tops references (likely complement existing worldenergydata BSEE work).\n- **OSDU** open subsets — if available under acceptable license.\n- **BSEE well log subset** — already partially in scope under [#365](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/365); this issue's intersection is \"the well-log slice with GR / formation labels usable for ML training.\"\n\n**Out of scope (separate concerns):**\n\n- Reservoir-engineering textbooks / coursework / methodology PDFs → those go to [llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40).\n- Cost / economics datasets → existing worldenergydata cost track.\n- Subsea-pipeline material → defer to a future \\`subsea-engineering\\` track.\n\n## Deliverable shape\n\nFollowing worldenergydata conventions (module-per-domain, schema + data-collection + tests):\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nsrc/worldenergydata/well_logs/\n├── __init__.py\n├── schema.py                    # WellLogRecord with GR, lithology, formation, X/Y/Z/MD\n├── data_collection/\n│   ├── force2020_dataset.py     # one module per ingested dataset\n│   ├── geolink_dataset.py\n│   ├── volve_dataset.py\n│   ├── nlog_dataset.py\n│   └── public_dataset.py        # unified loader\n└── tests/\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nPer-dataset module pattern matches existing \\`src/worldenergydata/cost/data_collection/public_dataset.py\\` style: curated + license-cited + provenance-clean.\n\n## License posture (load-bearing)\n\n- Cite-only datasets (commercial / paywalled) MUST NOT be ingested as data; they may be referenced in docstrings.\n- Redistributable datasets (CC-BY, CC0, public-domain, explicit-permission) are eligible for inclusion in the ingest pipeline.\n- Each dataset module records its license in the docstring header per existing worldenergydata convention.\n- Adopt [#361](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/361) calc-citation-contract for any standards-derived numerical claim.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (high-level — full plan to follow)\n\n- [ ] Per-dataset license audit completed; documented in \\`docs/research/well-logs-datasets.md\\`.\n- [ ] At least 2 datasets cleared for redistribution and ingested as worldenergydata modules with full test coverage.\n- [ ] Public Python query API parity with cost / HSE pattern.\n- [ ] Cross-link to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) and [vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#40](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40).\n- [ ] Plan posted via worldenergydata's standard \\`docs/plans/\\` workflow with adversarial review.\n\n## Plan tier (proposed)\n\n**T3** — multiple dataset audits, license-compliance is load-bearing, cross-cutting with [#365](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/365) / [#366](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/366) / [#361](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/361). Plan to follow in a separate session per worldenergydata's normal workflow.\n\n## Time budget\n\nEstimated 2–4 sessions for the plan + adversarial review. Implementation (per-dataset waves) runs as a multi-week background thread parallel to the Kaggle modeling work, per the [PLANNING-ROADMAP](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/blob/main/docs/plans/PLANNING-ROADMAP.md) revised sequencing.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/392","display_title":"feat(data): public well-log datasets for wellbore geology — Kaggle ROGII companion ingest"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
