{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":["vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","vamseeachanta/digitalmodel","vamseeachanta/assetutilities","vamseeachanta/worldenergydata","vamseeachanta/llm-wiki","vamseeachanta/assethold","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-website","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-strategy"],"query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-approved\"","topn":50,"sort":"updated","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\", \"issue_number\": 2269, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\\n\\nPart of #1782.\\nPrimary reference: #25.\\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\\n\\nExpected deliverables:\\n- baseline docs\\n- run/validation entrypoints\\n- minimal smoke example\\n- troubleshooting guidance\\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\\n\\n## Notes\\nImplementation should prefer:\\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"display_title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\", \"issue_number\": 2402, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR\\u00d72 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model \\u00a77 \\u2014 **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model \\u00a73).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per \\u00a73 \\u2014 enforced and tested\\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s \\u2014 measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) \\u2014 live in their own issues.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"display_title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962\", \"title\": \"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring \\u2014 audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode\", \"issue_number\": 1962, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nSystematic refactoring of the workspace-hub repo ecosystem, starting with tier-1 repositories. The goal is to reduce architectural debt, consolidate duplicate patterns, enforce consistent structure, and improve agent navigability across all tier-1 repos.\\n\\n## Tier-1 Repos (Priority Order)\\n\\n| # | Repo | Purpose | Maturity | Depends On |\\n|---|------|---------|----------|------------|\\n| 1 | `digitalmodel/` | Engineering digital twin (asset integrity, CP, GIS, hydro) | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 2 | `assetutilities/` | Shared engineering utilities (config, units, calculations) | stable | \\u2014 |\\n| 3 | `assethold/` | Asset portfolio financial analysis | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 4 | `worldenergydata/` | Global energy market data (BSEE, EIA, drilling) | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 5 | `CAD-DEVELOPMENTS/` | CAD solvers, models, database, utilities | beta | \\u2014 |\\n| 6 | `aceengineer-website/` | Consulting website | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n| 7 | `aceengineer-strategy/` | GTM, business strategy | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n| 8 | `sabithaandkrishnaestates/` | SKEstates Inc. business ops | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n\\n## Refactoring Scope\\n\\n### Phase 1: Audit (analysis-only, no code changes)\\n- [ ] Run `repo-architecture-analysis` on each tier-1 repo\\n- [ ] Identify cross-repo duplicate code (especially assetutilities consumers)\\n- [ ] Map dependency graph (imports, shared configs, data flows)\\n- [ ] Catalog test coverage per repo (current state)\\n- [ ] Identify orphaned/dead code, unused modules, oversized files (>400 lines)\\n- [ ] Score each repo against the Control-Plane Contract (AGENTS.md, provider adapters)\\n- [ ] Identify skill duplicates across repos (134 known from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 audit)\\n\\n### Phase 2: Plan (per-repo refactor plans)\\n- [ ] Generate refactor plan per tier-1 repo with estimated effort\\n- [ ] Prioritize by: business value \\u00d7 technical debt severity \\u00d7 dependency impact\\n- [ ] Identify breaking changes and migration paths\\n- [ ] Define test coverage targets (tier-1 = 85% per pytest.tier1.ini)\\n\\n### Phase 3: Execute (TDD, incremental, per-repo)\\n- [ ] Execute refactors repo-by-repo following dependency order (assetutilities first)\\n- [ ] TDD mandatory \\u2014 tests before implementation\\n- [ ] Each repo refactor as a separate sub-issue for tracking\\n\\n## Execution Strategy: Claude Code Plan Mode (Cloud)\\n\\n### Claude Code `--permission-mode plan` (\\\"Ultraplan\\\")\\n\\nClaude Code v2.1.92 supports `--permission-mode plan` which restricts the agent to **read-only analysis and planning** \\u2014 no file writes, no shell mutations. This is ideal for Phase 1 (Audit) and Phase 2 (Plan).\\n\\n**Proposed execution:**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Phase 1: Audit each tier-1 repo in plan mode (safe, read-only)\\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\\\\n  --print \\\\\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\\\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\\\\n  -p \\\"Audit the repository architecture of digitalmodel/. Analyze: module structure, dependency graph, test coverage, dead code, file sizes >400 lines, AGENTS.md compliance. Output a structured JSON report.\\\"\\n\\n# Phase 2: Generate refactor plan\\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\\\\n  --print \\\\\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\\\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\\\\n  -p \\\"Given the audit report, generate a prioritized refactor plan for digitalmodel/. Include: breaking changes, migration steps, test targets, estimated effort per module.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### Cloud Execution Considerations\\n\\n| Aspect | Status | Notes |\\n|--------|--------|-------|\\n| **Claude Code CLI** | Installed (v2.1.92) | Available on ace-linux-1 |\\n| **Plan mode** | Supported | `--permission-mode plan` \\u2014 read-only, safe for audit |\\n| **API-key mode** | Supported | `--bare` + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for headless/cloud runs |\\n| **Print mode** | Supported | `-p` / `--print` for non-interactive batch execution |\\n| **Budget cap** | Supported | `--max-budget-usd` to control spend per run |\\n| **Cloud sandbox** | Possible | Can run via Hermes `delegate_task` with `acp_command='claude'` |\\n| **Max subscription** | Claude Max $200/mo | Rate-limited but sufficient for plan-mode audit |\\n\\n### Recommended Approach\\n1. **Phase 1 + 2 (Audit + Plan)**: Run Claude Code in plan mode via `delegate_task(acp_command='claude')` \\u2014 subagents get isolated context, read-only, budget-capped\\n2. **Phase 3 (Execute)**: Requires interactive Claude Code sessions with full permissions \\u2014 NOT suited for autonomous cloud execution without user oversight\\n\\n## Adversarial Review Requirements\\n\\nPer [AI Review Routing Policy](docs/standards/AI_REVIEW_ROUTING_POLICY.md):\\n\\n- **3-agent adversarial review at BOTH stages** (plan + code/artifact)\\n- Claude: orchestrator + reviewer\\n- Codex: implementation worker + adversarial reviewer\\n- Gemini: architecture reviewer + adversarial reviewer\\n- Max 3 review iterations per deliverable\\n- All MAJOR findings must be resolved before completion\\n\\n### Review Checkpoints\\n1. **After Phase 1 (Audit)**: All 3 agents review the audit findings\\n2. **After Phase 2 (Plan)**: All 3 agents review each repo's refactor plan\\n3. **After Phase 3 (Execute)**: All 3 agents review code changes per repo\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1567 \\u2014 Feature: Continuous Repo Architecture Intelligence\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1545 \\u2014 Agentic feature progression for repo ecosystem productivity under GSD\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1603 \\u2014 Multi-repo architecture scan \\u2014 expand scanner to all tier-1 repos\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 \\u2014 Cross-agent session corpus audit (134 duplicate skills identified)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1734 \\u2014 chore: add domain skills to assethold (tier-1 with 0 skills)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1661 \\u2014 Architecture scanner: dependency cycle detection and layering violations\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#113 \\u2014 ROADMAP: Repo ecosystem 3-6 month horizon\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Audit report generated for each tier-1 repo\\n- [ ] Refactor plan per repo reviewed and approved by all 3 agents\\n- [ ] Phase 3 sub-issues created with clear scope per repo\\n- [ ] Test coverage meets tier-1 target (85%) after refactoring\\n- [ ] Zero cross-repo duplicate skills remaining\\n- [ ] All repos score 100% on Control-Plane Contract compliance\\n- [ ] Dependency graph documented and validated\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962\", \"display_title\": \"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring \\u2014 audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/596\", \"title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize digitalmodel folder/file structure\", \"issue_number\": 596, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nRepo-specific planning issue for normalizing `digitalmodel` folder/file structure as the first repo in the tier-1 repo-by-repo refactor wave.\\n\\nThis child issue is anchored to:\\n- Parent umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1962\\n- Folder-structure contract epic: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2397\\n- Inventory evidence: `workspace-hub/docs/reports/2026-05-07-tier1-folder-structure-inventory.md`\\n\\n## Why digitalmodel first\\n\\n`digitalmodel` is the first repo in the approved tier-1 refactor priority order from workspace-hub#1962. Current live inventory shows it is:\\n\\n- on `main`\\n- `0` commits ahead / `0` behind upstream\\n- no tracked dirty files\\n- already has the canonical high-level paths: `.claude`, `.github`, `config`, `docs`, `scripts`, `src`, `tests`\\n\\nThat makes it a low-risk first candidate for a repo-specific structure plan before moving to dependency-critical or dirty repos.\\n\\n## Initial inventory signals\\n\\nObserved root/structure drift candidates from 2026-05-07 inventory:\\n\\n- generated/output candidates: `benchmark_output`, `build`, `cache`, `dist`, `logs`, `outputs`, `results`, `site`, `test_output_ss`\\n- developer/runtime state candidates: `.benchmarks`, `.hypothesis`, `.mypy_cache`, `.pytest_cache`, `.ruff_cache`, `.swarm`\\n- root generated files: `coverage.json`, `coverage.xml`, `coverage.wrk149.focused.xml`, `coverage.wrk149.priority.xml`\\n- domain/product dirs that require classification rather than blind moves: `benchmarks`, `memory`, `notebooks`, `projects`, `reports`, `specs`\\n\\nNo implementation is authorized by this issue alone.\\n\\n## Required workflow\\n\\nFollow workspace-hub issue-planning mode:\\n\\n1. Resource intelligence before plan drafting:\\n   - read `digitalmodel/AGENTS.md`\\n   - inspect `docs/README.md`, routing maps, `pyproject.toml`, `.gitignore`, CI workflows, and test layout\\n   - classify generated artifacts vs durable report fixtures vs domain assets\\n2. Draft a plan in the appropriate `docs/plans/` location with:\\n   - Artifact Map\\n   - path-level migration matrix\\n   - safe-rename vs breaking-path migration classification\\n   - TDD/verification list\\n   - explicit approval gate\\n3. Run adversarial plan review.\\n4. Move to `status:plan-review` only after review artifacts exist.\\n5. Wait for user approval (`status:plan-approved` + local approval marker) before implementation.\\n6. Execute with TDD/verification and transactional closeout.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria for the plan stage\\n\\n- [ ] Plan inventories digitalmodel top-level folders and root files with classifications.\\n- [ ] Plan separates generated artifacts, durable reports/fixtures, docs, scripts/tools, package source, tests, and domain assets.\\n- [ ] Plan identifies which moves are safe housekeeping and which are breaking path migrations.\\n- [ ] Plan includes tests/checks for import stability, docs links/stale paths, `.gitignore` boundaries, and representative repo smoke tests.\\n- [ ] Plan explicitly states what will **not** be moved in the first implementation pass.\\n- [ ] No implementation occurs before user approval.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/596\", \"display_title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize digitalmodel folder/file structure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\", \"issue_number\": 2657, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\\n\\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\\n\\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\\n\\nReads:\\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\\n- `github.github-issues`\\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\\n\\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\\n\\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\\n\\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\\n\\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"display_title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\", \"issue_number\": 2656, \"body\": \"## Objective\\n\\nPlan a conservative, repo-by-repo folder/file structure normalization for `workspace-hub` under the workspace-hub tier-1 ecosystem workflow.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nPlanning only until explicit user approval. The plan must inventory current structure, identify root clutter/generated-output risk, propose a bounded Phase 1 refactor contract, define TDD/verification gates, and preserve evidence needed for rollback.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n- Canonical plan artifact under `docs/plans/`.\\n- Review artifact under `scripts/review/results/`.\\n- Final issue comment linking the plan and review artifact.\\n\\n## Approval Gate\\n\\nNo file moves, package reorganization, deletion, or cleanup execution is authorized until this issue is explicitly approved after plan review.\\n\\nParent ecosystem anchors: `workspace-hub#1962`, `workspace-hub#2397`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"display_title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/278\", \"title\": \"Restore broken modules.* compatibility shims after bsee and marine_safety consolidation\", \"issue_number\": 278, \"body\": \"Summary\\nThe recent consolidation of `modules/bsee` and `modules/marine_safety` claims backward-compatible re-exports, but the current package surface is broken.\\n\\nEvidence\\n- Recent consolidation removed legacy files while leaving package `__init__.py` files importing deleted submodules\\n- Examples observed during review:\\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/bsee/analysis/type_curves/__init__.py` imports modules that no longer exist\\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/importers/__init__.py` imports deleted importer modules\\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/analysis/incidents/__init__.py` imports deleted analysis modules\\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/processors/__init__.py` imports deleted processor modules\\n- Focused regression reproduced with:\\n  - `PYTHONPATH='src:../assetutilities/src' uv run pytest tests/modules/bsee/analysis/test_type_curves.py -q`\\n  - collection fails because the old import surface is gone/broken\\n\\nWhy this is risky\\n- This is a real compatibility break, not just cleanup noise\\n- Legacy imports used by tests/scripts/examples now fail at import time\\n- The commit message promises backward compatibility that the code does not provide\\n\\nRecommended fix\\n- Restore shim modules for deleted paths or update all package re-exports and downstream imports atomically\\n- Add explicit compatibility tests for promised legacy import paths before removing old modules\\n\\nAcceptance criteria\\n- Legacy import paths used by current tests/scripts import successfully or are fully migrated\\n- Compatibility expectations are encoded in tests\\n- Package `__init__.py` files no longer import deleted modules\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/278\", \"display_title\": \"Restore broken modules.* compatibility shims after bsee and marine_safety consolidation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/559\", \"title\": \"fix(marine_ops): test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation \\u2014 strict-greater on equal floats (use >=)\", \"issue_number\": 559, \"body\": \"Sub-issue of [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609) cluster R6 (heterogeneous OCIMF/RAO/integration). Individual-test issue per user direction to maintain visibility (\\\"9 individual issues to help keep gap\\\").\\n\\n## Test nodeid\\n`tests/marine_ops/marine_engineering/integration/test_hydro_rao_integration.py::TestHydroRAOIntegration::test_full_matrix_interpolation`\\n\\n## Top error (verbatim from triage plan)\\n> `Added mass should be diagonally dominant at (3,1)`: `assert 624146.29 > 624146.29` (strict-greater on equal floats \\u2014 should be `>=`).\\n\\n## Implicated source\\n- Test: `tests/marine_ops/marine_engineering/integration/test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation` \\u2014 assertion uses `>` where it should use `>=` (or include a tolerance).\\n\\n## Hypothesis\\n**(b) test fix** \\u2014 strict-greater-than against arithmetically equal floats. Replace `>` with `>=` (or `pytest.approx`) for diagonal-dominance check. Low-risk single-line edit per triage plan recommendation (see `docs/plans/2026-05-03-2609-marine-ops-triage.md` open question 5).\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- This single test will pass at digitalmodel HEAD with no `--maxfail`-induced cascade.\\n- No regression in sibling `test_hydro_rao_integration.py` tests.\\n\\n## Reference\\n- Triage plan: `docs/plans/2026-05-03-2609-marine-ops-triage.md` (cluster R6, sub-defect 4)\\n- Parent: [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609)\\n- Sister sub-issues from Lanes b + c: see [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609) for siblings.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/559\", \"display_title\": \"fix(marine_ops): test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation \\u2014 strict-greater on equal floats (use >=)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\", \"issue_number\": 26, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\\n\\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\\n- Explicitly exclude:\\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\", \"issue_number\": 25, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\\n\\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \\\"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\\\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\\n\\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/72\", \"title\": \"Cleanup: resolve merge markers blocking editable install and downstream pytest\", \"issue_number\": 72, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`assetutilities` currently contains unresolved merge markers in:\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml`\\n- `src/assetutilities/common/update_deep.py`\\n\\nThis breaks downstream workflows, including:\\n\\n- `uv` metadata generation for editable dependency `assetutilities`\\n- `digitalmodel` commands such as `PYTHONPATH=src uv run python -m pytest tests/solvers/calculix/test_fem_chain.py`\\n- direct `pytest` startup in `digitalmodel`, because importing `assetutilities.common.update_deep` raises a `SyntaxError`\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\nDiscovered while validating `vamseeachanta/digitalmodel#460`.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Remove merge markers from `pyproject.toml`\\n- [ ] Remove merge markers from `src/assetutilities/common/update_deep.py`\\n- [ ] `uv` can resolve editable `assetutilities` successfully\\n- [ ] downstream `digitalmodel` targeted pytest startup succeeds past import / metadata initialization\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/72\", \"display_title\": \"Cleanup: resolve merge markers blocking editable install and downstream pytest\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\", \"issue_number\": 19, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\\n\\n## Context\\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\\n\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` \\u2014 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` \\u2014 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` \\u2014 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\\n\\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\\n\\n## Problem\\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\\n\\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\\n\\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\", \"issue_number\": 14, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\\n\\n## Source of record\\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\\n\\n## Why\\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\\n\\n## Scope\\nIn scope:\\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\\n- No source/staging cleanup.\\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/58\", \"title\": \"YAML Plotting\", \"issue_number\": 58, \"body\": \"placeholder for yml plots\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/58\", \"display_title\": \"YAML Plotting\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/56\", \"title\": \"productivity | Meetings\", \"issue_number\": 56, \"body\": \"- [ ] Develop an AI tool for meetings, recognizing voice  and\\u00a0giving\\u00a0summary out of it \", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/56\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | Meetings\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/52\", \"title\": \"YAML file split\", \"issue_number\": 52, \"body\": \"- [x] create individual function for ruamel as module\\n- [x] refactor save yml files\\n- [x] make an X-Y plot out of 2 arrays in the yml file using our visualization template\\n\\n- [x] Install program. https://www.orcina.com/orcaflex/demo/\\n  - [ ] Automate the opening or otherwise of the OrcaFlex .yml  test.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/52\", \"display_title\": \"YAML file split\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/42\", \"title\": \"productivity | PB Hardware and Utility Readiness\", \"issue_number\": 42, \"body\": \"- [ ] clone client project, https://github.com/vamseeachanta/seanation\\n- [ ] Install programs\\n  - [x] Github account (login and comment) (PB)\\n    - [x] working seamlessly \\n    - [x] explore github digitalmodel online . https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel\\n  - [x] Autocad (license)\\n  - [x] FreeCAD\\n  - [ ] Git (PB)\\n    - [x] Install git from link here. https://git-scm.com/ (PB)\\n    - [ ] set-up daily commit cycle using git-bash (VA)\\n\\n\\n- [ ] Hardware\\n  - [ ] Blender (not compatible). Remote access to windows/Linux? (VA)\\n  - [x] Get earphones (PB)\\n\\n- [x] Learn Google Meet\\n  - [x] Schedule 4 meetings independently\\n\\n  - [ ] Miniconda Python\\n    - [x] Install python https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/install/ (PB)\\n    - [ ] Further work to be assigned (VA)\\n\\n  - [x] install notepad++. https://notepad-plus-plus.org/downloads/\\n  - [x] install VSCOde. https://code.visualstudio.com/\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/42\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | PB Hardware and Utility Readiness\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/40\", \"title\": \" productivity | Marketing\", \"issue_number\": 40, \"body\": \"- [ ] Actively manage LinkedIn and X \\n- [ ] website simplification and revamp for AceEngineer \\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/40\", \"display_title\": \" productivity | Marketing\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/39\", \"title\": \"productivity | email clean up\", \"issue_number\": 39, \"body\": \"- [x] email is not for storage\\n- [x] method or script to clean up \\n  - [x] emails with starred & important should reside forever\\n  - [x] other emails not important and older than 365 days (n days) should be deleted\\n  - [x] reduce or eliminate spam over time\\n\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/39\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | email clean up\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/38\", \"title\": \"productivity | Knowledge Management\", \"issue_number\": 38, \"body\": \"- [ ] Read obsidian resources provided by Siva\\n  - [ ] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cBm95iCcX2E\\n  - [ ] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nJ660t5ku9A\\n  - [ ] other?\\n- [ ] Install required packages across machines\\n- [ ] tba\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/38\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | Knowledge Management\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/37\", \"title\": \"Scalability | Process, People\", \"issue_number\": 37, \"body\": \"- [ ] Sales\\r\\n  - [ ] ?\\r\\n- [ ] Process\\r\\n- [ ] Enhance productivity\\r\\n  - [ ] Samdan - ? \\r\\n  - [ ] Prasad - ?\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/37\", \"display_title\": \"Scalability | Process, People\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/36\", \"title\": \"productivity | Consolidate hardware\", \"issue_number\": 36, \"body\": \"- [ ] setup linux machine\\n  - [x] Advanced graphics card\\n  - [ ] sound card seem to exist via graphics card\\n  - [ ] setup smb for 8 TB drive\\n  - [ ] double monitor for Linux machine\\n  - [ ] remote login for india employees\\n    - [ ] XSERVER for source \\n    - [ ] XClient for target \\n  - [ ] ACMA remote login on Linux machine?\\n- [ ] USB-C sound card for 2nd computer for ACMA meetings?\\n- [ ] wired internet \\n  - [ ] if outages are frequeny, explore options\\n  - [ ] tba\\n- [x] KVM - functional\\n  - observations:\\n    - Single monitor set-up for 3 PCs (2 windows and linux) \\n    - 1 keyboard & mouse combo working seamlessly\\n    - wired remote handy to change\\n    - double monitor requires twice the wires  (Not setup due to graphics card limitation on 2 other PCs)\\n  - 3 PCs input\\n  - 1 keyboard, 1 mouse input\\n  - 1 monitor output\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/36\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | Consolidate hardware\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/35\", \"title\": \"productivity | Consolidate repos\", \"issue_number\": 35, \"body\": \"- [ ] Repo management\\r\\n  - [ ] Remove/Consolidate stale repos\\r\\n  - [ ] Issues only in select repos i.e. digitalmodel, aceengineer_admin, assetutilities\\r\\n  - [ ] No stale branches in repos\\r\\n- [ ] Remove/Consolidate following repos:\\r\\n  - [x] energy Public\\r\\n  - [ ] energydata Public\\r\\n  - [ ] teamresumes Public\\r\\n  - [ ] acma-projects Private\\r\\n  - [ ] assetutilities Public\\r\\n  - [ ] achantas-data Private\\r\\n  - [ ] digitalmodel Public\\r\\n  - [ ] doris Private\\r\\n  - [ ] aceengineer-admin Private\\r\\n  - [ ] client_projects\\r\\n  - [ ] achantas-media Private\\r\\n  - [x] saipem Private\\r\\n  - [x] investments Private\\r\\n  - [x] rock-oil-field Private\\r\\n  - [x] py_package Public\\r\\n  - [ ] hobbies Public\\r\\n  - [x] spire_projects Private\\r\\n  - [x] hairbyliz Public\\r\\n  - [x] ecs Private\\r\\n  - [x] structuralstrength Public\\r\\n  - [x] pipecapacity Public\\r\\n  - [x] pyintegrity Public\\r\\n  - [x] predyct Private\\r\\n  - [x] petrope Private\\r\\n  - [x] leveraged-multi-family-analysis Public\\r\\n  - [x] digitaltwinfeed Private\\r\\n  - [x] probabilisticrisk Public\\r\\n  - [x] OGManufacturing Private\\r\\n  - [ ] sd-work Private\\r\\n  - [ ] achantas Private\\r\\n  - [x] aceengineer-website Private\\r\\n  - [x] aceengineercode Public\\r\\n  - [x] pymvil Public\\r\\n  - [x] python_react_postgresql Private\\r\\n  - [x] amgsharepointcontents Public\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/35\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | Consolidate repos\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/33\", \"title\": \"productivity | Consolidate data\", \"issue_number\": 33, \"body\": \"- [ ] setup linux machine\\r\\n  - [ ] ?\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/33\", \"display_title\": \"productivity | Consolidate data\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/31\", \"title\": \"tech debt | ACMA | Source Files | Sync vs. Copy\", \"issue_number\": 31, \"body\": \"Objective: \\r\\n- [ ] Determine the best way from one of methods below and implement in ACMA WLNG project\\r\\n- [ ] Prepare boiler plate code for ignoring at folder level not file level\\r\\n\\r\\nMethod 1 (Ideal):\\r\\n- Run and sync in same location\\r\\n- explicit definition using git ignore at folder level\\r\\n- sync folders should be clear upfront for project or client.\\r\\n\\r\\nMethod 2: Separate Location, Copy relevant\\r\\n- Run in run_location\\r\\n- sync in sync_location\\r\\n- Have a batch to copy relevant files from run_location to sync_location\\r\\n\\r\\nMethod 3: Another method?\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/31\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | ACMA | Source Files | Sync vs. Copy\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30\", \"title\": \"tech debt | AI agents\", \"issue_number\": 30, \"body\": \"Objective:\\r\\n- Utilize AI agents in day to day work to help with code\\r\\n- Interface AI agent configurations with copilot (?)\\r\\n- Develop ecosystem for this purpose\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] Define AI agents\\r\\n- [ ] Write yml files for ai agents.\\r\\n  - [x] prelim by AI. see prelim file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/202501/_coding_agents/multi_agent.yaml\\r\\n  - [ ] visionaries (steve jobs, etc.) (VA)\\r\\n  - [x] python programmer (SS)\\r\\n    - [ ] Write a test any time a program fails (manual)\\r\\n    - [ ] Simplify input file preparation (parametric - less scope of mistakes and more for AI to prepare the files)\\r\\n    - [ ] Think of and think like AI agents in all the work.\\r\\n    - [ ] consistent variable or file naming\\r\\n  - [x] devops ci-cd  (SS)\\r\\n  - [ ] engineer physics (VA)\\r\\n  - [ ] engineer finance (VA)\\r\\n  - [ ] continual improvement using AI. Refer to our repositories and our own work and the corrections we made to the work.  (VA)\\r\\n- [ ] Prompt templates (.yaml)\\r\\n- [ ] Transfer work to other libraries\\r\\n  - [ ] assetutilities (all ai work will be here)\\r\\n  - [ ] determine best method to transfer to other libraries seamlessly \\r\\n  - [ ] digitalmodel\\r\\n  - [ ] energydata etc.\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | AI agents\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/19\", \"title\": \"tech debt | git | branch, computer and multiuser merge\", \"issue_number\": 19, \"body\": \"Objective:\\n- Repo developers will have a daily (1 hr) gitbash script that will execute automatically.\\n- Test requirements: New code (by any user in any computer) should not fail existing tests in master.\\n  - If any tests fail, the team should know at earliest\\n -  at merge, run unit and integration tests\\n- Branch management\\n  - Current branch\\n    - name: $YYYY$MM\\n    - Branch on cloud and PR created\\n  - Stale branches\\n    - No branches other than $YYYY$MM\\n    - $YYYY$(MM-1) should be pushed to remote\\n \\n- [ ] Prerequisite: \\n  - [ ] develop AI agents: python programmer, ci-cd engineer. see https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30\\n  - [ ] gitbash knowledge across team (running, simple scripting guidance)\\n- [ ] implementation strategy\\n  - [ ] scripts in gitbash. see evolving notes: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/fce0e9596fbe7f8419edcac0c638308f690ca3af/docs/sub_shell/gitbash.md\\n  - [ ] conscious choice of script execution: local vs. github command server vs. other?\\n- [ ] branch management\\n  - [x] name convention: YYYYMM\\n  - [ ] merge at start of month\\n  - [ ] remove all stale branches in all repos\\n  - [ ] daily script to create report\\n    - [x] check local and remote branches. Suggest to consolidate them\\n    - [x] check correct branch\\n    - [ ] if unexisting, create new one and push to remote?\\n    - [ ] end of month actions?\\n- [ ] commit - name\\n- [ ] commit prehooks\\n\\n- [ ] assetutilities\\n  - [x] No stale branches. \\n    - [x] delete 2024 branch\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] digitalmodel\\n  - [x] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] teamresumes\\n  - [x] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] energydata\\n  - [x] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] assethold\\n  - [x] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] energy\\n  - [ ] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] relocate documentation\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] acma-projects\\n  - [x] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] achantasdata\\n  - [ ] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] achantasmedia\\n  - [ ] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\\n- [ ] aceengineer-admin\\n  - [ ] No stale branches\\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \\n  - [ ] merge at end of month\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/19\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | git | branch, computer and multiuser merge\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/60\", \"title\": \"repo | package development\", \"issue_number\": 60, \"body\": \"- [ ] develop git bash scripts to manage package uploads to PyPI for all repo's. \\n- [ ] Migrate to GitHub Actions (Twine under the hood) over time\\n  - [ ] https://www.caktusgroup.com/blog/2021/02/11/automating-pypi-releases/\\n  - [ ] https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/publishing-package-distribution-releases-using-github-actions-ci-cd-workflows/\\n  - [ ] Learn how to manage secrets to upload to pypi\\n- [ ] Create pypi tokens for repo\\n  - [ ] https://pypi.org/help/#apitoken\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/60\", \"display_title\": \"repo | package development\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/59\", \"title\": \"yaml_utilities | Variable Definition\", \"issue_number\": 59, \"body\": \"Objective: establish the best way to define variables in YAML files to identify the following scenarios\\n\\n- [ ] incorporate the logic in our repos. ( together ) , see image below \\n- [x] YAML single variable and directive block\\n  - [x] Refer : https://docs.geoserver.org/2.21.x/en/user/styling/ysld/reference/variables.html\\n  - [x] Example yaml file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/3ba6d9bff20957d4659ad7beed6727404a55014f/tests/modules/yaml_utlities/yml/variables/variable_example_1.yml\\n  - [x] test the code for both single and block variables\\n\\n- [x] YAML placeholders\\n  - [x] Refer : https://stackoverflow.com/questions/41620674/use-placeholders-in-yaml\\n  - [x] Example yaml file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/3ba6d9bff20957d4659ad7beed6727404a55014f/tests/modules/yaml_utlities/yml/variables/variable_example_2.yml\\n  - [x] Test code for yml placeholder in python\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/59\", \"display_title\": \"yaml_utilities | Variable Definition\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/41\", \"title\": \"tech debt | Clean code\", \"issue_number\": 41, \"body\": \"Objective: Assumption that consistent code will help AI add new code/documentation faster, seamless, \\n\\nhttps://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/202502/docs/clean_code.md\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/41\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | Clean code\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/29\", \"title\": \"tech debt | switch engine to registry design pattern\", \"issue_number\": 29, \"body\": \"siva used it with writers.py, doris_writer.py. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe way reportgen uses the registry design (to read a writer class name from config yml, then initialize the appropriate writer class and initiate the run method) is similar/ same as what engine is doing. \\r\\n\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/29\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | switch engine to registry design pattern\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/28\", \"title\": \"tech debt | switch to loguru\", \"issue_number\": 28, \"body\": \"- [x] currently assetutilities uses python built-in logging. Log files are also crated.\\n\\n- [x] loguru has color coded logging and much more detailed diagnostic context. \\n\\n- [x] Ensure loguru messages are added to the default run log files in log directory (@samdansk2 )\\n- [x] Add documentation to assetutilities (@samdansk2 )\\n\\nReferences:\\nhttps://betterstack.com/community/guides/logging/loguru/\\nhttps://github.com/Delgan/loguru/issues/80\\nhttps://loguru.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/logger.html\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/28\", \"display_title\": \"tech debt | switch to loguru\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/75\", \"title\": \"Simplify CI test environment to use the declared test dependency path\", \"issue_number\": 75, \"body\": \"Summary\\nThe recent fixes restored the canonical pytest command and async plugin support, but CI still installs test tooling via a mixed path:\\n- `uv sync --group dev`\\n- `uv pip install pytest-benchmark`\\n\\nWhy this is a future cleanup item\\n- The repo now has a clearer testing contract, but CI still does not use a single declared test dependency path\\n- Mixing a dev group with an ad hoc `uv pip install` is harder to reason about and can drift from `pyproject.toml`\\n\\nSuggested follow-up\\n- Standardize CI on one explicit dependency path for test execution\\n- Prefer using the declared test dependency set directly, or otherwise document why CI intentionally differs\\n- Remove the extra ad hoc `uv pip install pytest-benchmark` step if it becomes redundant\\n\\nAcceptance criteria\\n- CI installs test dependencies through one consistent declared path\\n- Workflow YAML matches the packaging model in `pyproject.toml`\\n- No unnecessary ad hoc pytest plugin install remains\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/75\", \"display_title\": \"Simplify CI test environment to use the declared test dependency path\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/281\", \"title\": \"WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7\", \"issue_number\": 281, \"body\": \"## WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7\\n\\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** orcaflex-license-machine\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udd28 Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udccb Plan</summary>\\n\\n## Description\\nExtract ~235 OrcaFlex .dat models from rock-oil-field/s7/, sanitize client references, convert to YAML, organize into library categories (jumper, installation, mooring, training), generate spec.yml for each model group, validate round-trip via 3-way benchmark.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- [ ] Sanitization script: `scripts/sanitize_s7_models.py`\\n- [ ] Spec extraction script: `scripts/extract_s7_specs.py`\\n- [ ] Legal deny list: `digitalmodel/.legal-deny-list.yaml`\\n- [ ] Sanitized models in `docs/modules/orcaflex/{jumper,installation,mooring,training}/`\\n- [ ] spec.yml for each model group\\n- [ ] Jumper analysis skill: `.claude/skills/orcaflex-jumper-analysis/SKILL.md`\\n- [ ] Legal sanity scan skill: `.claude/skills/legal-sanity-scan/SKILL.md`\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (exit code 0)\\n- [ ] Round-trip validation on jumper + mooring models\\n\\n## Progress\\n- 2026-02-11: Plan approved. Scripts and skills creation in progress.\\n\\n## Agentic AI Horizon\\n\\n- Extracting and cataloguing OrcaFlex models from rock-oil-field/s7 creates a sanitised reference library that agents can use for pattern matching and schema design \\u2014 high reuse value.\\n- OrcaFlex model extraction and sanitisation requires domain expertise to identify what is generic vs client-specific; this won't be automated by better models.\\n- **Disposition: do now** \\u2014 reference model extraction is prerequisite for WRK-032, WRK-036, and WRK-045; close this working item promptly.\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\u2705 Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] Sanitization script: `scripts/sanitize_s7_models.py`\\n- [ ] Spec extraction script: `scripts/extract_s7_specs.py`\\n- [ ] Legal deny list: `digitalmodel/.legal-deny-list.yaml`\\n- [ ] Sanitized models in `docs/modules/orcaflex/{jumper,installation,mooring,training}/`\\n- [ ] spec.yml for each model group\\n- [ ] Jumper analysis skill: `.claude/skills/orcaflex-jumper-analysis/SKILL.md`\\n- [ ] Legal sanity scan skill: `.claude/skills/legal-sanity-scan/SKILL.md`\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (exit code 0)\\n- [ ] Round-trip validation on jumper + mooring models\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83e\\uddea TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udcca Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/281\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/284\", \"title\": \"WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms\", \"issue_number\": 284, \"body\": \"## WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms\\n\\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** acma-ansys05\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udd28 Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udccb Plan</summary>\\n\\n# Update OrcaFlex License Agreement\\n\\n## What\\nUpdate the OrcaFlex license agreement document with correct party addresses, ensure compliance with the existing ACMA-OrcaFlex agreement, and clarify 3rd-party usage terms.\\n\\n## Reference Documents\\n- **Preliminary agreement**: `D:\\\\workspace-hub\\\\aceengineer-admin\\\\admin\\\\orcaflex\\\\`\\n- **ACMA agreement to comply with**: `ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf` (same folder)\\n\\n## Required Changes\\n\\n### 1. Add Party Addresses\\n- **ACMA Address**: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\\n- **Achanta Aceengineer Inc Address**: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\\n\\n### 2. Compliance Check\\n- Review `ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf` and ensure the updated agreement complies with all terms\\n\\n### 3. Third-Party Clarification\\n- Clarify the definition and role of \\\"3rd party\\\" in the agreement\\n- Add 3rd-party usage terms if needed to cover sublicensing or subcontracting scenarios\\n\\n## Why\\nProper legal documentation with correct addresses, compliance with existing agreements, and clear 3rd-party terms protects all parties and ensures the OrcaFlex license is used within contractual bounds.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] ACMA address added to agreement: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\\n- [ ] Achanta Aceengineer Inc address added: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\\n- [ ] Agreement reviewed against ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf for compliance\\n- [ ] 3rd-party definition clarified in agreement\\n- [ ] Additional 3rd-party terms added if gaps identified\\n- [ ] Final document ready for review\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\u2705 Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] ACMA address added to agreement: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\\n- [ ] Achanta Aceengineer Inc address added: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\\n- [ ] Agreement reviewed against ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf for compliance\\n- [ ] 3rd-party definition clarified in agreement\\n- [ ] Additional 3rd-party terms added if gaps identified\\n- [ ] Final document ready for review\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83e\\uddea TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udcca Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/284\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/283\", \"title\": \"WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels \\u2014 AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response\", \"issue_number\": 283, \"body\": \"## WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels \\u2014 AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response\\n\\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\\n**Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** orcaflex-license-machine\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udd28 Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udccb Plan</summary>\\n\\n# Passing Ship Analysis for Moored Vessels\\n\\n## What\\nBuild a passing ship analysis capability for moored vessels. Calculate hydrodynamic forces on a moored vessel due to a passing ship (surge, sway, yaw), evaluate mooring line tensions under passing ship events, and generate standardized reports. Covers perpendicular and parallel passing cases, with/without wind, at varying speeds and distances.\\n\\n## Why\\n- Passing ship effects are a critical design case for port/terminal mooring systems\\n- ~15+ historical projects demonstrate recurring demand for this analysis type\\n- Currently relies on standalone Excel tool (`PassingShipForceCalculator.xlsm`) and manual AQWA runs\\n- Standardizing into the digitalmodel framework enables parametric studies, consistent reporting, and reuse\\n\\n## Resources (local, not in repo)\\n- **Tool**: `G:\\\\ACMA Tool\\\\Passing Ships\\\\` \\u2014 existing passing ship force calculator (Excel-based)\\n- **Archive**: `R:\\\\Archive - Drive J\\\\` \\u2014 ~15+ past project folders with AQWA models, reports, and results\\n- **Key tool files**: `PassingShipForceCalculator.xlsm` (force calculation), `PassingShipForceCalculator 3.7 knot.xlsm` (speed variant)\\n- **Output examples**: Line tension plots at various passing speeds (3.0 knot, 3.7 knot), mooring line groups (1-6, 7-12)\\n\\n## Technical Scope\\n1. **Passing ship force model** \\u2014 hydrodynamic interaction forces (surge, sway, yaw) as function of:\\n   - Passing ship speed, size (displacement, length, beam, draft)\\n   - Moored vessel dimensions\\n   - Separation distance (lateral)\\n   - Water depth / depth-to-draft ratio\\n   - Passing angle (parallel, perpendicular, oblique)\\n2. **Mooring response** \\u2014 time-domain mooring analysis with passing ship force time history:\\n   - Line tensions per mooring line\\n   - Vessel motions (surge, sway, yaw excursions)\\n   - Fender loads\\n   - Combined with wind, current, wave (with/without passing vessel scenarios)\\n3. **Analysis cases** \\u2014 parametric matrix:\\n   - Wind with passing vessel / wind without passing vessel\\n   - Perpendicular passing / parallel passing\\n   - Multiple passing speeds\\n   - Short ship / long ship variants\\n4. **PassingShipForceCalculator extraction** \\u2014 reverse-engineer the Excel tool logic into Python\\n5. **AQWA integration** \\u2014 passing ship force application in AQWA mooring analysis (or OrcaFlex equivalent)\\n6. **Reporting** \\u2014 standardized HTML report per WRK-129 convention\\n\\n## PassingShipSpec \\u2014 Analysis Specification\\nCreate a `PassingShipSpec` (similar to `DiffractionSpec` pattern) that fully defines a passing ship analysis:\\n- **Moored vessel**: hull geometry, mooring arrangement, loading condition, RAOs\\n- **Passing ship**: type, displacement, LOA, beam, draft, speed, track (distance, angle)\\n- **Environment**: water depth, wind speed/direction, current, wave conditions\\n- **Analysis matrix**: cases (with/without wind, with/without passing, speeds, angles)\\n- **Output requests**: line tensions, vessel motions, fender loads, force time histories\\n- Spec format: YAML (`spec.yml`), validated by Pydantic schema, drives automated analysis pipeline\\n\\n## Benchmarking \\u2014 5-7 Historical Projects\\nReproduce 5-7 past passing ship projects from `R:\\\\Archive - Drive J\\\\` to validate the new implementation:\\n1. Extract original analysis inputs (vessel data, mooring layout, passing ship parameters, environmental conditions)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\u2705 Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [x] `PassingShipSpec` Pydantic schema defined and validated\\n- [x] Passing ship force calculation implemented in Python (from Excel tool extraction)\\n- [x] Force time history generation for given passing scenario (speed, distance, ship size)\\n- [ ] Mooring response analysis with passing ship forces (line tensions, motions)\\n- [ ] Parametric study capability (speed \\u00d7 distance \\u00d7 wind \\u00d7 passing angle matrix)\\n- [ ] 5-7 benchmark cases reproduced from historical projects, results within tolerance\\n- [ ] Each benchmark has sanitized `spec.yml` in `docs/domains/orcaflex/passing_ship/`\\n- [ ] Standardized HTML report with force plots, tension envelopes, motion time histories\\n- [x] Integration with existing hydrodynamics module\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83e\\uddea TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udcca Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/283\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels \\u2014 AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/280\", \"title\": \"WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat\", \"issue_number\": 280, \"body\": \"## WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat\\n\\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering/marine\\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** acma-ansys05\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udd28 Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udccb Plan</summary>\\n\\n# OrcaFlex Format Converter: License-Required Tasks\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe OrcaFlex Three-Way Format Converter (`format_converter/`) was implemented on a non-licensed machine. **All 102 tests pass** using YAML-only operations. The following tasks require an OrcaFlex license (OrcFxAPI) and must be completed on a licensed machine.\\n\\n## Completed (no license needed)\\n\\n- [x] `yaml_utils.py` \\u2014 Canonical `OrcaFlexDumper`, `orcaflex_dump()`, `orcaflex_load()`\\n- [x] `protocols.py` \\u2014 `ConversionReport` dataclass, `FormatConverter` protocol\\n- [x] `section_mapping.py` \\u2014 `SECTION_MAPPING`, `REVERSE_SECTION_MAPPING`, `INPUT_PARAMETERS`\\n- [x] `format_detector.py` \\u2014 `FormatType` enum, `detect_format()`\\n- [x] `single_to_modular.py` \\u2014 `SingleToModularConverter` (promoted from yaml_to_include.py)\\n- [x] `modular_to_single.py` \\u2014 `ModularToSingleConverter` (extracted from level_3_physical.py)\\n- [x] `spec_to_modular.py` \\u2014 `SpecToModularConverter` (wraps ModularModelGenerator)\\n- [x] `spec_to_single.py` \\u2014 `SpecToSingleConverter` (chains spec\\u2192modular\\u2192single)\\n- [x] `modular_to_spec.py` \\u2014 `ModularToSpecConverter` (best-effort reverse extraction)\\n- [x] `single_to_spec.py` \\u2014 `SingleToSpecConverter` (chains single\\u2192modular\\u2192spec)\\n- [x] `cli.py` \\u2014 8 subcommands (single2modular, modular2single, spec2modular, etc.)\\n- [x] `__main__.py` \\u2014 `python -m` entry point\\n- [x] `pyproject.toml` \\u2014 `orcaflex-convert` entry point registered\\n- [x] 102 tests passing (yaml_utils, format_detector, single\\u2194modular, round-trip, spec conversions, CLI)\\n\\n## Pending Tasks (require OrcaFlex license)\\n\\n### 1. End-to-end OrcaFlex validation test\\nRun converted YAML files through OrcaFlex to verify they load and simulate correctly:\\n```bash\\n# On licensed machine:\\nuv run python -m digitalmodel.modules.orcaflex.format_converter \\\\\\n    single2modular \\\"docs/modules/orcaflex/examples/raw/A01/A01 Catenary riser.yml\\\" \\\\\\n    -o /tmp/a01_modular/\\n\\n# Load in OrcaFlex and verify static analysis runs\\nuv run python -c \\\"\\nimport OrcFxAPI\\nmodel = OrcFxAPI.Model()\\nmodel.LoadData('/tmp/a01_modular/master.yml')\\nmodel.CalculateStatics()\\nprint('Static analysis OK')\\n\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Round-trip OrcaFlex binary fidelity test\\nVerify round-trip through OrcaFlex binary format preserves model:\\n```\\nA01.yml \\u2192 single2modular \\u2192 modular \\u2192 OrcaFlex load \\u2192 OrcaFlex save \\u2192 compare\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Update backward-compat wrapper in `scripts/conversion/yaml_to_include.py`\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\u2705 Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [x] `yaml_utils.py` \\u2014 Canonical `OrcaFlexDumper`, `orcaflex_dump()`, `orcaflex_load()`\\n- [x] `protocols.py` \\u2014 `ConversionReport` dataclass, `FormatConverter` protocol\\n- [x] `section_mapping.py` \\u2014 `SECTION_MAPPING`, `REVERSE_SECTION_MAPPING`, `INPUT_PARAMETERS`\\n- [x] `format_detector.py` \\u2014 `FormatType` enum, `detect_format()`\\n- [x] `single_to_modular.py` \\u2014 `SingleToModularConverter` (promoted from yaml_to_include.py)\\n- [x] `modular_to_single.py` \\u2014 `ModularToSingleConverter` (extracted from level_3_physical.py)\\n- [x] `spec_to_modular.py` \\u2014 `SpecToModularConverter` (wraps ModularModelGenerator)\\n- [x] `spec_to_single.py` \\u2014 `SpecToSingleConverter` (chains spec\\u2192modular\\u2192single)\\n- [x] `modular_to_spec.py` \\u2014 `ModularToSpecConverter` (best-effort reverse extraction)\\n- [x] `single_to_spec.py` \\u2014 `SingleToSpecConverter` (chains single\\u2192modular\\u2192spec)\\n- [x] `cli.py` \\u2014 8 subcommands (single2modular, modular2single, spec2modular, etc.)\\n- [x] `__main__.py` \\u2014 `python -m` entry point\\n- [x] `pyproject.toml` \\u2014 `orcaflex-convert` entry point registered\\n- [x] 102 tests passing (yaml_utils, format_detector, single\\u2194modular, round-trip, spec conversions, CLI)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83e\\uddea TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udcca Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/280\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/277\", \"title\": \"WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering \\u2014 hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies\", \"issue_number\": 277, \"body\": \"## WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering \\u2014 hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies\\n\\n**Status:** working | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering/pipeline\\n**Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** ace-linux-2\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udd28 Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udccb Plan</summary>\\n\\n# FreeCAD Deep Parametric Engineering\\n\\n## Mission\\n\\nEnable production-grade FreeCAD automation for parametric hull generation with hydrostatic analysis, FEM preprocessing through the CalculiX solver chain, and design table driven parameter sweep studies with automated exports.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe freecad-automation skill covers the API surface. This item adds depth for real engineering work:\\n\\n1. **Parametric hull generation with hydrostatics** \\u2014 define hull form via principal dimensions (L, B, T, Cb) \\u2192 generate NURBS hull surface \\u2192 compute hydrostatics (displacement, KM, BM, waterplane area) \\u2192 export to STEP/STL for downstream solvers\\n2. **FEM preprocessing chain** \\u2014 geometry \\u2192 gmsh mesh \\u2192 boundary conditions \\u2192 material properties \\u2192 CalculiX input deck \\u2192 solve \\u2192 extract stress/displacement results\\n3. **Design table driven studies** \\u2014 YAML-defined parameter matrix (e.g., plate thickness, stiffener spacing, material grade) \\u2192 batch FreeCAD model generation \\u2192 batch FEM analysis \\u2192 results comparison table\\n4. **Round-trip validation** \\u2014 FreeCAD \\u2192 STEP \\u2192 gmsh mesh \\u2192 verify watertightness \\u2192 OpenFOAM/AQWA case setup (validates the full pipeline from CAD to solver)\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nFreeCAD is the only open-source parametric CAD tool in the stack. Making it work reliably for hull design and structural analysis enables rapid concept screening without commercial licenses. The FEM chain through CalculiX provides structural validation capability that currently requires ANSYS (licensed, limited to acma-ansys05).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Hull generator: input (L=100m, B=20m, T=8m, Cb=0.7) \\u2192 FreeCAD NURBS hull \\u2192 hydrostatics within 2% of analytical\\n- [ ] FEM chain: plate with hole \\u2192 gmsh mesh \\u2192 CalculiX \\u2192 stress concentration factor within 5% of analytical (Kt \\u2248 3.0)\\n- [ ] Design table: 3+ parameter variations \\u2192 batch generation \\u2192 results comparison YAML\\n- [ ] Round-trip: FreeCAD hull \\u2192 STEP \\u2192 gmsh \\u2192 STL \\u2192 verify closed surface (manifold check)\\n- [ ] All operations headless via freecadcmd (no GUI dependency)\\n- [ ] Integration tests with known engineering problems (simply supported beam, pressure vessel)\\n- [ ] Update freecad-automation skill with deep workflow sections\\n\\n## Plan\\n\\n*To be developed at Stage 4.*\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\u2705 Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] Hull generator: input (L=100m, B=20m, T=8m, Cb=0.7) \\u2192 FreeCAD NURBS hull \\u2192 hydrostatics within 2% of analytical\\n- [ ] FEM chain: plate with hole \\u2192 gmsh mesh \\u2192 CalculiX \\u2192 stress concentration factor within 5% of analytical (Kt \\u2248 3.0)\\n- [ ] Design table: 3+ parameter variations \\u2192 batch generation \\u2192 results comparison YAML\\n- [ ] Round-trip: FreeCAD hull \\u2192 STEP \\u2192 gmsh \\u2192 STL \\u2192 verify closed surface (manifold check)\\n- [ ] All operations headless via freecadcmd (no GUI dependency)\\n- [ ] Integration tests with known engineering problems (simply supported beam, pressure vessel)\\n- [ ] Update freecad-automation skill with deep workflow sections\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83e\\uddea TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>\\ud83d\\udcca Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/277\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering \\u2014 hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/271\", \"title\": \"WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration \\u2014 Phase 2 deployment for both clients\", \"issue_number\": 271, \"body\": \"## WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration \\u2014 Phase 2 deployment for both clients\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['frontierdeepwater', 'TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nDeploy engineering AI chatbots via Microsoft Teams for both Client 1 and Client 2,\\nreplacing the desktop demo with a persistent, team-accessible assistant.\\n\\nBoth clients have Microsoft Teams \\u2014 this enables a low-friction deployment path\\nwithout requiring browser setup or CLI access per engineer.\\n\\n### Architecture\\n\\n**Option A (Recommended \\u2014 start here):**\\nTeams + Azure Bot Service + Claude API\\n```\\nEngineer (Teams) \\u2192 Azure Bot Service \\u2192 Claude API (with system prompt)\\n                       \\u2193\\n                 Logging / audit trail (Azure)\\n```\\n- System prompts from WRK-625 (Client 1) / WRK-629 (Client 2) loaded as bot persona\\n- No RAG required for Phase 2 \\u2014 system prompt + conversation context sufficient\\n- Cost: ~$20-200/mo per team (Claude API usage)\\n- Setup time: 1-2 days with Azure Bot Framework SDK\\n\\n**Option B (Graduate to when usage grows):**\\nTeams + Azure Bot Service + RAG backend\\n```\\nEngineer (Teams) \\u2192 Azure Bot Service \\u2192 RAG retriever \\u2192 Company knowledge base\\n                       \\u2193                    \\u2193\\n                 Claude API          Azure Cognitive Search / Pinecone\\n```\\n- Index calculation memos, project reports, design basis docs\\n- Cost: $500-2,000/mo\\n- Setup time: 2-4 weeks\\n\\n### Phase 2 Deliverables\\n\\n**Teams bot configuration:**\\n- `deployment/teams-bot/manifest.json` \\u2014 Teams app manifest\\n- `deployment/teams-bot/bot.py` \\u2014 Azure Bot Service handler (Python)\\n  - Routes messages to Claude API with discipline-specific system prompt\\n  - Handles conversation threading (multi-turn context)\\n  - Logs Q&A to Azure Table Storage for audit trail\\n- `deployment/teams-bot/config.yaml` \\u2014 API keys (env vars), model selection, rate limits\\n- `deployment/teams-bot/system_prompts/` \\u2014 symlink to `ai-initiatives/prompts/`\\n\\n**Client 1 Teams bot:**\\n- Bot name: \\\"Rigid Jumper Assistant\\\" (SME1's team channel)\\n- System prompt: `rigid_jumper_assistant.md` from WRK-625\\n- Fallback: \\\"Pipeline Engineering Assistant\\\" if pipeline queries detected\\n\\n**Client 2 Teams bot:**\\n- Bot name: \\\"Structural Engineering Assistant\\\"\\n- System prompt: `structural_offshore_assistant.md` from WRK-629\\n- Focused on diffraction / plate FFS / GoA\\n\\n**Shared infrastructure:**\\n- Azure resource group `aceengineer-ai-clients` with shared Bot Service\\n- Per-client app registrations (separate AAD apps for auth isolation)\\n- Usage dashboard: Azure Monitor \\u2192 daily token consumption per client\\n\\n### Rollout Plan\\n\\n```\\nWeek 2-3: Deploy bot to 2-3 engineers per team (pilot)\\nWeek 4:   Evaluate usage metrics, refine prompts from pilot feedback\\nWeek 5+:  Expand to full team; decide on RAG upgrade (Option B)\\n```\\n\\n### Knowledge Base Integration (Option B path)\\n\\nWhen graduating to RAG:\\n- Index sources: calculation memos, SOWs, design basis docs (client uploads)\\n- Chunking strategy: section-level (## headers) with frontmatter metadata\\n- Retrieval: top-3 chunks by cosine similarity, injected into Claude context\\n- Document store: Azure Blob Storage + Azure Cognitive Search\\n- Privacy: client 1 and client 2 data in separate search indexes (no cross-contamination)\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nMicrosoft Teams is already the communication hub at both clients \\u2014 deploying the AI\\nassistant there removes the \\\"I have to open another tab\\\" friction that kills adoption.\\nBot appears in the engineer's existing channel; questions feel natural in chat format.\\nAzure Bot Service + Claude API is a 2-day setup with no new infrastructure beyond\\nwhat both clients already have (Microsoft 365 / Azure tenant).\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] `deployment/teams-bot/bot.py` implemented with Claude API integration\\n- [ ] `deployment/teams-bot/manifest.json` created for Teams app deployment\\n- [ ] Client 1 bot deployed to test Teams tenant and validated (3 questions)\\n- [ ] Client 2 bot deployed to test Teams tenant and validated (3 questions)\\n- [ ] Conversation threading (multi-turn context) working\\n- [ ] Audit log (Q&A pairs) persisted to Azure Table Storage\\n- [ ] Usage dashboard stub in Azure Monitor\\n- [ ] README: 1-page deployment guide for client IT admin\\n- [ ] No client API keys or tenant IDs hardcoded \\u2014 all via env vars\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/271\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration \\u2014 Phase 2 deployment for both clients\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/270\", \"title\": \"WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package\", \"issue_number\": 270, \"body\": \"## WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** marine\\n\\n**Repo:** ['TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nDays 2\\u20135 deliverables for Client 2 engineering AI demo.\\n\\n### Calculation Templates (Day 2)\\n\\n**Diffraction analysis templates:**\\n- `demo/calc_diffraction_panel_model_setup.md` \\u2014 AQWA/WAMIT model conventions prompt:\\n  panel mesh requirements (8 panels per wavelength min), symmetry planes, free surface,\\n  waterplane area check, zero-speed vs forward speed; typical RAO output format\\n- `demo/calc_rao_interpretation.md` \\u2014 RAO extraction prompt: peak period identification,\\n  heading matrix coverage, cancellation frequencies, cross-coupling terms (heave/pitch)\\n- `demo/calc_qtf_second_order.md` \\u2014 QTF usage: difference-frequency loads for mooring\\n  low-frequency response; sum-frequency for TLP/spar springing; Newman's approximation\\n  when full QTF not available\\n\\n**Plate FFS calculation templates:**\\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part4_metal_loss.md` \\u2014 API 579-1 Part 4 for plate: average\\n  measured thickness vs minimum required; RSF_a screening; Level 1 vs Level 2 distinction\\n  for plates (no hoop stress \\u2014 limit load governs); MFFL (minimum future flaw limit)\\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part8_distortion.md` \\u2014 Part 8 shell distortions: peaking/angular\\n  misalignment in welds, out-of-roundness; equivalent stress from distortion; buckling\\n  interaction check for stiffened plates\\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part9_cracks.md` \\u2014 FAD approach for crack-like flaws:\\n  K_r vs L_r diagram; BS 7910 Level 2B; fracture toughness input (K_mat or J_mat);\\n  fatigue crack growth projection (Paris law); remaining life calculation\\n\\n**GoA analysis templates:**\\n- `demo/calc_goa_seismic_check.md` \\u2014 API RP 2EQ spectral analysis: platform period,\\n  base shear, OLE/CLE/ALE limit states; pushover capacity check\\n- `demo/calc_goa_extreme_metocean.md` \\u2014 100-yr GoA wave/current/wind parameters;\\n  comparison with GoM (typically harsher wave heights, lower Hs for ice-dominated zones);\\n  API RP 2N ice loading: first-year ridges, multi-year ice pressure, ice crushing force\\n\\n### Multi-Step Workflows (Day 4)\\n\\n**Diffraction-to-structural load workflow:**\\nFile: `demo/workflow_diffraction_to_structural.md`\\n1. Input: water depth, vessel/structure dimensions, wave environment (Hs, Tp, heading)\\n2. Step 1 \\u2192 panel model adequacy check (mesh density for peak period)\\n3. Step 2 \\u2192 RAO interpretation (identify governing responses by heading)\\n4. Step 3 \\u2192 combined load derivation (wave + wind + current for governing sea state)\\n5. Step 4 \\u2192 structural utilisation flag (member/joint check indication)\\n6. Output: summary table \\u2014 governing headings, load cases for detailed structural check\\n\\n**GoA FFS decision workflow:**\\nFile: `demo/workflow_goa_ffs_decision.md`\\n1. Input: inspection findings (wall loss % / crack dimensions / distortion mm)\\n2. Step 1 \\u2192 GoA environment severity classification (ice zone, seismic zone, metocean)\\n3. Step 2 \\u2192 FFS Level 1 screening (API 579-1 plates)\\n4. Step 3 \\u2192 remaining life at GoA corrosion rate\\n5. Step 4 \\u2192 re-inspection interval recommendation (BSEE GoA ops environment)\\n6. Output: FFS verdict + GoA-specific inspection schedule\\n\\n### Maritime Legal Case Templates (Day 4)\\n\\n**Casualty investigation analysis:**\\n- `demo/maritime_casualty_analysis.md` \\u2014 prompt template for reviewing MAIB/NTSB/USCG\\n  reports: extract contributing factors \\u2192 ISM Code failures \\u2192 root-cause hierarchy;\\n  sample: parse a MAIB report section and output structured findings table\\n- `demo/maritime_statistical_context.md` \\u2014 prompt using `worldenergydata.MAIBLoader` +\\n  `NTSBMarineLoader` (WRK-320): \\\"find comparable incidents for vessel type X / failure\\n  mode Y\\\" \\u2192 precedent table with dates, vessel types, outcomes, regulatory citations\\n\\n**Expert witness support:**\\n- `demo/expert_witness_report_template.md` \\u2014 structured technical report for legal:\\n  scope of appointment, methodology, engineering findings, opinion (standard of care),\\n  limitations; Daubert-compliant framing; deposition Q&A prep prompt\\n- `demo/liability_framing_prompt.md` \\u2014 translate engineering findings into\\n  legal causation language: \\\"the failure of [component] was a proximate cause of...\\n  consistent with / inconsistent with the standard of care because...\\\"\\n\\n**Maritime legal decision workflow:**\\nFile: `demo/workflow_maritime_legal_analysis.md`\\n1. Input: incident description (vessel type, operation, casualty type, jurisdiction)\\n2. Step 1 \\u2192 applicable regulatory framework (USCG CFR / MAIB / IMO)\\n3. Step 2 \\u2192 ISM Code non-conformity screen (safety management system failures)\\n4. Step 3 \\u2192 comparable incident precedents (MAIB/NTSB database query)\\n5. Step 4 \\u2192 standard of care assessment (industry practice vs regulatory requirement)\\n6. Step 5 \\u2192 damages estimation framework (limitation of liability, P&I coverage)\\n7. Output: case analysis memo outline with evidence gaps flagged\\n\\n### BSEE GoA Data Prompts (Day 4)\\nFile: `demo/goa_bsee_data_queries.md`\\n- GoA active leases, historical platforms (Cook Inlet focus)\\n- Environmental study requirements for GoA OCS projects\\n- Seismic hazard data for GoA vs GOM structural design\\n- Ice zone classification per USCG/BSEE GoA regulations\\n\\n### Demo Package (Day 5)\\nFile: `demo/demo_script_client2.md`\\n- 15-20 min flow: diffraction overview \\u2192 plate FFS walkthrough \\u2192 GoA live data query\\n- 3 \\\"wow\\\" moments: QTF second-order loads, plate crack FAD diagram, GoA vs GOM comparison\\n- FAQ: \\\"How does AI handle site-specific GoA conditions?\\\" \\u2014 BSEE data integration demo\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nDiffraction workflows + FFS for plates + GoA is a high-value combination for offshore\\nstructural integrity work that is typically very time-intensive (multi-day model setup,\\nmanual code checks). The GoA angle is differentiated \\u2014 most AI demos focus on GoM.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] 3 diffraction templates with AQWA/WAMIT conventions and sample I/O\\n- [ ] 3 plate FFS templates (Part 4/8/9) with worked examples\\n- [ ] 2 GoA-specific calc templates (seismic + metocean) with sample parameters\\n- [ ] Diffraction-to-structural workflow prompt chain documented\\n- [ ] GoA FFS decision workflow documented\\n- [ ] BSEE GoA data query prompts tested\\n- [ ] 4 maritime legal templates created (casualty analysis, statistical context, expert\\n- [ ] Maritime legal decision workflow (7-step) documented with sample I/O\\n- [ ] MAIB/NTSB statistical context prompt validated against `worldenergydata` loaders\\n- [ ] Demo script (15-20 min) includes maritime legal showcase (casualty analysis moment)\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/270\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/269\", \"title\": \"WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base\", \"issue_number\": 269, \"body\": \"## WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** marine\\n\\n**Repo:** ['TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nDay 1 foundation for Client 2 engineering AI demo. Client 2 focus areas:\\n- **Diffraction analysis** \\u2014 wave-structure interaction, RAOs, QTFs, panel model setup\\n- **Fitness for service (FFS) for plates** \\u2014 API 579-1 assessments for plate/shell geometry\\n  (not pipe \\u2014 different remaining strength methodology)\\n- **Gulf of Alaska (GoA) analysis** \\u2014 seismic, extreme metocean, ice loading, environmental\\n- **Maritime legal cases consulting** \\u2014 casualty investigation support, expert witness\\n  technical analysis, MAIB/NTSB/USCG report interpretation, admiralty law interface\\n\\n### 1. System Prompt \\u2014 Client 2 Structural/Offshore Assistant\\n\\nFile: `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/structural_offshore_assistant.md`\\n\\nCore competencies to include:\\n- **Diffraction analysis**: AQWA, WAMIT, OrcaFlex wave interaction; panel model conventions;\\n  RAO extraction and interpretation; QTF for second-order wave loads; wave heading matrices\\n- **FFS for plates/shells**: API 579-1 Part 4 (general metal loss in plate), Part 5 (local LTA),\\n  Part 8 (shell distortions \\u2014 peaking, ovality, buckles), Part 9 (crack-like flaws via FAD),\\n  Part 3 (brittle fracture); remaining strength factor for plate vs pipe distinction\\n- **GoA analysis**: API RP 2EQ seismic, API RP 2MET extreme metocean, ice loading per API RP 2N,\\n  environmental permitting under NEPA/ESA, extreme 100-yr wave/current parameters\\n- Primary codes: API RP 2EQ, API RP 2A-WSD/LRFD, ISO 19902, API 579-1, BS 7910,\\n  API RP 2MET, API RP 2N (Arctic), AISC 360, AWS D1.1\\n\\n### 2. Knowledge Base Files\\n\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/api_579_plate_ffs.md` \\u2014 Part 4/5/8/9 for plates;\\n  key distinction: plate remaining strength uses limit load vs pipe burst pressure\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/diffraction_analysis_reference.md` \\u2014 panel method\\n  theory; AQWA/WAMIT model setup conventions; RAO/QTF interpretation; damping models\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/goa_design_criteria.md` \\u2014 100-yr design parameters;\\n  seismic zones; ice drift/pressure; BSEE GoA lease/permit context; ADEC environmental reqs\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/api_rp_2a_structural.md` \\u2014 tubular joint checks,\\n  member utilisation, fatigue SCFs, in-service inspection intervals\\n\\n### 4. System Prompt \\u2014 Maritime Legal Cases Consultant\\n\\nFile: `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/maritime_legal_consultant.md`\\n\\nCore competencies:\\n- **Casualty investigation**: MAIB (UK), NTSB Marine (US), USCG MISLE incident databases;\\n  root-cause taxonomy (equipment failure, human factors, weather, management system);\\n  ISM Code non-conformity identification; SOLAS Chapter IX compliance review\\n- **Expert witness support**: technical analysis for admiralty proceedings; translating\\n  engineering findings into lay language; report structure for legal proceedings;\\n  probability of causation framing; standards of care (industry vs regulatory)\\n- **Admiralty law interface**: collision regulations (COLREGs); salvage and wreck removal;\\n  limitation of liability (Limitation Act / Jones Act / MLC 2006); cargo damage claims\\n  (Hague-Visby Rules, Hamburg Rules); P&I Club process and club circular interpretation\\n- **USCG / BSEE regulatory**: CFR 46 (vessel inspection), CFR 33 (navigation), OCS safety\\n  regulations; incident notification requirements; MOC (management of change) for maritime\\n- **Incident data analysis**: leverage `worldenergydata.MAIBLoader` + `NTSBMarineLoader`\\n  (WRK-320 done) for statistical incident context; vessel type vs failure mode correlation;\\n  comparable casualty precedents for damages estimation\\n\\nPrimary references: MAIB investigation reports, NTSB marine accident reports, USCG Marine\\nCasualty Reports, ISM Code, SOLAS, MARPOL, COLREGs, MLC 2006, Jones Act (46 USC 30104),\\nLimitation of Shipowners' Liability Act (46 USC 30501-30512)\\n\\n### 5. Knowledge Base Files \\u2014 Maritime Legal\\n\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/maritime_casualty_investigation.md` \\u2014 MAIB/NTSB/USCG\\n  investigation process; ISM Code audit framework; root-cause taxonomy table\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/admiralty_law_reference.md` \\u2014 COLREGs rules summary;\\n  Jones Act key provisions; limitation of liability thresholds; P&I Club claim stages\\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/expert_witness_framework.md` \\u2014 report structure for\\n  legal proceedings; Daubert standard (US) / Civil Evidence Act (UK); how to frame\\n  engineering opinion as standard of care; deposition preparation checklist\\n\\n### 6. Folder Scaffold\\n\\n```\\nai-initiatives-client2/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 prompts/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 structural_offshore_assistant.md\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 maritime_legal_consultant.md\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 knowledge/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api_579_plate_ffs.md\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 diffraction_analysis_reference.md\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 goa_design_criteria.md\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api_rp_2a_structural.md\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 maritime_casualty_investigation.md\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 admiralty_law_reference.md\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 expert_witness_framework.md\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 demo/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 pilot/\\n```\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nClient 2's disciplines are structurally different from Client 1:\\n- Diffraction is a numerical/frequency-domain speciality \\u2014 the AI context files need to carry\\n  the panel model conventions and output format knowledge\\n- Plate FFS follows different methodology than pipe FFS (Part 4/5 uses net-section collapse for\\n  plates, not burst pressure) \\u2014 requires separate knowledge base\\n- GoA context overlaps with Client 1 but adds Arctic/seismic dimension unique to this client\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] System prompt created at `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/structural_offshore_assistant.md`\\n- [ ] 4 knowledge base markdown files created\\n- [ ] Maritime legal system prompt created with MAIB/NTSB/COLREGs/Jones Act coverage\\n- [ ] 3 maritime legal knowledge base files created\\n- [ ] 5 test questions validated per focus area (diffraction, plate FFS, GoA, maritime legal)\\n- [ ] FFS plate vs pipe distinction clearly handled in system prompt\\n- [ ] Expert witness report structure included in maritime prompt\\n- [ ] No client-specific proprietary data \\u2014 public codes/standards only\\n- [ ] `target_repos` updated from TBD to actual client repo when created\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/269\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo \\u2014 diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/272\", \"title\": \"WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit \\u2014 version + clause consistency via Gemini\", \"issue_number\": 272, \"body\": \"## WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit \\u2014 version + clause consistency via Gemini\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['digitalmodel'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\ndigitalmodel implements calculations against 15+ engineering standards\\n(DNV, API, ISO, ABS, BS). Version years and clause numbers are embedded as\\nstring literals and comments throughout the codebase. Inconsistencies cause\\ncalculation errors when a standard is revised.\\n\\nUse Gemini to sweep all engineering modules in one pass and produce a\\nstandards-citation-audit report flagging:\\n1. Conflicting version years for the same standard across modules\\n2. Clause citations that look implausible (wrong section numbering pattern)\\n3. Modules referencing a standard without a version year\\n4. Standards used in multiple modules with different acceptance thresholds\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nEngineering standards evolve; using mixed version years in the same codebase can produce\\ncontradictory acceptance criteria for the same parameter. Gemini's large context makes a\\nsingle-pass audit of 15+ modules practical without losing cross-module context.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] `specs/wrk/WRK-662/standards-citation-audit.md` with all 4 tables populated\\n- [ ] CONFLICT table has \\u2264 5 items OR all conflicts are resolved with inline comments\\n- [ ] MISSING VERSION table has action taken (year added or deferred with rationale)\\n- [ ] Cross-check against standards-transfer-ledger shows \\u226580% of cited standards\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/272\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit \\u2014 version + clause consistency via Gemini\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/470\", \"title\": \"Seakeeping analysis using OpenFOAM \\u2014 CFD-based ship motion simulation\", \"issue_number\": 470, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nLinkedIn post by Belal Sherif on seakeeping simulation using OpenFOAM:\\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/posts/belal-sherif-5a1980243_a-new-seakeeping-simulation-whats-special-share-7442515370885685248-heR3\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd seakeeping analysis capability using OpenFOAM for CFD-based ship/vessel motion simulation in waves. This goes beyond potential-flow BEM solvers (Capytaine, OrcaWave, AQWA) by capturing viscous effects, slamming, green water, and nonlinear wave-body interaction.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### Phase 1 \\u2014 Literature and Method Survey\\n- Review OpenFOAM seakeeping tutorials and published workflows (interDyMFoam, overInterDyMFoam with overset meshes)\\n- Catalog mesh motion strategies: morphing, overset/chimera, 6-DOF rigid body solver\\n- Identify benchmark cases (Wigley hull, DTMB 5415, KCS) with experimental data\\n\\n### Phase 2 \\u2014 Basic Seakeeping Setup\\n- Regular wave generation (Stokes 2nd/5th, stream function) using waveMaker or waves2Foam/olaFlow\\n- Ship hull mesh import from FreeCAD or STL\\n- 6-DOF motion solver coupling (sixDoFRigidBodyMotion)\\n- Heave and pitch RAO extraction in head seas\\n\\n### Phase 3 \\u2014 Advanced Capabilities\\n- Irregular sea state simulations (JONSWAP / PM spectra)\\n- Multi-directional seas, oblique headings (roll, sway, yaw)\\n- Green water / deck wetness detection\\n- Slamming pressure extraction on bow/bottom panels\\n- Added resistance in waves (drift force integration)\\n\\n### Phase 4 \\u2014 Validation and Integration\\n- Benchmark against BEM codes (Capytaine #464, OrcaWave) for linear regime\\n- Compare with model test data where available\\n- Integration with digitalmodel YAML-driven workflow (spec.yml pattern)\\n- ParaView post-processing automation for motion animations\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n\\n- Primary solvers: interDyMFoam (dynamic mesh), overInterDyMFoam (overset)\\n- Wave libraries: olaFlow (preferred, actively maintained), waves2Foam, or built-in waveMaker\\n- Mesh: snappyHexMesh or cfMesh for hull meshing; overset for large-amplitude motions\\n- Related issues: #154 (OpenFOAM deep solver workflows), #139 (OpenFOAM CFD capability), #155 (CAD-to-CFD pipeline), #464 (Capytaine BEM)\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Reproduce at least one published seakeeping benchmark (heave/pitch RAO within 10% of exp data)\\n- [ ] YAML-driven workflow: spec.yml -> mesh -> simulate -> extract RAOs\\n- [ ] Documentation with tutorial walkthrough\\n- [ ] Comparison plot: OpenFOAM CFD vs BEM (Capytaine or OrcaWave) for same hull\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/470\", \"display_title\": \"Seakeeping analysis using OpenFOAM \\u2014 CFD-based ship motion simulation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/463\", \"title\": \"Populate ship-dimensions dataset from ship plans (manual curation follow-on)\", \"issue_number\": 463, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nTrack the remaining manual-curation work after the ship-dimensions template + loader code was completed in `#457`.\\n\\n## Context\\n`#457` delivered the code-side foundation:\\n- default ship-dimensions template loading\\n- stricter vessel-entry validation\\n- registry merge normalization into `ship_data`\\n- naval-architecture package exports\\n- regression tests for default loading, alias handling, and merge normalization\\n\\nThe remaining work is not code scaffolding. It is data population and verification against source materials.\\n\\n## Remaining work\\n1. Use the canonical ship-dimensions template artifact to populate vessel dimensions from the ship-plan PDFs.\\n2. Record the required vessel fields without inventing values.\\n3. Cross-reference against Jane's where available.\\n4. Mark verified entries appropriately.\\n5. Run the relevant validation once the dataset is populated.\\n\\n## Blockers\\n- Blocked by `#461` to recover or replace the missing upstream template artifact from `WRK-1339` Child E.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- canonical template/input path is resolved via `#461`\\n- ship-dimensions dataset is populated with the intended vessel coverage\\n- verified entries are marked from source cross-reference\\n- downstream validation passes on the populated dataset\\n\\n## Notes\\nThis issue intentionally covers the manual/dataset portion only. The template + loader implementation was completed under `#457`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/463\", \"display_title\": \"Populate ship-dimensions dataset from ship plans (manual curation follow-on)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/469\", \"title\": \"Assess AI agent session artifact dirs across machines (.codex, .gemini, .claude/skills)\", \"issue_number\": 469, \"body\": \"## Purpose\\n\\nTrack the per-machine assessment of how AI agent session artifact directories (`.codex/`, `.gemini/`, `.claude/skills/` symlink files) should be handled in the repo. This issue records decisions made on each machine so they can be compared and a consistent policy confirmed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nThree agent ecosystems each write working directories into the repo root:\\n\\n| Dir pattern | Agent | Content |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `.codex/CuXXX/` | Codex | session JSONL, scheduler log, coordination skills snapshot |\\n| `.gemini/CuXXX/` | Gemini | same structure as Codex |\\n| `.claude/skills/{guidelines,meta,workflows}` | Claude | symlink pointer files \\u2192 `workspace-hub/.claude/skills/_internal/` |\\n| `.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated` | Claude | datestamp of last skill propagation |\\n\\nAll three agents share the **same RAG aggregation pipeline**: their session logs are extracted nightly and written to `workspace-hub/.claude/skills/session-logs/aggregated/` (AI explanations TSV, human prompts TSV, tool stats). That aggregated output is the canonical cross-analysis artifact \\u2014 the per-session `CuXXX` dirs are raw source already consumed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Decision Log\\n\\n### Machine: ACMA-ANSYS05 (Windows 11, licensed-win-1) \\u2014 2026-04-02\\n\\n**`.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/`**\\n- **Decision: gitignore** \\u2705\\n- Rationale: Transient per-session working dirs, 50+ accumulated. Raw content already aggregated upstream. No unique value to commit.\\n- Action taken: Added `.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/` to `.gitignore` (commit `e4b1ea6f`, pushed `2c741fc3`).\\n\\n**`.claude/skills/{guidelines,meta,workflows}`**\\n- **Status: OPEN \\u2014 needs assessment**\\n- These are ASCII text files containing relative symlink targets (e.g. `../../../.claude/skills/_internal/guidelines`). They are ecosystem propagation artifacts \\u2014 set by `workspace-hub` propagation on 2026-03-31.\\n- Question: Should these be committed (so other machines get the correct skill pointers on clone), or gitignored (they are regenerated by propagation)?\\n- On this machine they are untracked but not yet gitignored.\\n\\n**`.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated`**\\n- **Status: OPEN \\u2014 needs assessment**\\n- Single-line datestamp file (`20260331`). Acts as a sentinel for the last propagation run.\\n- Question: Commit as state marker, or gitignore as machine-local runtime file?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Questions to Resolve Per Machine\\n\\n1. Are `.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/` already gitignored on your machine, or were they accumulating untracked?\\n2. Do `.claude/skills/guidelines`, `.claude/skills/meta`, `.claude/skills/workflows` exist? Are they symlinks or text pointer files?\\n3. Does `.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated` exist, and what date does it contain?\\n4. Does cloning the repo and running without propagation break anything if the pointer files are absent?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\n- [ ] Assess on remaining licensed machines (ACMA-ANSYS04, etc.)\\n- [ ] Decide: commit `.claude/skills` pointer files vs gitignore + regenerate on clone\\n- [ ] If committing: add to a dedicated `chore(skills):` commit pattern\\n- [ ] If gitignoring: add hook or setup script to regenerate on clone/pull\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/469\", \"display_title\": \"Assess AI agent session artifact dirs across machines (.codex, .gemini, .claude/skills)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/467\", \"title\": \"Subsea structure installation analysis \\u2014 vessel performance and real-time motion feedback\", \"issue_number\": 467, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nEnable rapid assessment of subsea structure installation feasibility across varying structure dimensions, water depths, and installation vessels \\u2014 then extend to real-time operational decision support.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### Phase 1: Installation Analysis Engine\\n- Parametric analysis: structure length \\u00d7 water depth \\u00d7 vessel type matrix\\n- Crane tip motion and hook load dynamics from vessel RAOs\\n- Lowering/lifting through splash zone assessment (DNV-RP-H103 \\u00a74)\\n- Weather window estimation from operability limits\\n- Quick-assess mode: screen multiple vessels against a given structure\\n\\n### Phase 2: Multi-Vessel Comparison\\n- Standardized vessel database with crane capacity curves and RAO libraries\\n- Side-by-side vessel comparison for a given installation task\\n- Cost-weighted operability ranking\\n- Sensitivity to heading, water depth, and wave period\\n\\n### Phase 3: Real-Time Motion Feedback\\n- Hook up measured vessel motions (MRU/IMU data feed)\\n- Compare real-time motions against allowable criteria\\n- Go/no-go decision support dashboard\\n- Alarm thresholds tied to installation phase (lift-off, splash zone, landing)\\n- Record and replay for post-operation review\\n\\n## Standards\\n\\n- DNV-RP-H103 (Modelling and Analysis of Marine Operations)\\n- DNV-ST-N001 (Marine Operations and Marine Warranty)\\n- DNV-RP-C205 \\u00a77 (hydrodynamic coefficients for vessel response)\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Capytaine module (#464) or existing AQWA/OrcaWave RAO libraries\\n- Marine ops module (`src/digitalmodel/marine_ops/`)\\n- Signal processing module (`src/digitalmodel/signal_processing/`) for MRU data\\n- Visualization module for dashboard/real-time display\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/467\", \"display_title\": \"Subsea structure installation analysis \\u2014 vessel performance and real-time motion feedback\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/466\", \"title\": \"Parametric hull analysis \\u2014 steady speed, passing ship, narrow water environments\", \"issue_number\": 466, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nExtend the hydrodynamics module with parametric hull analysis capabilities for real-world operational scenarios in restricted waterways.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### 1. Parametric Hull Analysis\\n- Systematic variation of hull form parameters (beam, draft, block coefficient, waterplane area)\\n- Added mass and damping sensitivity to hull geometry\\n- Automated sweep across hull variants with result comparison\\n\\n### 2. Steady Speed (Forward Speed) Analysis\\n- BEM analysis with forward speed effects on wave-body interaction\\n- Speed-dependent added mass and damping corrections\\n- Wave resistance estimation at operational speeds\\n- DNV-RP-C205 \\u00a77.4 forward speed corrections\\n\\n### 3. Passing Ship Analysis\\n- Multi-body hydrodynamic interaction between passing vessels\\n- Suction forces and moments as function of separation distance, speed, and relative heading\\n- Time-domain force histories for moored vessel response\\n- Leverages existing `src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/passing_ship/` module\\n\\n### 4. Narrow/Shallow Water Effects\\n- Finite depth corrections for restricted waterways (DNV-RP-C205 \\u00a73.5)\\n- Bank effects and channel confinement on hydrodynamic coefficients\\n- Speed-dependent squat and trim in shallow water\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n- Vessel operator charts: parametric plots showing operational limits per vessel type\\n- Comparison tables across vessel variants for given environmental conditions\\n- Integration with Capytaine BEM module (#464) for open-source solver path\\n\\n## Standards\\n\\n- DNV-RP-C205 \\u00a73.5 (shallow water), \\u00a77.4 (forward speed)\\n- PIANC guidelines for ship-ship interaction in confined waterways\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Capytaine module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/capytaine/`) \\u2014 #464\\n- Passing ship module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/passing_ship/`)\\n- Hull library (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/hull_library/`)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/466\", \"display_title\": \"Parametric hull analysis \\u2014 steady speed, passing ship, narrow water environments\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/465\", \"title\": \"Capytaine ship hull benchmarking \\u2014 OC4 semi-sub + WAMIT validation\", \"issue_number\": 465, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nThe Capytaine BEM module (#464) is implemented with a sphere analytical benchmark (Hulme 1982). Ship hull validation is the logical next step to establish confidence for production use.\\n\\n## Available data in repo\\n\\n- **OC4 Semi-sub**: geometry mesh (`docs/domains/orcawave/examples/L02 OC4 Semi-sub/`) + full specification (mass 13.473M kg, CoG, inertia, water depth 200m)\\n- **WAMIT validation cases**: 12 cases in `docs/domains/orcawave/L00_validation_wamit/` (cylinder, box, ISSC TLP, multi-body) with reference `.dat` files\\n- **Unit box benchmark**: synthetic 3-way comparison (AQWA, OrcaWave, BEMRosetta) in `docs/benchmarks/unit_box/`\\n- **WAMIT reference loader**: existing infrastructure at `src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/diffraction/wamit_reference_loader.py`\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. **OC4 semi-sub benchmark**: load GDF mesh \\u2192 Capytaine solve \\u2192 compare RAOs against WAMIT/OrcaWave reference\\n2. **WAMIT cylinder validation** (case 2.1): compare added mass/damping against WAMIT reference data\\n3. **Cross-solver comparison plots**: Capytaine vs existing AQWA/OrcaWave results for shared geometries\\n4. **Tolerance criteria**: define pass/fail thresholds per DNV-RP-C205 guidance\\n\\n## Standards\\n\\n- DNV-RP-C205 \\u00a77.1 (potential flow validation)\\n- IEA Wind OC4 project (semi-submersible reference)\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Capytaine module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/capytaine/`) \\u2014 done in #464\\n- Capytaine env at `/mnt/local-analysis/capytaine-env`\\n- WAMIT reference loader for ground truth extraction\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/465\", \"display_title\": \"Capytaine ship hull benchmarking \\u2014 OC4 semi-sub + WAMIT validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/464\", \"title\": \"Add hydrodynamic BEM analysis module (Capytaine)\", \"issue_number\": 464, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdd wave-body interaction analysis to digitalmodel using Capytaine BEM solver \\u2014 diffraction, radiation, added mass, damping coefficients, and RAOs for floating/submerged bodies.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n- Capytaine 2.3.1 installed and verified on dev-secondary (2026-03-26)\\n- Env: `/mnt/local-analysis/capytaine-env` (Python 3.12, scipy, numpy, vtk, meshio, xarray, matplotlib)\\n- Sphere diffraction test passing \\u2014 solver fully functional\\n- Backlog item 999.2 in workspace-hub ROADMAP.md\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n- digitalmodel adapter: mesh import (meshio/STL/GDF formats), problem setup, result extraction\\n- Standard calculations: diffraction forces, radiation coefficients (added mass + damping), RAOs\\n- Validation against known benchmarks (OC3/OC4 spar, semi-sub, barge)\\n- Standards traceability: DNV-RP-C205 (environmental conditions and loads)\\n- Result export: xarray datasets, plots, summary tables\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Consider Capytaine's Hierarchical Toeplitz matrices for large meshes\\n- dev-secondary has OpenMP + NVIDIA T400 for parallelism\\n- Follow digitalmodel calculation module pattern established in Phase 01 (manifest schema, CI validation)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/464\", \"display_title\": \"Add hydrodynamic BEM analysis module (Capytaine)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/461\", \"title\": \"Recover ship-dimensions template artifact from WRK-1339 Child E\", \"issue_number\": 461, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nRecover or deliberately replace the missing Child E deliverable from `WRK-1339` so downstream ship-dimensions work can proceed inside `workspace-hub` without guessing schema or output paths.\\n\\n## Why\\n`WRK-1380` is currently blocked because the expected upstream artifact is absent from the local `workspace-hub` checkout. Local recovery checked:\\n- current `workspace-hub` files\\n- `WRK-1339` asset folder\\n- repo history\\n- nearby sibling/child WRKs\\n- existing GitHub issue discussion\\n\\nNone of those produced:\\n- `generate-ship-dimension-template.py`, or\\n- a generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n1. Confirm whether `WRK-1339` ever produced either:\\n   - `generate-ship-dimension-template.py`, or\\n   - a generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\\n2. If the artifact exists outside the current checkout, import it into the canonical `workspace-hub` location.\\n3. If the artifact does not exist anywhere, define and create the replacement deliverable explicitly.\\n4. Record the canonical path for:\\n   - the generator or replacement script\\n   - the generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\\n5. Update downstream WRKs, especially `WRK-1380`, with the resolved paths.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- a canonical ship-dimensions template source exists in `workspace-hub`\\n- the canonical output path for `ship-dimensions.yaml` is documented\\n- `WRK-1380` can reference concrete local paths instead of unresolved blockers\\n- no schema keys or output paths are invented ad hoc downstream\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/461\", \"display_title\": \"Recover ship-dimensions template artifact from WRK-1339 Child E\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation","issue_number":2269,"body":"## Summary\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\n\nPart of #1782.\nPrimary reference: #25.\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\n\n## Motivation\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\n\n## Scope\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\n\nExpected deliverables:\n- baseline docs\n- run/validation entrypoints\n- minimal smoke example\n- troubleshooting guidance\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\n\n## Notes\nImplementation should prefer:\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","display_title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)","issue_number":2402,"body":"## Context\n\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR×2 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\n\n## Problem\n\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model §7 — **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model §3).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per §3 — enforced and tested\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s — measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\n\n## Scope boundaries\n\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) — live in their own issues.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","display_title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962","title":"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring — audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode","issue_number":1962,"body":"## Summary\n\nSystematic refactoring of the workspace-hub repo ecosystem, starting with tier-1 repositories. The goal is to reduce architectural debt, consolidate duplicate patterns, enforce consistent structure, and improve agent navigability across all tier-1 repos.\n\n## Tier-1 Repos (Priority Order)\n\n| # | Repo | Purpose | Maturity | Depends On |\n|---|------|---------|----------|------------|\n| 1 | `digitalmodel/` | Engineering digital twin (asset integrity, CP, GIS, hydro) | beta | assetutilities |\n| 2 | `assetutilities/` | Shared engineering utilities (config, units, calculations) | stable | — |\n| 3 | `assethold/` | Asset portfolio financial analysis | beta | assetutilities |\n| 4 | `worldenergydata/` | Global energy market data (BSEE, EIA, drilling) | beta | assetutilities |\n| 5 | `CAD-DEVELOPMENTS/` | CAD solvers, models, database, utilities | beta | — |\n| 6 | `aceengineer-website/` | Consulting website | — | — |\n| 7 | `aceengineer-strategy/` | GTM, business strategy | — | — |\n| 8 | `sabithaandkrishnaestates/` | SKEstates Inc. business ops | — | — |\n\n## Refactoring Scope\n\n### Phase 1: Audit (analysis-only, no code changes)\n- [ ] Run `repo-architecture-analysis` on each tier-1 repo\n- [ ] Identify cross-repo duplicate code (especially assetutilities consumers)\n- [ ] Map dependency graph (imports, shared configs, data flows)\n- [ ] Catalog test coverage per repo (current state)\n- [ ] Identify orphaned/dead code, unused modules, oversized files (>400 lines)\n- [ ] Score each repo against the Control-Plane Contract (AGENTS.md, provider adapters)\n- [ ] Identify skill duplicates across repos (134 known from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 audit)\n\n### Phase 2: Plan (per-repo refactor plans)\n- [ ] Generate refactor plan per tier-1 repo with estimated effort\n- [ ] Prioritize by: business value × technical debt severity × dependency impact\n- [ ] Identify breaking changes and migration paths\n- [ ] Define test coverage targets (tier-1 = 85% per pytest.tier1.ini)\n\n### Phase 3: Execute (TDD, incremental, per-repo)\n- [ ] Execute refactors repo-by-repo following dependency order (assetutilities first)\n- [ ] TDD mandatory — tests before implementation\n- [ ] Each repo refactor as a separate sub-issue for tracking\n\n## Execution Strategy: Claude Code Plan Mode (Cloud)\n\n### Claude Code `--permission-mode plan` (\"Ultraplan\")\n\nClaude Code v2.1.92 supports `--permission-mode plan` which restricts the agent to **read-only analysis and planning** — no file writes, no shell mutations. This is ideal for Phase 1 (Audit) and Phase 2 (Plan).\n\n**Proposed execution:**\n\n```bash\n# Phase 1: Audit each tier-1 repo in plan mode (safe, read-only)\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\n  --print \\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\n  -p \"Audit the repository architecture of digitalmodel/. Analyze: module structure, dependency graph, test coverage, dead code, file sizes >400 lines, AGENTS.md compliance. Output a structured JSON report.\"\n\n# Phase 2: Generate refactor plan\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\n  --print \\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\n  -p \"Given the audit report, generate a prioritized refactor plan for digitalmodel/. Include: breaking changes, migration steps, test targets, estimated effort per module.\"\n```\n\n### Cloud Execution Considerations\n\n| Aspect | Status | Notes |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| **Claude Code CLI** | Installed (v2.1.92) | Available on ace-linux-1 |\n| **Plan mode** | Supported | `--permission-mode plan` — read-only, safe for audit |\n| **API-key mode** | Supported | `--bare` + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for headless/cloud runs |\n| **Print mode** | Supported | `-p` / `--print` for non-interactive batch execution |\n| **Budget cap** | Supported | `--max-budget-usd` to control spend per run |\n| **Cloud sandbox** | Possible | Can run via Hermes `delegate_task` with `acp_command='claude'` |\n| **Max subscription** | Claude Max $200/mo | Rate-limited but sufficient for plan-mode audit |\n\n### Recommended Approach\n1. **Phase 1 + 2 (Audit + Plan)**: Run Claude Code in plan mode via `delegate_task(acp_command='claude')` — subagents get isolated context, read-only, budget-capped\n2. **Phase 3 (Execute)**: Requires interactive Claude Code sessions with full permissions — NOT suited for autonomous cloud execution without user oversight\n\n## Adversarial Review Requirements\n\nPer [AI Review Routing Policy](docs/standards/AI_REVIEW_ROUTING_POLICY.md):\n\n- **3-agent adversarial review at BOTH stages** (plan + code/artifact)\n- Claude: orchestrator + reviewer\n- Codex: implementation worker + adversarial reviewer\n- Gemini: architecture reviewer + adversarial reviewer\n- Max 3 review iterations per deliverable\n- All MAJOR findings must be resolved before completion\n\n### Review Checkpoints\n1. **After Phase 1 (Audit)**: All 3 agents review the audit findings\n2. **After Phase 2 (Plan)**: All 3 agents review each repo's refactor plan\n3. **After Phase 3 (Execute)**: All 3 agents review code changes per repo\n\n## Related Issues\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1567 — Feature: Continuous Repo Architecture Intelligence\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1545 — Agentic feature progression for repo ecosystem productivity under GSD\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1603 — Multi-repo architecture scan — expand scanner to all tier-1 repos\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 — Cross-agent session corpus audit (134 duplicate skills identified)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1734 — chore: add domain skills to assethold (tier-1 with 0 skills)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1661 — Architecture scanner: dependency cycle detection and layering violations\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#113 — ROADMAP: Repo ecosystem 3-6 month horizon\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Audit report generated for each tier-1 repo\n- [ ] Refactor plan per repo reviewed and approved by all 3 agents\n- [ ] Phase 3 sub-issues created with clear scope per repo\n- [ ] Test coverage meets tier-1 target (85%) after refactoring\n- [ ] Zero cross-repo duplicate skills remaining\n- [ ] All repos score 100% on Control-Plane Contract compliance\n- [ ] Dependency graph documented and validated\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962","display_title":"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring — audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/596","title":"chore(repo-structure): normalize digitalmodel folder/file structure","issue_number":596,"body":"## Summary\n\nRepo-specific planning issue for normalizing `digitalmodel` folder/file structure as the first repo in the tier-1 repo-by-repo refactor wave.\n\nThis child issue is anchored to:\n- Parent umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1962\n- Folder-structure contract epic: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2397\n- Inventory evidence: `workspace-hub/docs/reports/2026-05-07-tier1-folder-structure-inventory.md`\n\n## Why digitalmodel first\n\n`digitalmodel` is the first repo in the approved tier-1 refactor priority order from workspace-hub#1962. Current live inventory shows it is:\n\n- on `main`\n- `0` commits ahead / `0` behind upstream\n- no tracked dirty files\n- already has the canonical high-level paths: `.claude`, `.github`, `config`, `docs`, `scripts`, `src`, `tests`\n\nThat makes it a low-risk first candidate for a repo-specific structure plan before moving to dependency-critical or dirty repos.\n\n## Initial inventory signals\n\nObserved root/structure drift candidates from 2026-05-07 inventory:\n\n- generated/output candidates: `benchmark_output`, `build`, `cache`, `dist`, `logs`, `outputs`, `results`, `site`, `test_output_ss`\n- developer/runtime state candidates: `.benchmarks`, `.hypothesis`, `.mypy_cache`, `.pytest_cache`, `.ruff_cache`, `.swarm`\n- root generated files: `coverage.json`, `coverage.xml`, `coverage.wrk149.focused.xml`, `coverage.wrk149.priority.xml`\n- domain/product dirs that require classification rather than blind moves: `benchmarks`, `memory`, `notebooks`, `projects`, `reports`, `specs`\n\nNo implementation is authorized by this issue alone.\n\n## Required workflow\n\nFollow workspace-hub issue-planning mode:\n\n1. Resource intelligence before plan drafting:\n   - read `digitalmodel/AGENTS.md`\n   - inspect `docs/README.md`, routing maps, `pyproject.toml`, `.gitignore`, CI workflows, and test layout\n   - classify generated artifacts vs durable report fixtures vs domain assets\n2. Draft a plan in the appropriate `docs/plans/` location with:\n   - Artifact Map\n   - path-level migration matrix\n   - safe-rename vs breaking-path migration classification\n   - TDD/verification list\n   - explicit approval gate\n3. Run adversarial plan review.\n4. Move to `status:plan-review` only after review artifacts exist.\n5. Wait for user approval (`status:plan-approved` + local approval marker) before implementation.\n6. Execute with TDD/verification and transactional closeout.\n\n## Acceptance criteria for the plan stage\n\n- [ ] Plan inventories digitalmodel top-level folders and root files with classifications.\n- [ ] Plan separates generated artifacts, durable reports/fixtures, docs, scripts/tools, package source, tests, and domain assets.\n- [ ] Plan identifies which moves are safe housekeeping and which are breaking path migrations.\n- [ ] Plan includes tests/checks for import stability, docs links/stale paths, `.gitignore` boundaries, and representative repo smoke tests.\n- [ ] Plan explicitly states what will **not** be moved in the first implementation pass.\n- [ ] No implementation occurs before user approval.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/596","display_title":"chore(repo-structure): normalize digitalmodel folder/file structure"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657","title":"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift","issue_number":2657,"body":"## Summary\n\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\n\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\n\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\n\nReads:\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\n- `github.github-issues`\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\n\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\n\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\n\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\n\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657","display_title":"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656","title":"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure","issue_number":2656,"body":"## Objective\n\nPlan a conservative, repo-by-repo folder/file structure normalization for `workspace-hub` under the workspace-hub tier-1 ecosystem workflow.\n\n## Scope\n\nPlanning only until explicit user approval. The plan must inventory current structure, identify root clutter/generated-output risk, propose a bounded Phase 1 refactor contract, define TDD/verification gates, and preserve evidence needed for rollback.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Canonical plan artifact under `docs/plans/`.\n- Review artifact under `scripts/review/results/`.\n- Final issue comment linking the plan and review artifact.\n\n## Approval Gate\n\nNo file moves, package reorganization, deletion, or cleanup execution is authorized until this issue is explicitly approved after plan review.\n\nParent ecosystem anchors: `workspace-hub#1962`, `workspace-hub#2397`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656","display_title":"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/278","title":"Restore broken modules.* compatibility shims after bsee and marine_safety consolidation","issue_number":278,"body":"Summary\nThe recent consolidation of `modules/bsee` and `modules/marine_safety` claims backward-compatible re-exports, but the current package surface is broken.\n\nEvidence\n- Recent consolidation removed legacy files while leaving package `__init__.py` files importing deleted submodules\n- Examples observed during review:\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/bsee/analysis/type_curves/__init__.py` imports modules that no longer exist\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/importers/__init__.py` imports deleted importer modules\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/analysis/incidents/__init__.py` imports deleted analysis modules\n  - `src/worldenergydata/modules/marine_safety/processors/__init__.py` imports deleted processor modules\n- Focused regression reproduced with:\n  - `PYTHONPATH='src:../assetutilities/src' uv run pytest tests/modules/bsee/analysis/test_type_curves.py -q`\n  - collection fails because the old import surface is gone/broken\n\nWhy this is risky\n- This is a real compatibility break, not just cleanup noise\n- Legacy imports used by tests/scripts/examples now fail at import time\n- The commit message promises backward compatibility that the code does not provide\n\nRecommended fix\n- Restore shim modules for deleted paths or update all package re-exports and downstream imports atomically\n- Add explicit compatibility tests for promised legacy import paths before removing old modules\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- Legacy import paths used by current tests/scripts import successfully or are fully migrated\n- Compatibility expectations are encoded in tests\n- Package `__init__.py` files no longer import deleted modules\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/worldenergydata/issues/278","display_title":"Restore broken modules.* compatibility shims after bsee and marine_safety consolidation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/559","title":"fix(marine_ops): test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation — strict-greater on equal floats (use >=)","issue_number":559,"body":"Sub-issue of [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609) cluster R6 (heterogeneous OCIMF/RAO/integration). Individual-test issue per user direction to maintain visibility (\"9 individual issues to help keep gap\").\n\n## Test nodeid\n`tests/marine_ops/marine_engineering/integration/test_hydro_rao_integration.py::TestHydroRAOIntegration::test_full_matrix_interpolation`\n\n## Top error (verbatim from triage plan)\n> `Added mass should be diagonally dominant at (3,1)`: `assert 624146.29 > 624146.29` (strict-greater on equal floats — should be `>=`).\n\n## Implicated source\n- Test: `tests/marine_ops/marine_engineering/integration/test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation` — assertion uses `>` where it should use `>=` (or include a tolerance).\n\n## Hypothesis\n**(b) test fix** — strict-greater-than against arithmetically equal floats. Replace `>` with `>=` (or `pytest.approx`) for diagonal-dominance check. Low-risk single-line edit per triage plan recommendation (see `docs/plans/2026-05-03-2609-marine-ops-triage.md` open question 5).\n\n## Acceptance\n- This single test will pass at digitalmodel HEAD with no `--maxfail`-induced cascade.\n- No regression in sibling `test_hydro_rao_integration.py` tests.\n\n## Reference\n- Triage plan: `docs/plans/2026-05-03-2609-marine-ops-triage.md` (cluster R6, sub-defect 4)\n- Parent: [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609)\n- Sister sub-issues from Lanes b + c: see [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2609](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2609) for siblings.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/559","display_title":"fix(marine_ops): test_hydro_rao_integration.py::test_full_matrix_interpolation — strict-greater on equal floats (use >=)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion","issue_number":26,"body":"## Summary\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\n\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\n\n## Scope\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\n- Explicitly exclude:\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\n\n## Deliverables\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains","issue_number":25,"body":"## Summary\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\n\n## Why\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\n\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\n\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\n\n## Scope\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\n\n## Deliverables\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/72","title":"Cleanup: resolve merge markers blocking editable install and downstream pytest","issue_number":72,"body":"## Summary\n\n`assetutilities` currently contains unresolved merge markers in:\n\n- `pyproject.toml`\n- `src/assetutilities/common/update_deep.py`\n\nThis breaks downstream workflows, including:\n\n- `uv` metadata generation for editable dependency `assetutilities`\n- `digitalmodel` commands such as `PYTHONPATH=src uv run python -m pytest tests/solvers/calculix/test_fem_chain.py`\n- direct `pytest` startup in `digitalmodel`, because importing `assetutilities.common.update_deep` raises a `SyntaxError`\n\n## Trigger\n\nDiscovered while validating `vamseeachanta/digitalmodel#460`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Remove merge markers from `pyproject.toml`\n- [ ] Remove merge markers from `src/assetutilities/common/update_deep.py`\n- [ ] `uv` can resolve editable `assetutilities` successfully\n- [ ] downstream `digitalmodel` targeted pytest startup succeeds past import / metadata initialization\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/72","display_title":"Cleanup: resolve merge markers blocking editable install and downstream pytest"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data","issue_number":19,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\n\n## Context\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\n\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` — 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` — 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` — 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\n\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\n\n## Problem\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\n\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\n\n## Scope\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\n\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements","issue_number":14,"body":"## Summary\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\n\n## Source of record\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\n\n## Why\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope:\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\n\nOut of scope:\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\n- No source/staging cleanup.\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\n\n## Related\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/58","title":"YAML Plotting","issue_number":58,"body":"placeholder for yml plots","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/58","display_title":"YAML Plotting"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/56","title":"productivity | Meetings","issue_number":56,"body":"- [ ] Develop an AI tool for meetings, recognizing voice  and giving summary out of it ","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/56","display_title":"productivity | Meetings"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/52","title":"YAML file split","issue_number":52,"body":"- [x] create individual function for ruamel as module\n- [x] refactor save yml files\n- [x] make an X-Y plot out of 2 arrays in the yml file using our visualization template\n\n- [x] Install program. https://www.orcina.com/orcaflex/demo/\n  - [ ] Automate the opening or otherwise of the OrcaFlex .yml  test.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/52","display_title":"YAML file split"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/42","title":"productivity | PB Hardware and Utility Readiness","issue_number":42,"body":"- [ ] clone client project, https://github.com/vamseeachanta/seanation\n- [ ] Install programs\n  - [x] Github account (login and comment) (PB)\n    - [x] working seamlessly \n    - [x] explore github digitalmodel online . https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel\n  - [x] Autocad (license)\n  - [x] FreeCAD\n  - [ ] Git (PB)\n    - [x] Install git from link here. https://git-scm.com/ (PB)\n    - [ ] set-up daily commit cycle using git-bash (VA)\n\n\n- [ ] Hardware\n  - [ ] Blender (not compatible). Remote access to windows/Linux? (VA)\n  - [x] Get earphones (PB)\n\n- [x] Learn Google Meet\n  - [x] Schedule 4 meetings independently\n\n  - [ ] Miniconda Python\n    - [x] Install python https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/install/ (PB)\n    - [ ] Further work to be assigned (VA)\n\n  - [x] install notepad++. https://notepad-plus-plus.org/downloads/\n  - [x] install VSCOde. https://code.visualstudio.com/\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/42","display_title":"productivity | PB Hardware and Utility Readiness"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/40","title":" productivity | Marketing","issue_number":40,"body":"- [ ] Actively manage LinkedIn and X \n- [ ] website simplification and revamp for AceEngineer \n\r\n\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/40","display_title":" productivity | Marketing"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/39","title":"productivity | email clean up","issue_number":39,"body":"- [x] email is not for storage\n- [x] method or script to clean up \n  - [x] emails with starred & important should reside forever\n  - [x] other emails not important and older than 365 days (n days) should be deleted\n  - [x] reduce or eliminate spam over time\n\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/39","display_title":"productivity | email clean up"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/38","title":"productivity | Knowledge Management","issue_number":38,"body":"- [ ] Read obsidian resources provided by Siva\n  - [ ] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cBm95iCcX2E\n  - [ ] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nJ660t5ku9A\n  - [ ] other?\n- [ ] Install required packages across machines\n- [ ] tba","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/38","display_title":"productivity | Knowledge Management"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/37","title":"Scalability | Process, People","issue_number":37,"body":"- [ ] Sales\r\n  - [ ] ?\r\n- [ ] Process\r\n- [ ] Enhance productivity\r\n  - [ ] Samdan - ? \r\n  - [ ] Prasad - ?\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/37","display_title":"Scalability | Process, People"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/36","title":"productivity | Consolidate hardware","issue_number":36,"body":"- [ ] setup linux machine\n  - [x] Advanced graphics card\n  - [ ] sound card seem to exist via graphics card\n  - [ ] setup smb for 8 TB drive\n  - [ ] double monitor for Linux machine\n  - [ ] remote login for india employees\n    - [ ] XSERVER for source \n    - [ ] XClient for target \n  - [ ] ACMA remote login on Linux machine?\n- [ ] USB-C sound card for 2nd computer for ACMA meetings?\n- [ ] wired internet \n  - [ ] if outages are frequeny, explore options\n  - [ ] tba\n- [x] KVM - functional\n  - observations:\n    - Single monitor set-up for 3 PCs (2 windows and linux) \n    - 1 keyboard & mouse combo working seamlessly\n    - wired remote handy to change\n    - double monitor requires twice the wires  (Not setup due to graphics card limitation on 2 other PCs)\n  - 3 PCs input\n  - 1 keyboard, 1 mouse input\n  - 1 monitor output\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/36","display_title":"productivity | Consolidate hardware"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/35","title":"productivity | Consolidate repos","issue_number":35,"body":"- [ ] Repo management\r\n  - [ ] Remove/Consolidate stale repos\r\n  - [ ] Issues only in select repos i.e. digitalmodel, aceengineer_admin, assetutilities\r\n  - [ ] No stale branches in repos\r\n- [ ] Remove/Consolidate following repos:\r\n  - [x] energy Public\r\n  - [ ] energydata Public\r\n  - [ ] teamresumes Public\r\n  - [ ] acma-projects Private\r\n  - [ ] assetutilities Public\r\n  - [ ] achantas-data Private\r\n  - [ ] digitalmodel Public\r\n  - [ ] doris Private\r\n  - [ ] aceengineer-admin Private\r\n  - [ ] client_projects\r\n  - [ ] achantas-media Private\r\n  - [x] saipem Private\r\n  - [x] investments Private\r\n  - [x] rock-oil-field Private\r\n  - [x] py_package Public\r\n  - [ ] hobbies Public\r\n  - [x] spire_projects Private\r\n  - [x] hairbyliz Public\r\n  - [x] ecs Private\r\n  - [x] structuralstrength Public\r\n  - [x] pipecapacity Public\r\n  - [x] pyintegrity Public\r\n  - [x] predyct Private\r\n  - [x] petrope Private\r\n  - [x] leveraged-multi-family-analysis Public\r\n  - [x] digitaltwinfeed Private\r\n  - [x] probabilisticrisk Public\r\n  - [x] OGManufacturing Private\r\n  - [ ] sd-work Private\r\n  - [ ] achantas Private\r\n  - [x] aceengineer-website Private\r\n  - [x] aceengineercode Public\r\n  - [x] pymvil Public\r\n  - [x] python_react_postgresql Private\r\n  - [x] amgsharepointcontents Public\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/35","display_title":"productivity | Consolidate repos"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/33","title":"productivity | Consolidate data","issue_number":33,"body":"- [ ] setup linux machine\r\n  - [ ] ?\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/33","display_title":"productivity | Consolidate data"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/31","title":"tech debt | ACMA | Source Files | Sync vs. Copy","issue_number":31,"body":"Objective: \r\n- [ ] Determine the best way from one of methods below and implement in ACMA WLNG project\r\n- [ ] Prepare boiler plate code for ignoring at folder level not file level\r\n\r\nMethod 1 (Ideal):\r\n- Run and sync in same location\r\n- explicit definition using git ignore at folder level\r\n- sync folders should be clear upfront for project or client.\r\n\r\nMethod 2: Separate Location, Copy relevant\r\n- Run in run_location\r\n- sync in sync_location\r\n- Have a batch to copy relevant files from run_location to sync_location\r\n\r\nMethod 3: Another method?\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/31","display_title":"tech debt | ACMA | Source Files | Sync vs. Copy"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30","title":"tech debt | AI agents","issue_number":30,"body":"Objective:\r\n- Utilize AI agents in day to day work to help with code\r\n- Interface AI agent configurations with copilot (?)\r\n- Develop ecosystem for this purpose\r\n\r\n- [x] Define AI agents\r\n- [ ] Write yml files for ai agents.\r\n  - [x] prelim by AI. see prelim file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/202501/_coding_agents/multi_agent.yaml\r\n  - [ ] visionaries (steve jobs, etc.) (VA)\r\n  - [x] python programmer (SS)\r\n    - [ ] Write a test any time a program fails (manual)\r\n    - [ ] Simplify input file preparation (parametric - less scope of mistakes and more for AI to prepare the files)\r\n    - [ ] Think of and think like AI agents in all the work.\r\n    - [ ] consistent variable or file naming\r\n  - [x] devops ci-cd  (SS)\r\n  - [ ] engineer physics (VA)\r\n  - [ ] engineer finance (VA)\r\n  - [ ] continual improvement using AI. Refer to our repositories and our own work and the corrections we made to the work.  (VA)\r\n- [ ] Prompt templates (.yaml)\r\n- [ ] Transfer work to other libraries\r\n  - [ ] assetutilities (all ai work will be here)\r\n  - [ ] determine best method to transfer to other libraries seamlessly \r\n  - [ ] digitalmodel\r\n  - [ ] energydata etc.\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30","display_title":"tech debt | AI agents"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/19","title":"tech debt | git | branch, computer and multiuser merge","issue_number":19,"body":"Objective:\n- Repo developers will have a daily (1 hr) gitbash script that will execute automatically.\n- Test requirements: New code (by any user in any computer) should not fail existing tests in master.\n  - If any tests fail, the team should know at earliest\n -  at merge, run unit and integration tests\n- Branch management\n  - Current branch\n    - name: $YYYY$MM\n    - Branch on cloud and PR created\n  - Stale branches\n    - No branches other than $YYYY$MM\n    - $YYYY$(MM-1) should be pushed to remote\n \n- [ ] Prerequisite: \n  - [ ] develop AI agents: python programmer, ci-cd engineer. see https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/30\n  - [ ] gitbash knowledge across team (running, simple scripting guidance)\n- [ ] implementation strategy\n  - [ ] scripts in gitbash. see evolving notes: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/fce0e9596fbe7f8419edcac0c638308f690ca3af/docs/sub_shell/gitbash.md\n  - [ ] conscious choice of script execution: local vs. github command server vs. other?\n- [ ] branch management\n  - [x] name convention: YYYYMM\n  - [ ] merge at start of month\n  - [ ] remove all stale branches in all repos\n  - [ ] daily script to create report\n    - [x] check local and remote branches. Suggest to consolidate them\n    - [x] check correct branch\n    - [ ] if unexisting, create new one and push to remote?\n    - [ ] end of month actions?\n- [ ] commit - name\n- [ ] commit prehooks\n\n- [ ] assetutilities\n  - [x] No stale branches. \n    - [x] delete 2024 branch\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] digitalmodel\n  - [x] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] teamresumes\n  - [x] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] energydata\n  - [x] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] assethold\n  - [x] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] energy\n  - [ ] No stale branches\n  - [ ] relocate documentation\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] acma-projects\n  - [x] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] achantasdata\n  - [ ] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] achantasmedia\n  - [ ] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n\n- [ ] aceengineer-admin\n  - [ ] No stale branches\n  - [ ] create new branch on 1st day of month\n  - [ ] Run tests at merge - 2 days and inform contributers \n  - [ ] merge at end of month\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/19","display_title":"tech debt | git | branch, computer and multiuser merge"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/60","title":"repo | package development","issue_number":60,"body":"- [ ] develop git bash scripts to manage package uploads to PyPI for all repo's. \n- [ ] Migrate to GitHub Actions (Twine under the hood) over time\n  - [ ] https://www.caktusgroup.com/blog/2021/02/11/automating-pypi-releases/\n  - [ ] https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/publishing-package-distribution-releases-using-github-actions-ci-cd-workflows/\n  - [ ] Learn how to manage secrets to upload to pypi\n- [ ] Create pypi tokens for repo\n  - [ ] https://pypi.org/help/#apitoken","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/60","display_title":"repo | package development"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/59","title":"yaml_utilities | Variable Definition","issue_number":59,"body":"Objective: establish the best way to define variables in YAML files to identify the following scenarios\n\n- [ ] incorporate the logic in our repos. ( together ) , see image below \n- [x] YAML single variable and directive block\n  - [x] Refer : https://docs.geoserver.org/2.21.x/en/user/styling/ysld/reference/variables.html\n  - [x] Example yaml file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/3ba6d9bff20957d4659ad7beed6727404a55014f/tests/modules/yaml_utlities/yml/variables/variable_example_1.yml\n  - [x] test the code for both single and block variables\n\n- [x] YAML placeholders\n  - [x] Refer : https://stackoverflow.com/questions/41620674/use-placeholders-in-yaml\n  - [x] Example yaml file: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/3ba6d9bff20957d4659ad7beed6727404a55014f/tests/modules/yaml_utlities/yml/variables/variable_example_2.yml\n  - [x] Test code for yml placeholder in python","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/59","display_title":"yaml_utilities | Variable Definition"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/41","title":"tech debt | Clean code","issue_number":41,"body":"Objective: Assumption that consistent code will help AI add new code/documentation faster, seamless, \n\nhttps://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/blob/202502/docs/clean_code.md\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/41","display_title":"tech debt | Clean code"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/29","title":"tech debt | switch engine to registry design pattern","issue_number":29,"body":"siva used it with writers.py, doris_writer.py. \r\n\r\nThe way reportgen uses the registry design (to read a writer class name from config yml, then initialize the appropriate writer class and initiate the run method) is similar/ same as what engine is doing. \r\n\r\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/29","display_title":"tech debt | switch engine to registry design pattern"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/28","title":"tech debt | switch to loguru","issue_number":28,"body":"- [x] currently assetutilities uses python built-in logging. Log files are also crated.\n\n- [x] loguru has color coded logging and much more detailed diagnostic context. \n\n- [x] Ensure loguru messages are added to the default run log files in log directory (@samdansk2 )\n- [x] Add documentation to assetutilities (@samdansk2 )\n\nReferences:\nhttps://betterstack.com/community/guides/logging/loguru/\nhttps://github.com/Delgan/loguru/issues/80\nhttps://loguru.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/logger.html\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/28","display_title":"tech debt | switch to loguru"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/75","title":"Simplify CI test environment to use the declared test dependency path","issue_number":75,"body":"Summary\nThe recent fixes restored the canonical pytest command and async plugin support, but CI still installs test tooling via a mixed path:\n- `uv sync --group dev`\n- `uv pip install pytest-benchmark`\n\nWhy this is a future cleanup item\n- The repo now has a clearer testing contract, but CI still does not use a single declared test dependency path\n- Mixing a dev group with an ad hoc `uv pip install` is harder to reason about and can drift from `pyproject.toml`\n\nSuggested follow-up\n- Standardize CI on one explicit dependency path for test execution\n- Prefer using the declared test dependency set directly, or otherwise document why CI intentionally differs\n- Remove the extra ad hoc `uv pip install pytest-benchmark` step if it becomes redundant\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- CI installs test dependencies through one consistent declared path\n- Workflow YAML matches the packaging model in `pyproject.toml`\n- No unnecessary ad hoc pytest plugin install remains\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/assetutilities/issues/75","display_title":"Simplify CI test environment to use the declared test dependency path"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/281","title":"WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7","issue_number":281,"body":"## WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7\n\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** orcaflex-license-machine\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>🔨 Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📋 Plan</summary>\n\n## Description\nExtract ~235 OrcaFlex .dat models from rock-oil-field/s7/, sanitize client references, convert to YAML, organize into library categories (jumper, installation, mooring, training), generate spec.yml for each model group, validate round-trip via 3-way benchmark.\n\n## Deliverables\n- [ ] Sanitization script: `scripts/sanitize_s7_models.py`\n- [ ] Spec extraction script: `scripts/extract_s7_specs.py`\n- [ ] Legal deny list: `digitalmodel/.legal-deny-list.yaml`\n- [ ] Sanitized models in `docs/modules/orcaflex/{jumper,installation,mooring,training}/`\n- [ ] spec.yml for each model group\n- [ ] Jumper analysis skill: `.claude/skills/orcaflex-jumper-analysis/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Legal sanity scan skill: `.claude/skills/legal-sanity-scan/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (exit code 0)\n- [ ] Round-trip validation on jumper + mooring models\n\n## Progress\n- 2026-02-11: Plan approved. Scripts and skills creation in progress.\n\n## Agentic AI Horizon\n\n- Extracting and cataloguing OrcaFlex models from rock-oil-field/s7 creates a sanitised reference library that agents can use for pattern matching and schema design — high reuse value.\n- OrcaFlex model extraction and sanitisation requires domain expertise to identify what is generic vs client-specific; this won't be automated by better models.\n- **Disposition: do now** — reference model extraction is prerequisite for WRK-032, WRK-036, and WRK-045; close this working item promptly.\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>✅ Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] Sanitization script: `scripts/sanitize_s7_models.py`\n- [ ] Spec extraction script: `scripts/extract_s7_specs.py`\n- [ ] Legal deny list: `digitalmodel/.legal-deny-list.yaml`\n- [ ] Sanitized models in `docs/modules/orcaflex/{jumper,installation,mooring,training}/`\n- [ ] spec.yml for each model group\n- [ ] Jumper analysis skill: `.claude/skills/orcaflex-jumper-analysis/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Legal sanity scan skill: `.claude/skills/legal-sanity-scan/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (exit code 0)\n- [ ] Round-trip validation on jumper + mooring models\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>🧪 TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📊 Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/281","display_title":"WRK-121: Extract & Catalog OrcaFlex Models from rock-oil-field/s7"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/284","title":"WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms","issue_number":284,"body":"## WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms\n\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** acma-ansys05\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>🔨 Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📋 Plan</summary>\n\n# Update OrcaFlex License Agreement\n\n## What\nUpdate the OrcaFlex license agreement document with correct party addresses, ensure compliance with the existing ACMA-OrcaFlex agreement, and clarify 3rd-party usage terms.\n\n## Reference Documents\n- **Preliminary agreement**: `D:\\workspace-hub\\aceengineer-admin\\admin\\orcaflex\\`\n- **ACMA agreement to comply with**: `ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf` (same folder)\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### 1. Add Party Addresses\n- **ACMA Address**: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\n- **Achanta Aceengineer Inc Address**: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\n\n### 2. Compliance Check\n- Review `ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf` and ensure the updated agreement complies with all terms\n\n### 3. Third-Party Clarification\n- Clarify the definition and role of \"3rd party\" in the agreement\n- Add 3rd-party usage terms if needed to cover sublicensing or subcontracting scenarios\n\n## Why\nProper legal documentation with correct addresses, compliance with existing agreements, and clear 3rd-party terms protects all parties and ensures the OrcaFlex license is used within contractual bounds.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ACMA address added to agreement: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\n- [ ] Achanta Aceengineer Inc address added: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\n- [ ] Agreement reviewed against ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf for compliance\n- [ ] 3rd-party definition clarified in agreement\n- [ ] Additional 3rd-party terms added if gaps identified\n- [ ] Final document ready for review\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>✅ Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] ACMA address added to agreement: 565 S. Mason Road #395, Katy, Texas 77450\n- [ ] Achanta Aceengineer Inc address added: 11511 Piping Rock Dr., Houston, TX 77077\n- [ ] Agreement reviewed against ACMA-OrcaFlex-agreement.pdf for compliance\n- [ ] 3rd-party definition clarified in agreement\n- [ ] Additional 3rd-party terms added if gaps identified\n- [ ] Final document ready for review\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>🧪 TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📊 Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/284","display_title":"WRK-133: Update OrcaFlex license agreement with addresses and 3rd-party terms"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/283","title":"WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels — AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response","issue_number":283,"body":"## WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels — AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response\n\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering/marine\n**Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** orcaflex-license-machine\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>🔨 Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📋 Plan</summary>\n\n# Passing Ship Analysis for Moored Vessels\n\n## What\nBuild a passing ship analysis capability for moored vessels. Calculate hydrodynamic forces on a moored vessel due to a passing ship (surge, sway, yaw), evaluate mooring line tensions under passing ship events, and generate standardized reports. Covers perpendicular and parallel passing cases, with/without wind, at varying speeds and distances.\n\n## Why\n- Passing ship effects are a critical design case for port/terminal mooring systems\n- ~15+ historical projects demonstrate recurring demand for this analysis type\n- Currently relies on standalone Excel tool (`PassingShipForceCalculator.xlsm`) and manual AQWA runs\n- Standardizing into the digitalmodel framework enables parametric studies, consistent reporting, and reuse\n\n## Resources (local, not in repo)\n- **Tool**: `G:\\ACMA Tool\\Passing Ships\\` — existing passing ship force calculator (Excel-based)\n- **Archive**: `R:\\Archive - Drive J\\` — ~15+ past project folders with AQWA models, reports, and results\n- **Key tool files**: `PassingShipForceCalculator.xlsm` (force calculation), `PassingShipForceCalculator 3.7 knot.xlsm` (speed variant)\n- **Output examples**: Line tension plots at various passing speeds (3.0 knot, 3.7 knot), mooring line groups (1-6, 7-12)\n\n## Technical Scope\n1. **Passing ship force model** — hydrodynamic interaction forces (surge, sway, yaw) as function of:\n   - Passing ship speed, size (displacement, length, beam, draft)\n   - Moored vessel dimensions\n   - Separation distance (lateral)\n   - Water depth / depth-to-draft ratio\n   - Passing angle (parallel, perpendicular, oblique)\n2. **Mooring response** — time-domain mooring analysis with passing ship force time history:\n   - Line tensions per mooring line\n   - Vessel motions (surge, sway, yaw excursions)\n   - Fender loads\n   - Combined with wind, current, wave (with/without passing vessel scenarios)\n3. **Analysis cases** — parametric matrix:\n   - Wind with passing vessel / wind without passing vessel\n   - Perpendicular passing / parallel passing\n   - Multiple passing speeds\n   - Short ship / long ship variants\n4. **PassingShipForceCalculator extraction** — reverse-engineer the Excel tool logic into Python\n5. **AQWA integration** — passing ship force application in AQWA mooring analysis (or OrcaFlex equivalent)\n6. **Reporting** — standardized HTML report per WRK-129 convention\n\n## PassingShipSpec — Analysis Specification\nCreate a `PassingShipSpec` (similar to `DiffractionSpec` pattern) that fully defines a passing ship analysis:\n- **Moored vessel**: hull geometry, mooring arrangement, loading condition, RAOs\n- **Passing ship**: type, displacement, LOA, beam, draft, speed, track (distance, angle)\n- **Environment**: water depth, wind speed/direction, current, wave conditions\n- **Analysis matrix**: cases (with/without wind, with/without passing, speeds, angles)\n- **Output requests**: line tensions, vessel motions, fender loads, force time histories\n- Spec format: YAML (`spec.yml`), validated by Pydantic schema, drives automated analysis pipeline\n\n## Benchmarking — 5-7 Historical Projects\nReproduce 5-7 past passing ship projects from `R:\\Archive - Drive J\\` to validate the new implementation:\n1. Extract original analysis inputs (vessel data, mooring layout, passing ship parameters, environmental conditions)\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>✅ Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [x] `PassingShipSpec` Pydantic schema defined and validated\n- [x] Passing ship force calculation implemented in Python (from Excel tool extraction)\n- [x] Force time history generation for given passing scenario (speed, distance, ship size)\n- [ ] Mooring response analysis with passing ship forces (line tensions, motions)\n- [ ] Parametric study capability (speed × distance × wind × passing angle matrix)\n- [ ] 5-7 benchmark cases reproduced from historical projects, results within tolerance\n- [ ] Each benchmark has sanitized `spec.yml` in `docs/domains/orcaflex/passing_ship/`\n- [ ] Standardized HTML report with force plots, tension envelopes, motion time histories\n- [x] Integration with existing hydrodynamics module\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>🧪 TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📊 Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/283","display_title":"WRK-131: Passing ship analysis for moored vessels — AQWA-based force calculation and mooring response"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/280","title":"WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat","issue_number":280,"body":"## WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat\n\n**Status:** blocked | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering/marine\n**Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** acma-ansys05\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>🔨 Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📋 Plan</summary>\n\n# OrcaFlex Format Converter: License-Required Tasks\n\n## Context\n\nThe OrcaFlex Three-Way Format Converter (`format_converter/`) was implemented on a non-licensed machine. **All 102 tests pass** using YAML-only operations. The following tasks require an OrcaFlex license (OrcFxAPI) and must be completed on a licensed machine.\n\n## Completed (no license needed)\n\n- [x] `yaml_utils.py` — Canonical `OrcaFlexDumper`, `orcaflex_dump()`, `orcaflex_load()`\n- [x] `protocols.py` — `ConversionReport` dataclass, `FormatConverter` protocol\n- [x] `section_mapping.py` — `SECTION_MAPPING`, `REVERSE_SECTION_MAPPING`, `INPUT_PARAMETERS`\n- [x] `format_detector.py` — `FormatType` enum, `detect_format()`\n- [x] `single_to_modular.py` — `SingleToModularConverter` (promoted from yaml_to_include.py)\n- [x] `modular_to_single.py` — `ModularToSingleConverter` (extracted from level_3_physical.py)\n- [x] `spec_to_modular.py` — `SpecToModularConverter` (wraps ModularModelGenerator)\n- [x] `spec_to_single.py` — `SpecToSingleConverter` (chains spec→modular→single)\n- [x] `modular_to_spec.py` — `ModularToSpecConverter` (best-effort reverse extraction)\n- [x] `single_to_spec.py` — `SingleToSpecConverter` (chains single→modular→spec)\n- [x] `cli.py` — 8 subcommands (single2modular, modular2single, spec2modular, etc.)\n- [x] `__main__.py` — `python -m` entry point\n- [x] `pyproject.toml` — `orcaflex-convert` entry point registered\n- [x] 102 tests passing (yaml_utils, format_detector, single↔modular, round-trip, spec conversions, CLI)\n\n## Pending Tasks (require OrcaFlex license)\n\n### 1. End-to-end OrcaFlex validation test\nRun converted YAML files through OrcaFlex to verify they load and simulate correctly:\n```bash\n# On licensed machine:\nuv run python -m digitalmodel.modules.orcaflex.format_converter \\\n    single2modular \"docs/modules/orcaflex/examples/raw/A01/A01 Catenary riser.yml\" \\\n    -o /tmp/a01_modular/\n\n# Load in OrcaFlex and verify static analysis runs\nuv run python -c \"\nimport OrcFxAPI\nmodel = OrcFxAPI.Model()\nmodel.LoadData('/tmp/a01_modular/master.yml')\nmodel.CalculateStatics()\nprint('Static analysis OK')\n\"\n```\n\n### 2. Round-trip OrcaFlex binary fidelity test\nVerify round-trip through OrcaFlex binary format preserves model:\n```\nA01.yml → single2modular → modular → OrcaFlex load → OrcaFlex save → compare\n```\n\n### 3. Update backward-compat wrapper in `scripts/conversion/yaml_to_include.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>✅ Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [x] `yaml_utils.py` — Canonical `OrcaFlexDumper`, `orcaflex_dump()`, `orcaflex_load()`\n- [x] `protocols.py` — `ConversionReport` dataclass, `FormatConverter` protocol\n- [x] `section_mapping.py` — `SECTION_MAPPING`, `REVERSE_SECTION_MAPPING`, `INPUT_PARAMETERS`\n- [x] `format_detector.py` — `FormatType` enum, `detect_format()`\n- [x] `single_to_modular.py` — `SingleToModularConverter` (promoted from yaml_to_include.py)\n- [x] `modular_to_single.py` — `ModularToSingleConverter` (extracted from level_3_physical.py)\n- [x] `spec_to_modular.py` — `SpecToModularConverter` (wraps ModularModelGenerator)\n- [x] `spec_to_single.py` — `SpecToSingleConverter` (chains spec→modular→single)\n- [x] `modular_to_spec.py` — `ModularToSpecConverter` (best-effort reverse extraction)\n- [x] `single_to_spec.py` — `SingleToSpecConverter` (chains single→modular→spec)\n- [x] `cli.py` — 8 subcommands (single2modular, modular2single, spec2modular, etc.)\n- [x] `__main__.py` — `python -m` entry point\n- [x] `pyproject.toml` — `orcaflex-convert` entry point registered\n- [x] 102 tests passing (yaml_utils, format_detector, single↔modular, round-trip, spec conversions, CLI)\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>🧪 TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📊 Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/280","display_title":"WRK-064: 'OrcaFlex format converter: license-required validation and backward-compat"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/277","title":"WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering — hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies","issue_number":277,"body":"## WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering — hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies\n\n**Status:** working | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering/pipeline\n**Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** ace-linux-2\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>🔨 Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📋 Plan</summary>\n\n# FreeCAD Deep Parametric Engineering\n\n## Mission\n\nEnable production-grade FreeCAD automation for parametric hull generation with hydrostatic analysis, FEM preprocessing through the CalculiX solver chain, and design table driven parameter sweep studies with automated exports.\n\n## What\n\nThe freecad-automation skill covers the API surface. This item adds depth for real engineering work:\n\n1. **Parametric hull generation with hydrostatics** — define hull form via principal dimensions (L, B, T, Cb) → generate NURBS hull surface → compute hydrostatics (displacement, KM, BM, waterplane area) → export to STEP/STL for downstream solvers\n2. **FEM preprocessing chain** — geometry → gmsh mesh → boundary conditions → material properties → CalculiX input deck → solve → extract stress/displacement results\n3. **Design table driven studies** — YAML-defined parameter matrix (e.g., plate thickness, stiffener spacing, material grade) → batch FreeCAD model generation → batch FEM analysis → results comparison table\n4. **Round-trip validation** — FreeCAD → STEP → gmsh mesh → verify watertightness → OpenFOAM/AQWA case setup (validates the full pipeline from CAD to solver)\n\n## Why\n\nFreeCAD is the only open-source parametric CAD tool in the stack. Making it work reliably for hull design and structural analysis enables rapid concept screening without commercial licenses. The FEM chain through CalculiX provides structural validation capability that currently requires ANSYS (licensed, limited to acma-ansys05).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Hull generator: input (L=100m, B=20m, T=8m, Cb=0.7) → FreeCAD NURBS hull → hydrostatics within 2% of analytical\n- [ ] FEM chain: plate with hole → gmsh mesh → CalculiX → stress concentration factor within 5% of analytical (Kt ≈ 3.0)\n- [ ] Design table: 3+ parameter variations → batch generation → results comparison YAML\n- [ ] Round-trip: FreeCAD hull → STEP → gmsh → STL → verify closed surface (manifold check)\n- [ ] All operations headless via freecadcmd (no GUI dependency)\n- [ ] Integration tests with known engineering problems (simply supported beam, pressure vessel)\n- [ ] Update freecad-automation skill with deep workflow sections\n\n## Plan\n\n*To be developed at Stage 4.*\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>✅ Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] Hull generator: input (L=100m, B=20m, T=8m, Cb=0.7) → FreeCAD NURBS hull → hydrostatics within 2% of analytical\n- [ ] FEM chain: plate with hole → gmsh mesh → CalculiX → stress concentration factor within 5% of analytical (Kt ≈ 3.0)\n- [ ] Design table: 3+ parameter variations → batch generation → results comparison YAML\n- [ ] Round-trip: FreeCAD hull → STEP → gmsh → STL → verify closed surface (manifold check)\n- [ ] All operations headless via freecadcmd (no GUI dependency)\n- [ ] Integration tests with known engineering problems (simply supported beam, pressure vessel)\n- [ ] Update freecad-automation skill with deep workflow sections\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>🧪 TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>📊 Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/277","display_title":"WRK-1251: FreeCAD deep parametric engineering — hull generation, FEM chain, design table studies"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/271","title":"WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration — Phase 2 deployment for both clients","issue_number":271,"body":"## WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration — Phase 2 deployment for both clients\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\n\n**Repo:** ['frontierdeepwater', 'TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nDeploy engineering AI chatbots via Microsoft Teams for both Client 1 and Client 2,\nreplacing the desktop demo with a persistent, team-accessible assistant.\n\nBoth clients have Microsoft Teams — this enables a low-friction deployment path\nwithout requiring browser setup or CLI access per engineer.\n\n### Architecture\n\n**Option A (Recommended — start here):**\nTeams + Azure Bot Service + Claude API\n```\nEngineer (Teams) → Azure Bot Service → Claude API (with system prompt)\n                       ↓\n                 Logging / audit trail (Azure)\n```\n- System prompts from WRK-625 (Client 1) / WRK-629 (Client 2) loaded as bot persona\n- No RAG required for Phase 2 — system prompt + conversation context sufficient\n- Cost: ~$20-200/mo per team (Claude API usage)\n- Setup time: 1-2 days with Azure Bot Framework SDK\n\n**Option B (Graduate to when usage grows):**\nTeams + Azure Bot Service + RAG backend\n```\nEngineer (Teams) → Azure Bot Service → RAG retriever → Company knowledge base\n                       ↓                    ↓\n                 Claude API          Azure Cognitive Search / Pinecone\n```\n- Index calculation memos, project reports, design basis docs\n- Cost: $500-2,000/mo\n- Setup time: 2-4 weeks\n\n### Phase 2 Deliverables\n\n**Teams bot configuration:**\n- `deployment/teams-bot/manifest.json` — Teams app manifest\n- `deployment/teams-bot/bot.py` — Azure Bot Service handler (Python)\n  - Routes messages to Claude API with discipline-specific system prompt\n  - Handles conversation threading (multi-turn context)\n  - Logs Q&A to Azure Table Storage for audit trail\n- `deployment/teams-bot/config.yaml` — API keys (env vars), model selection, rate limits\n- `deployment/teams-bot/system_prompts/` — symlink to `ai-initiatives/prompts/`\n\n**Client 1 Teams bot:**\n- Bot name: \"Rigid Jumper Assistant\" (SME1's team channel)\n- System prompt: `rigid_jumper_assistant.md` from WRK-625\n- Fallback: \"Pipeline Engineering Assistant\" if pipeline queries detected\n\n**Client 2 Teams bot:**\n- Bot name: \"Structural Engineering Assistant\"\n- System prompt: `structural_offshore_assistant.md` from WRK-629\n- Focused on diffraction / plate FFS / GoA\n\n**Shared infrastructure:**\n- Azure resource group `aceengineer-ai-clients` with shared Bot Service\n- Per-client app registrations (separate AAD apps for auth isolation)\n- Usage dashboard: Azure Monitor → daily token consumption per client\n\n### Rollout Plan\n\n```\nWeek 2-3: Deploy bot to 2-3 engineers per team (pilot)\nWeek 4:   Evaluate usage metrics, refine prompts from pilot feedback\nWeek 5+:  Expand to full team; decide on RAG upgrade (Option B)\n```\n\n### Knowledge Base Integration (Option B path)\n\nWhen graduating to RAG:\n- Index sources: calculation memos, SOWs, design basis docs (client uploads)\n- Chunking strategy: section-level (## headers) with frontmatter metadata\n- Retrieval: top-3 chunks by cosine similarity, injected into Claude context\n- Document store: Azure Blob Storage + Azure Cognitive Search\n- Privacy: client 1 and client 2 data in separate search indexes (no cross-contamination)\n\n### Why\n\nMicrosoft Teams is already the communication hub at both clients — deploying the AI\nassistant there removes the \"I have to open another tab\" friction that kills adoption.\nBot appears in the engineer's existing channel; questions feel natural in chat format.\nAzure Bot Service + Claude API is a 2-day setup with no new infrastructure beyond\nwhat both clients already have (Microsoft 365 / Azure tenant).\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] `deployment/teams-bot/bot.py` implemented with Claude API integration\n- [ ] `deployment/teams-bot/manifest.json` created for Teams app deployment\n- [ ] Client 1 bot deployed to test Teams tenant and validated (3 questions)\n- [ ] Client 2 bot deployed to test Teams tenant and validated (3 questions)\n- [ ] Conversation threading (multi-turn context) working\n- [ ] Audit log (Q&A pairs) persisted to Azure Table Storage\n- [ ] Usage dashboard stub in Azure Monitor\n- [ ] README: 1-page deployment guide for client IT admin\n- [ ] No client API keys or tenant IDs hardcoded — all via env vars\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/271","display_title":"WRK-631: feat(frontierdeepwater): Microsoft Teams chatbot integration — Phase 2 deployment for both clients"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/270","title":"WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package","issue_number":270,"body":"## WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** marine\n\n**Repo:** ['TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nDays 2–5 deliverables for Client 2 engineering AI demo.\n\n### Calculation Templates (Day 2)\n\n**Diffraction analysis templates:**\n- `demo/calc_diffraction_panel_model_setup.md` — AQWA/WAMIT model conventions prompt:\n  panel mesh requirements (8 panels per wavelength min), symmetry planes, free surface,\n  waterplane area check, zero-speed vs forward speed; typical RAO output format\n- `demo/calc_rao_interpretation.md` — RAO extraction prompt: peak period identification,\n  heading matrix coverage, cancellation frequencies, cross-coupling terms (heave/pitch)\n- `demo/calc_qtf_second_order.md` — QTF usage: difference-frequency loads for mooring\n  low-frequency response; sum-frequency for TLP/spar springing; Newman's approximation\n  when full QTF not available\n\n**Plate FFS calculation templates:**\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part4_metal_loss.md` — API 579-1 Part 4 for plate: average\n  measured thickness vs minimum required; RSF_a screening; Level 1 vs Level 2 distinction\n  for plates (no hoop stress — limit load governs); MFFL (minimum future flaw limit)\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part8_distortion.md` — Part 8 shell distortions: peaking/angular\n  misalignment in welds, out-of-roundness; equivalent stress from distortion; buckling\n  interaction check for stiffened plates\n- `demo/calc_plate_ffs_part9_cracks.md` — FAD approach for crack-like flaws:\n  K_r vs L_r diagram; BS 7910 Level 2B; fracture toughness input (K_mat or J_mat);\n  fatigue crack growth projection (Paris law); remaining life calculation\n\n**GoA analysis templates:**\n- `demo/calc_goa_seismic_check.md` — API RP 2EQ spectral analysis: platform period,\n  base shear, OLE/CLE/ALE limit states; pushover capacity check\n- `demo/calc_goa_extreme_metocean.md` — 100-yr GoA wave/current/wind parameters;\n  comparison with GoM (typically harsher wave heights, lower Hs for ice-dominated zones);\n  API RP 2N ice loading: first-year ridges, multi-year ice pressure, ice crushing force\n\n### Multi-Step Workflows (Day 4)\n\n**Diffraction-to-structural load workflow:**\nFile: `demo/workflow_diffraction_to_structural.md`\n1. Input: water depth, vessel/structure dimensions, wave environment (Hs, Tp, heading)\n2. Step 1 → panel model adequacy check (mesh density for peak period)\n3. Step 2 → RAO interpretation (identify governing responses by heading)\n4. Step 3 → combined load derivation (wave + wind + current for governing sea state)\n5. Step 4 → structural utilisation flag (member/joint check indication)\n6. Output: summary table — governing headings, load cases for detailed structural check\n\n**GoA FFS decision workflow:**\nFile: `demo/workflow_goa_ffs_decision.md`\n1. Input: inspection findings (wall loss % / crack dimensions / distortion mm)\n2. Step 1 → GoA environment severity classification (ice zone, seismic zone, metocean)\n3. Step 2 → FFS Level 1 screening (API 579-1 plates)\n4. Step 3 → remaining life at GoA corrosion rate\n5. Step 4 → re-inspection interval recommendation (BSEE GoA ops environment)\n6. Output: FFS verdict + GoA-specific inspection schedule\n\n### Maritime Legal Case Templates (Day 4)\n\n**Casualty investigation analysis:**\n- `demo/maritime_casualty_analysis.md` — prompt template for reviewing MAIB/NTSB/USCG\n  reports: extract contributing factors → ISM Code failures → root-cause hierarchy;\n  sample: parse a MAIB report section and output structured findings table\n- `demo/maritime_statistical_context.md` — prompt using `worldenergydata.MAIBLoader` +\n  `NTSBMarineLoader` (WRK-320): \"find comparable incidents for vessel type X / failure\n  mode Y\" → precedent table with dates, vessel types, outcomes, regulatory citations\n\n**Expert witness support:**\n- `demo/expert_witness_report_template.md` — structured technical report for legal:\n  scope of appointment, methodology, engineering findings, opinion (standard of care),\n  limitations; Daubert-compliant framing; deposition Q&A prep prompt\n- `demo/liability_framing_prompt.md` — translate engineering findings into\n  legal causation language: \"the failure of [component] was a proximate cause of...\n  consistent with / inconsistent with the standard of care because...\"\n\n**Maritime legal decision workflow:**\nFile: `demo/workflow_maritime_legal_analysis.md`\n1. Input: incident description (vessel type, operation, casualty type, jurisdiction)\n2. Step 1 → applicable regulatory framework (USCG CFR / MAIB / IMO)\n3. Step 2 → ISM Code non-conformity screen (safety management system failures)\n4. Step 3 → comparable incident precedents (MAIB/NTSB database query)\n5. Step 4 → standard of care assessment (industry practice vs regulatory requirement)\n6. Step 5 → damages estimation framework (limitation of liability, P&I coverage)\n7. Output: case analysis memo outline with evidence gaps flagged\n\n### BSEE GoA Data Prompts (Day 4)\nFile: `demo/goa_bsee_data_queries.md`\n- GoA active leases, historical platforms (Cook Inlet focus)\n- Environmental study requirements for GoA OCS projects\n- Seismic hazard data for GoA vs GOM structural design\n- Ice zone classification per USCG/BSEE GoA regulations\n\n### Demo Package (Day 5)\nFile: `demo/demo_script_client2.md`\n- 15-20 min flow: diffraction overview → plate FFS walkthrough → GoA live data query\n- 3 \"wow\" moments: QTF second-order loads, plate crack FAD diagram, GoA vs GOM comparison\n- FAQ: \"How does AI handle site-specific GoA conditions?\" — BSEE data integration demo\n\n### Why\n\nDiffraction workflows + FFS for plates + GoA is a high-value combination for offshore\nstructural integrity work that is typically very time-intensive (multi-day model setup,\nmanual code checks). The GoA angle is differentiated — most AI demos focus on GoM.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] 3 diffraction templates with AQWA/WAMIT conventions and sample I/O\n- [ ] 3 plate FFS templates (Part 4/8/9) with worked examples\n- [ ] 2 GoA-specific calc templates (seismic + metocean) with sample parameters\n- [ ] Diffraction-to-structural workflow prompt chain documented\n- [ ] GoA FFS decision workflow documented\n- [ ] BSEE GoA data query prompts tested\n- [ ] 4 maritime legal templates created (casualty analysis, statistical context, expert\n- [ ] Maritime legal decision workflow (7-step) documented with sample I/O\n- [ ] MAIB/NTSB statistical context prompt validated against `worldenergydata` loaders\n- [ ] Demo script (15-20 min) includes maritime legal showcase (casualty analysis moment)\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/270","display_title":"WRK-630: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal workflows + demo package"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/269","title":"WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base","issue_number":269,"body":"## WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** marine\n\n**Repo:** ['TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nDay 1 foundation for Client 2 engineering AI demo. Client 2 focus areas:\n- **Diffraction analysis** — wave-structure interaction, RAOs, QTFs, panel model setup\n- **Fitness for service (FFS) for plates** — API 579-1 assessments for plate/shell geometry\n  (not pipe — different remaining strength methodology)\n- **Gulf of Alaska (GoA) analysis** — seismic, extreme metocean, ice loading, environmental\n- **Maritime legal cases consulting** — casualty investigation support, expert witness\n  technical analysis, MAIB/NTSB/USCG report interpretation, admiralty law interface\n\n### 1. System Prompt — Client 2 Structural/Offshore Assistant\n\nFile: `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/structural_offshore_assistant.md`\n\nCore competencies to include:\n- **Diffraction analysis**: AQWA, WAMIT, OrcaFlex wave interaction; panel model conventions;\n  RAO extraction and interpretation; QTF for second-order wave loads; wave heading matrices\n- **FFS for plates/shells**: API 579-1 Part 4 (general metal loss in plate), Part 5 (local LTA),\n  Part 8 (shell distortions — peaking, ovality, buckles), Part 9 (crack-like flaws via FAD),\n  Part 3 (brittle fracture); remaining strength factor for plate vs pipe distinction\n- **GoA analysis**: API RP 2EQ seismic, API RP 2MET extreme metocean, ice loading per API RP 2N,\n  environmental permitting under NEPA/ESA, extreme 100-yr wave/current parameters\n- Primary codes: API RP 2EQ, API RP 2A-WSD/LRFD, ISO 19902, API 579-1, BS 7910,\n  API RP 2MET, API RP 2N (Arctic), AISC 360, AWS D1.1\n\n### 2. Knowledge Base Files\n\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/api_579_plate_ffs.md` — Part 4/5/8/9 for plates;\n  key distinction: plate remaining strength uses limit load vs pipe burst pressure\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/diffraction_analysis_reference.md` — panel method\n  theory; AQWA/WAMIT model setup conventions; RAO/QTF interpretation; damping models\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/goa_design_criteria.md` — 100-yr design parameters;\n  seismic zones; ice drift/pressure; BSEE GoA lease/permit context; ADEC environmental reqs\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/api_rp_2a_structural.md` — tubular joint checks,\n  member utilisation, fatigue SCFs, in-service inspection intervals\n\n### 4. System Prompt — Maritime Legal Cases Consultant\n\nFile: `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/maritime_legal_consultant.md`\n\nCore competencies:\n- **Casualty investigation**: MAIB (UK), NTSB Marine (US), USCG MISLE incident databases;\n  root-cause taxonomy (equipment failure, human factors, weather, management system);\n  ISM Code non-conformity identification; SOLAS Chapter IX compliance review\n- **Expert witness support**: technical analysis for admiralty proceedings; translating\n  engineering findings into lay language; report structure for legal proceedings;\n  probability of causation framing; standards of care (industry vs regulatory)\n- **Admiralty law interface**: collision regulations (COLREGs); salvage and wreck removal;\n  limitation of liability (Limitation Act / Jones Act / MLC 2006); cargo damage claims\n  (Hague-Visby Rules, Hamburg Rules); P&I Club process and club circular interpretation\n- **USCG / BSEE regulatory**: CFR 46 (vessel inspection), CFR 33 (navigation), OCS safety\n  regulations; incident notification requirements; MOC (management of change) for maritime\n- **Incident data analysis**: leverage `worldenergydata.MAIBLoader` + `NTSBMarineLoader`\n  (WRK-320 done) for statistical incident context; vessel type vs failure mode correlation;\n  comparable casualty precedents for damages estimation\n\nPrimary references: MAIB investigation reports, NTSB marine accident reports, USCG Marine\nCasualty Reports, ISM Code, SOLAS, MARPOL, COLREGs, MLC 2006, Jones Act (46 USC 30104),\nLimitation of Shipowners' Liability Act (46 USC 30501-30512)\n\n### 5. Knowledge Base Files — Maritime Legal\n\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/maritime_casualty_investigation.md` — MAIB/NTSB/USCG\n  investigation process; ISM Code audit framework; root-cause taxonomy table\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/admiralty_law_reference.md` — COLREGs rules summary;\n  Jones Act key provisions; limitation of liability thresholds; P&I Club claim stages\n- `ai-initiatives-client2/knowledge/expert_witness_framework.md` — report structure for\n  legal proceedings; Daubert standard (US) / Civil Evidence Act (UK); how to frame\n  engineering opinion as standard of care; deposition preparation checklist\n\n### 6. Folder Scaffold\n\n```\nai-initiatives-client2/\n├── prompts/\n│   ├── structural_offshore_assistant.md\n│   └── maritime_legal_consultant.md\n├── knowledge/\n│   ├── api_579_plate_ffs.md\n│   ├── diffraction_analysis_reference.md\n│   ├── goa_design_criteria.md\n│   ├── api_rp_2a_structural.md\n│   ├── maritime_casualty_investigation.md\n│   ├── admiralty_law_reference.md\n│   └── expert_witness_framework.md\n├── demo/\n└── pilot/\n```\n\n### Why\n\nClient 2's disciplines are structurally different from Client 1:\n- Diffraction is a numerical/frequency-domain speciality — the AI context files need to carry\n  the panel model conventions and output format knowledge\n- Plate FFS follows different methodology than pipe FFS (Part 4/5 uses net-section collapse for\n  plates, not burst pressure) — requires separate knowledge base\n- GoA context overlaps with Client 1 but adds Arctic/seismic dimension unique to this client\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] System prompt created at `ai-initiatives-client2/prompts/structural_offshore_assistant.md`\n- [ ] 4 knowledge base markdown files created\n- [ ] Maritime legal system prompt created with MAIB/NTSB/COLREGs/Jones Act coverage\n- [ ] 3 maritime legal knowledge base files created\n- [ ] 5 test questions validated per focus area (diffraction, plate FFS, GoA, maritime legal)\n- [ ] FFS plate vs pipe distinction clearly handled in system prompt\n- [ ] Expert witness report structure included in maritime prompt\n- [ ] No client-specific proprietary data — public codes/standards only\n- [ ] `target_repos` updated from TBD to actual client repo when created\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/269","display_title":"WRK-629: feat(client2): engineering AI demo — diffraction + plate FFS + GoA + maritime legal system prompts + knowledge base"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/272","title":"WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit — version + clause consistency via Gemini","issue_number":272,"body":"## WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit — version + clause consistency via Gemini\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\n\n**Repo:** ['digitalmodel'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\ndigitalmodel implements calculations against 15+ engineering standards\n(DNV, API, ISO, ABS, BS). Version years and clause numbers are embedded as\nstring literals and comments throughout the codebase. Inconsistencies cause\ncalculation errors when a standard is revised.\n\nUse Gemini to sweep all engineering modules in one pass and produce a\nstandards-citation-audit report flagging:\n1. Conflicting version years for the same standard across modules\n2. Clause citations that look implausible (wrong section numbering pattern)\n3. Modules referencing a standard without a version year\n4. Standards used in multiple modules with different acceptance thresholds\n\n### Why\n\nEngineering standards evolve; using mixed version years in the same codebase can produce\ncontradictory acceptance criteria for the same parameter. Gemini's large context makes a\nsingle-pass audit of 15+ modules practical without losing cross-module context.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] `specs/wrk/WRK-662/standards-citation-audit.md` with all 4 tables populated\n- [ ] CONFLICT table has ≤ 5 items OR all conflicts are resolved with inline comments\n- [ ] MISSING VERSION table has action taken (year added or deferred with rationale)\n- [ ] Cross-check against standards-transfer-ledger shows ≥80% of cited standards\n- [ ] Legal scan passes\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/272","display_title":"WRK-662: analysis(digitalmodel): engineering standards citation audit — version + clause consistency via Gemini"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/470","title":"Seakeeping analysis using OpenFOAM — CFD-based ship motion simulation","issue_number":470,"body":"## Context\n\nLinkedIn post by Belal Sherif on seakeeping simulation using OpenFOAM:\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/posts/belal-sherif-5a1980243_a-new-seakeeping-simulation-whats-special-share-7442515370885685248-heR3\n\n## Description\n\nAdd seakeeping analysis capability using OpenFOAM for CFD-based ship/vessel motion simulation in waves. This goes beyond potential-flow BEM solvers (Capytaine, OrcaWave, AQWA) by capturing viscous effects, slamming, green water, and nonlinear wave-body interaction.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Phase 1 — Literature and Method Survey\n- Review OpenFOAM seakeeping tutorials and published workflows (interDyMFoam, overInterDyMFoam with overset meshes)\n- Catalog mesh motion strategies: morphing, overset/chimera, 6-DOF rigid body solver\n- Identify benchmark cases (Wigley hull, DTMB 5415, KCS) with experimental data\n\n### Phase 2 — Basic Seakeeping Setup\n- Regular wave generation (Stokes 2nd/5th, stream function) using waveMaker or waves2Foam/olaFlow\n- Ship hull mesh import from FreeCAD or STL\n- 6-DOF motion solver coupling (sixDoFRigidBodyMotion)\n- Heave and pitch RAO extraction in head seas\n\n### Phase 3 — Advanced Capabilities\n- Irregular sea state simulations (JONSWAP / PM spectra)\n- Multi-directional seas, oblique headings (roll, sway, yaw)\n- Green water / deck wetness detection\n- Slamming pressure extraction on bow/bottom panels\n- Added resistance in waves (drift force integration)\n\n### Phase 4 — Validation and Integration\n- Benchmark against BEM codes (Capytaine #464, OrcaWave) for linear regime\n- Compare with model test data where available\n- Integration with digitalmodel YAML-driven workflow (spec.yml pattern)\n- ParaView post-processing automation for motion animations\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- Primary solvers: interDyMFoam (dynamic mesh), overInterDyMFoam (overset)\n- Wave libraries: olaFlow (preferred, actively maintained), waves2Foam, or built-in waveMaker\n- Mesh: snappyHexMesh or cfMesh for hull meshing; overset for large-amplitude motions\n- Related issues: #154 (OpenFOAM deep solver workflows), #139 (OpenFOAM CFD capability), #155 (CAD-to-CFD pipeline), #464 (Capytaine BEM)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Reproduce at least one published seakeeping benchmark (heave/pitch RAO within 10% of exp data)\n- [ ] YAML-driven workflow: spec.yml -> mesh -> simulate -> extract RAOs\n- [ ] Documentation with tutorial walkthrough\n- [ ] Comparison plot: OpenFOAM CFD vs BEM (Capytaine or OrcaWave) for same hull","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/470","display_title":"Seakeeping analysis using OpenFOAM — CFD-based ship motion simulation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/463","title":"Populate ship-dimensions dataset from ship plans (manual curation follow-on)","issue_number":463,"body":"## Summary\nTrack the remaining manual-curation work after the ship-dimensions template + loader code was completed in `#457`.\n\n## Context\n`#457` delivered the code-side foundation:\n- default ship-dimensions template loading\n- stricter vessel-entry validation\n- registry merge normalization into `ship_data`\n- naval-architecture package exports\n- regression tests for default loading, alias handling, and merge normalization\n\nThe remaining work is not code scaffolding. It is data population and verification against source materials.\n\n## Remaining work\n1. Use the canonical ship-dimensions template artifact to populate vessel dimensions from the ship-plan PDFs.\n2. Record the required vessel fields without inventing values.\n3. Cross-reference against Jane's where available.\n4. Mark verified entries appropriately.\n5. Run the relevant validation once the dataset is populated.\n\n## Blockers\n- Blocked by `#461` to recover or replace the missing upstream template artifact from `WRK-1339` Child E.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- canonical template/input path is resolved via `#461`\n- ship-dimensions dataset is populated with the intended vessel coverage\n- verified entries are marked from source cross-reference\n- downstream validation passes on the populated dataset\n\n## Notes\nThis issue intentionally covers the manual/dataset portion only. The template + loader implementation was completed under `#457`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/463","display_title":"Populate ship-dimensions dataset from ship plans (manual curation follow-on)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/469","title":"Assess AI agent session artifact dirs across machines (.codex, .gemini, .claude/skills)","issue_number":469,"body":"## Purpose\n\nTrack the per-machine assessment of how AI agent session artifact directories (`.codex/`, `.gemini/`, `.claude/skills/` symlink files) should be handled in the repo. This issue records decisions made on each machine so they can be compared and a consistent policy confirmed.\n\n---\n\n## Background\n\nThree agent ecosystems each write working directories into the repo root:\n\n| Dir pattern | Agent | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.codex/CuXXX/` | Codex | session JSONL, scheduler log, coordination skills snapshot |\n| `.gemini/CuXXX/` | Gemini | same structure as Codex |\n| `.claude/skills/{guidelines,meta,workflows}` | Claude | symlink pointer files → `workspace-hub/.claude/skills/_internal/` |\n| `.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated` | Claude | datestamp of last skill propagation |\n\nAll three agents share the **same RAG aggregation pipeline**: their session logs are extracted nightly and written to `workspace-hub/.claude/skills/session-logs/aggregated/` (AI explanations TSV, human prompts TSV, tool stats). That aggregated output is the canonical cross-analysis artifact — the per-session `CuXXX` dirs are raw source already consumed.\n\n---\n\n## Decision Log\n\n### Machine: ACMA-ANSYS05 (Windows 11, licensed-win-1) — 2026-04-02\n\n**`.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/`**\n- **Decision: gitignore** ✅\n- Rationale: Transient per-session working dirs, 50+ accumulated. Raw content already aggregated upstream. No unique value to commit.\n- Action taken: Added `.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/` to `.gitignore` (commit `e4b1ea6f`, pushed `2c741fc3`).\n\n**`.claude/skills/{guidelines,meta,workflows}`**\n- **Status: OPEN — needs assessment**\n- These are ASCII text files containing relative symlink targets (e.g. `../../../.claude/skills/_internal/guidelines`). They are ecosystem propagation artifacts — set by `workspace-hub` propagation on 2026-03-31.\n- Question: Should these be committed (so other machines get the correct skill pointers on clone), or gitignored (they are regenerated by propagation)?\n- On this machine they are untracked but not yet gitignored.\n\n**`.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated`**\n- **Status: OPEN — needs assessment**\n- Single-line datestamp file (`20260331`). Acts as a sentinel for the last propagation run.\n- Question: Commit as state marker, or gitignore as machine-local runtime file?\n\n---\n\n## Questions to Resolve Per Machine\n\n1. Are `.codex/Cu*/` and `.gemini/Cu*/` already gitignored on your machine, or were they accumulating untracked?\n2. Do `.claude/skills/guidelines`, `.claude/skills/meta`, `.claude/skills/workflows` exist? Are they symlinks or text pointer files?\n3. Does `.claude/skills/.ecosystem-propagated` exist, and what date does it contain?\n4. Does cloning the repo and running without propagation break anything if the pointer files are absent?\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [ ] Assess on remaining licensed machines (ACMA-ANSYS04, etc.)\n- [ ] Decide: commit `.claude/skills` pointer files vs gitignore + regenerate on clone\n- [ ] If committing: add to a dedicated `chore(skills):` commit pattern\n- [ ] If gitignoring: add hook or setup script to regenerate on clone/pull","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/469","display_title":"Assess AI agent session artifact dirs across machines (.codex, .gemini, .claude/skills)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/467","title":"Subsea structure installation analysis — vessel performance and real-time motion feedback","issue_number":467,"body":"## Context\n\nEnable rapid assessment of subsea structure installation feasibility across varying structure dimensions, water depths, and installation vessels — then extend to real-time operational decision support.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Phase 1: Installation Analysis Engine\n- Parametric analysis: structure length × water depth × vessel type matrix\n- Crane tip motion and hook load dynamics from vessel RAOs\n- Lowering/lifting through splash zone assessment (DNV-RP-H103 §4)\n- Weather window estimation from operability limits\n- Quick-assess mode: screen multiple vessels against a given structure\n\n### Phase 2: Multi-Vessel Comparison\n- Standardized vessel database with crane capacity curves and RAO libraries\n- Side-by-side vessel comparison for a given installation task\n- Cost-weighted operability ranking\n- Sensitivity to heading, water depth, and wave period\n\n### Phase 3: Real-Time Motion Feedback\n- Hook up measured vessel motions (MRU/IMU data feed)\n- Compare real-time motions against allowable criteria\n- Go/no-go decision support dashboard\n- Alarm thresholds tied to installation phase (lift-off, splash zone, landing)\n- Record and replay for post-operation review\n\n## Standards\n\n- DNV-RP-H103 (Modelling and Analysis of Marine Operations)\n- DNV-ST-N001 (Marine Operations and Marine Warranty)\n- DNV-RP-C205 §7 (hydrodynamic coefficients for vessel response)\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Capytaine module (#464) or existing AQWA/OrcaWave RAO libraries\n- Marine ops module (`src/digitalmodel/marine_ops/`)\n- Signal processing module (`src/digitalmodel/signal_processing/`) for MRU data\n- Visualization module for dashboard/real-time display","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/467","display_title":"Subsea structure installation analysis — vessel performance and real-time motion feedback"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/466","title":"Parametric hull analysis — steady speed, passing ship, narrow water environments","issue_number":466,"body":"## Context\n\nExtend the hydrodynamics module with parametric hull analysis capabilities for real-world operational scenarios in restricted waterways.\n\n## Scope\n\n### 1. Parametric Hull Analysis\n- Systematic variation of hull form parameters (beam, draft, block coefficient, waterplane area)\n- Added mass and damping sensitivity to hull geometry\n- Automated sweep across hull variants with result comparison\n\n### 2. Steady Speed (Forward Speed) Analysis\n- BEM analysis with forward speed effects on wave-body interaction\n- Speed-dependent added mass and damping corrections\n- Wave resistance estimation at operational speeds\n- DNV-RP-C205 §7.4 forward speed corrections\n\n### 3. Passing Ship Analysis\n- Multi-body hydrodynamic interaction between passing vessels\n- Suction forces and moments as function of separation distance, speed, and relative heading\n- Time-domain force histories for moored vessel response\n- Leverages existing `src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/passing_ship/` module\n\n### 4. Narrow/Shallow Water Effects\n- Finite depth corrections for restricted waterways (DNV-RP-C205 §3.5)\n- Bank effects and channel confinement on hydrodynamic coefficients\n- Speed-dependent squat and trim in shallow water\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Vessel operator charts: parametric plots showing operational limits per vessel type\n- Comparison tables across vessel variants for given environmental conditions\n- Integration with Capytaine BEM module (#464) for open-source solver path\n\n## Standards\n\n- DNV-RP-C205 §3.5 (shallow water), §7.4 (forward speed)\n- PIANC guidelines for ship-ship interaction in confined waterways\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Capytaine module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/capytaine/`) — #464\n- Passing ship module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/passing_ship/`)\n- Hull library (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/hull_library/`)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/466","display_title":"Parametric hull analysis — steady speed, passing ship, narrow water environments"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/465","title":"Capytaine ship hull benchmarking — OC4 semi-sub + WAMIT validation","issue_number":465,"body":"## Context\n\nThe Capytaine BEM module (#464) is implemented with a sphere analytical benchmark (Hulme 1982). Ship hull validation is the logical next step to establish confidence for production use.\n\n## Available data in repo\n\n- **OC4 Semi-sub**: geometry mesh (`docs/domains/orcawave/examples/L02 OC4 Semi-sub/`) + full specification (mass 13.473M kg, CoG, inertia, water depth 200m)\n- **WAMIT validation cases**: 12 cases in `docs/domains/orcawave/L00_validation_wamit/` (cylinder, box, ISSC TLP, multi-body) with reference `.dat` files\n- **Unit box benchmark**: synthetic 3-way comparison (AQWA, OrcaWave, BEMRosetta) in `docs/benchmarks/unit_box/`\n- **WAMIT reference loader**: existing infrastructure at `src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/diffraction/wamit_reference_loader.py`\n\n## Scope\n\n1. **OC4 semi-sub benchmark**: load GDF mesh → Capytaine solve → compare RAOs against WAMIT/OrcaWave reference\n2. **WAMIT cylinder validation** (case 2.1): compare added mass/damping against WAMIT reference data\n3. **Cross-solver comparison plots**: Capytaine vs existing AQWA/OrcaWave results for shared geometries\n4. **Tolerance criteria**: define pass/fail thresholds per DNV-RP-C205 guidance\n\n## Standards\n\n- DNV-RP-C205 §7.1 (potential flow validation)\n- IEA Wind OC4 project (semi-submersible reference)\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Capytaine module (`src/digitalmodel/hydrodynamics/capytaine/`) — done in #464\n- Capytaine env at `/mnt/local-analysis/capytaine-env`\n- WAMIT reference loader for ground truth extraction","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/465","display_title":"Capytaine ship hull benchmarking — OC4 semi-sub + WAMIT validation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/464","title":"Add hydrodynamic BEM analysis module (Capytaine)","issue_number":464,"body":"## Summary\n\nAdd wave-body interaction analysis to digitalmodel using Capytaine BEM solver — diffraction, radiation, added mass, damping coefficients, and RAOs for floating/submerged bodies.\n\n## Context\n\n- Capytaine 2.3.1 installed and verified on dev-secondary (2026-03-26)\n- Env: `/mnt/local-analysis/capytaine-env` (Python 3.12, scipy, numpy, vtk, meshio, xarray, matplotlib)\n- Sphere diffraction test passing — solver fully functional\n- Backlog item 999.2 in workspace-hub ROADMAP.md\n\n## Requirements\n\n- digitalmodel adapter: mesh import (meshio/STL/GDF formats), problem setup, result extraction\n- Standard calculations: diffraction forces, radiation coefficients (added mass + damping), RAOs\n- Validation against known benchmarks (OC3/OC4 spar, semi-sub, barge)\n- Standards traceability: DNV-RP-C205 (environmental conditions and loads)\n- Result export: xarray datasets, plots, summary tables\n\n## Notes\n\n- Consider Capytaine's Hierarchical Toeplitz matrices for large meshes\n- dev-secondary has OpenMP + NVIDIA T400 for parallelism\n- Follow digitalmodel calculation module pattern established in Phase 01 (manifest schema, CI validation)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/464","display_title":"Add hydrodynamic BEM analysis module (Capytaine)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/461","title":"Recover ship-dimensions template artifact from WRK-1339 Child E","issue_number":461,"body":"## Summary\nRecover or deliberately replace the missing Child E deliverable from `WRK-1339` so downstream ship-dimensions work can proceed inside `workspace-hub` without guessing schema or output paths.\n\n## Why\n`WRK-1380` is currently blocked because the expected upstream artifact is absent from the local `workspace-hub` checkout. Local recovery checked:\n- current `workspace-hub` files\n- `WRK-1339` asset folder\n- repo history\n- nearby sibling/child WRKs\n- existing GitHub issue discussion\n\nNone of those produced:\n- `generate-ship-dimension-template.py`, or\n- a generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\n\n## Required outcome\n1. Confirm whether `WRK-1339` ever produced either:\n   - `generate-ship-dimension-template.py`, or\n   - a generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\n2. If the artifact exists outside the current checkout, import it into the canonical `workspace-hub` location.\n3. If the artifact does not exist anywhere, define and create the replacement deliverable explicitly.\n4. Record the canonical path for:\n   - the generator or replacement script\n   - the generated `ship-dimensions.yaml` template\n5. Update downstream WRKs, especially `WRK-1380`, with the resolved paths.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- a canonical ship-dimensions template source exists in `workspace-hub`\n- the canonical output path for `ship-dimensions.yaml` is documented\n- `WRK-1380` can reference concrete local paths instead of unresolved blockers\n- no schema keys or output paths are invented ad hoc downstream\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/issues/461","display_title":"Recover ship-dimensions template artifact from WRK-1339 Child E"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
