{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":["vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","vamseeachanta/digitalmodel","vamseeachanta/assetutilities","vamseeachanta/worldenergydata","vamseeachanta/llm-wiki","vamseeachanta/assethold","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-website","vamseeachanta/aceengineer-strategy"],"query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:blocked\"","topn":50,"sort":"updated","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\", \"issue_number\": 2269, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\\n\\nPart of #1782.\\nPrimary reference: #25.\\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\\n\\nExpected deliverables:\\n- baseline docs\\n- run/validation entrypoints\\n- minimal smoke example\\n- troubleshooting guidance\\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\\n\\n## Notes\\nImplementation should prefer:\\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"display_title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\", \"issue_number\": 2402, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR\\u00d72 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model \\u00a77 \\u2014 **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model \\u00a73).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per \\u00a73 \\u2014 enforced and tested\\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s \\u2014 measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) \\u2014 live in their own issues.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"display_title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\", \"issue_number\": 26, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\\n\\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\\n- Explicitly exclude:\\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\", \"issue_number\": 25, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\\n\\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \\\"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\\\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\\n\\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\", \"issue_number\": 19, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\\n\\n## Context\\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\\n\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` \\u2014 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` \\u2014 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` \\u2014 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\\n\\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\\n\\n## Problem\\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\\n\\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\\n\\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\", \"issue_number\": 14, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\\n\\n## Source of record\\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\\n\\n## Why\\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\\n\\n## Scope\\nIn scope:\\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\\n- No source/staging cleanup.\\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152\", \"title\": \"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage\", \"issue_number\": 2152, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd the golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage.\\n\\n## Why\\nValidator and renderer work need stable example artifacts representing healthy, degraded, and invalid runs. Fixtures also flush out schema ambiguities early.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- add valid weekly-review run artifact fixtures for minimal, full, degraded, and multi-machine runs\\n- add invalid fixtures for missing keys, bad enums, bad timestamps, and malformed sections\\n- define expected validator outcomes for invalid cases\\n- document fixture naming and refresh rules\\n- wire fixtures into validator CI tests\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- valid and invalid fixture corpus\\n- expected validator outputs\\n- fixture README\\n- CI test usage\\n\\n## Parent\\n- Parent issues: #2146, #2147, #2089\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152\", \"display_title\": \"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation","issue_number":2269,"body":"## Summary\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\n\nPart of #1782.\nPrimary reference: #25.\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\n\n## Motivation\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\n\n## Scope\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\n\nExpected deliverables:\n- baseline docs\n- run/validation entrypoints\n- minimal smoke example\n- troubleshooting guidance\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\n\n## Notes\nImplementation should prefer:\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","display_title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)","issue_number":2402,"body":"## Context\n\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR×2 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\n\n## Problem\n\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model §7 — **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model §3).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per §3 — enforced and tested\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s — measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\n\n## Scope boundaries\n\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) — live in their own issues.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","display_title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion","issue_number":26,"body":"## Summary\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\n\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\n\n## Scope\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\n- Explicitly exclude:\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\n\n## Deliverables\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains","issue_number":25,"body":"## Summary\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\n\n## Why\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\n\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\n\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\n\n## Scope\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\n\n## Deliverables\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data","issue_number":19,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\n\n## Context\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\n\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` — 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` — 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` — 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\n\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\n\n## Problem\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\n\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\n\n## Scope\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\n\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements","issue_number":14,"body":"## Summary\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\n\n## Source of record\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\n\n## Why\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope:\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\n\nOut of scope:\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\n- No source/staging cleanup.\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\n\n## Related\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152","title":"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage","issue_number":2152,"body":"## Summary\nAdd the golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage.\n\n## Why\nValidator and renderer work need stable example artifacts representing healthy, degraded, and invalid runs. Fixtures also flush out schema ambiguities early.\n\n## Scope\n- add valid weekly-review run artifact fixtures for minimal, full, degraded, and multi-machine runs\n- add invalid fixtures for missing keys, bad enums, bad timestamps, and malformed sections\n- define expected validator outcomes for invalid cases\n- document fixture naming and refresh rules\n- wire fixtures into validator CI tests\n\n## Deliverables\n- valid and invalid fixture corpus\n- expected validator outputs\n- fixture README\n- CI test usage\n\n## Parent\n- Parent issues: #2146, #2147, #2089\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152","display_title":"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
