s `pushed_at` re-fetched at write time via `gh api repos/anthropics/financial-services --jq '.pushed_at'`. (Note: value drifted from 2026-05-07T21:10:05Z at plan-draft to 2026-05-09T11:28:47Z now \\u2014 verifies the \\\"re-fetch at write time\\\" approach.) |\\n| 4. Slug convention unhandled (org-as-author) | MINOR | Slug changed from `anthropics-2026-financial-services-managed-agents.md` to `2026-05-09-anthropics-financial-services.md` (date-first per Pattern B precedent `2026-04-17-hn-cadquery.md`). Dropped redundant \\\"managed-agents\\\" qualifier. |\\n| 5. Hermes mitigation underspecified | BLOCKER | New \\\"Hermes Cleanup Mitigation\\\" section: explicit `pgrep` detection trigger, branch fallback name (`ingest/2026-05-09-anthropics-financial-services`), no-push policy, approval-gate unchanged. |\\n| 6. Firewall-language verbatim claim unverifiable | BLOCKER | Exact phrase pinned in plan body and pasted into the Log update template. Acceptance criterion now reads \\\"byte-equal match against this phrase.\\\" |\\n| 7. Past-tense / uncommitted-spec dependency | MINOR | Issue body now states \\\"this issue body is the canonical plan; the on-disk spec is reference material for human reviewers, not implementation input.\\\" |\\n\\n**Re-review:** dispatching Codex round-2 against the revised body.\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"name\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4\", \"id\": 23155845}, \"id\": 4414417561, \"pull_request_review_id\": null, \"in_reply_to_id\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"review\": null, \"side\": null, \"line\": null, \"start_line\": null, \"path\": null, \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Revision 2 \\u2014 Codex MAJOR findings addressed</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Round-1 Codex review returned MAJOR with 7 findings, 5 blockers. Revision-2 maps:</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Finding</th>\\n<th>Severity</th>\\n<th>Resolution</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>1. Header pluralization not in plan; counter drift visible (header \\\"13 pages\\\" vs frontmatter <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">source_count: 16</code>)</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>Live verification: actual file count is <strong>23</strong> (deflated phantoms). Plan now explicitly reconciles to ground-truth: frontmatter <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">source_count: 16\\u219224</code>, header <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">(13 pages)\\u2192(24 pages)</code>. Marine-eng \\\"+1-by-convention\\\" rule cited but rejected here because it preserves <em>inflation</em>; deflation has no upstream-convention reason to keep.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>2. Frontmatter schema invented (no peer match)</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>Verified two peer patterns: A (internal repo-docs) uses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">source_path</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">source_type</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ingested</code>; B (external sources, e.g., <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">2026-04-17-hn-cadquery.md</code>) uses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sources:</code> scalar list + <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">domain: engineering</code>. New page now follows Pattern B verbatim. Dropped invented <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">license</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">observed_pushed_at</code> keys.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>3. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">observed_pushed_at</code> unpinned</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>Mooted by Finding 2 fix (no longer in frontmatter). Body prose cites <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">pushed_at</code> re-fetched at write time via <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">gh api repos/anthropics/financial-services --jq '.pushed_at'</code>. (Note: value drifted from 2026-05-07T21:10:05Z at plan-draft to 2026-05-09T11:28:47Z now \\u2014 verifies the \\\"re-fetch at write time\\\" approach.)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>4. Slug convention unhandled (org-as-author)</td>\\n<td>MINOR</td>\\n<td>Slug changed from <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">anthropics-2026-financial-services-managed-agents.md</code> to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">2026-05-09-anthropics-financial-services.md</code> (date-first per Pattern B precedent <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">2026-04-17-hn-cadquery.md</code>). Dropped redundant \\\"managed-agents\\\" qualifier.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>5. Hermes mitigation underspecified</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>New \\\"Hermes Cleanup Mitigation\\\" section: explicit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">pgrep</code> detection trigger, branch fallback name (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ingest/2026-05-09-anthropics-financial-services</code>), no-push policy, approval-gate unchanged.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>6. Firewall-language verbatim claim unverifiable</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>Exact phrase pinned in plan body and pasted into the Log update template. Acceptance criterion now reads \\\"byte-equal match against this phrase.\\\"</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>7. Past-tense / uncommitted-spec dependency</td>\\n<td>MINOR</td>\\n<td>Issue body now states \\\"this issue body is the canonical plan; the on-disk spec is reference material for human reviewers, not implementation input.\\\"</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Re-review:</strong> dispatching Codex round-2 against the revised body.</p>\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2659#issuecomment-4414428071\", \"body\": \"## Revision 3 \\u2014 Codex round-2 stale-count defect addressed\\n\\nRound-2 review confirmed all 7 round-1 findings RESOLVED but flagged 1 new defect:\\n\\n| Round-2 finding | Severity | Resolution in revision-3 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Stale-count fragility \\u2014 plan hardcoded `source_count: 24` based on plan-draft observation; if another ingest lands before implementation, value is wrong | BLOCKER | Replaced frozen `24` with a write-time rule. Acceptance criterion now reads \\\"at write time, N = count(sources/*.md before staging); set source_count and header to N+1.\\\" Static `24` retained as a baseline expectation only \\u2014 implementing agent must re-count and surface divergence. |\\n\\nRound-3 dispatch incoming. Per memory `feedback_codex_sustained_major_loop.md`, if round-3 also returns MAJOR I will surface the consensus-vs-minority decision rather than continuing to cycle.\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"name\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4\", \"id\": 23155845}, \"id\": 4414428071, \"pull_request_review_id\": null, \"in_reply_to_id\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"review\": null, \"side\": null, \"line\": null, \"start_line\": null, \"path\": null, \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Revision 3 \\u2014 Codex round-2 stale-count defect addressed</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Round-2 review confirmed all 7 round-1 findings RESOLVED but flagged 1 new defect:</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Round-2 finding</th>\\n<th>Severity</th>\\n<th>Resolution in revision-3</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Stale-count fragility \\u2014 plan hardcoded <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">source_count: 24</code> based on plan-draft observation; if another ingest lands before implementation, value is wrong</td>\\n<td>BLOCKER</td>\\n<td>Replaced frozen <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">24</code> with a write-time rule. Acceptance criterion now reads \\\"at write time, N = count(sources/*.md before staging); set source_count and header to N+1.\\\" Static <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">24</code> retained as a baseline expectation only \\u2014 implementing agent must re-count and surface divergence.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Round-3 dispatch incoming. Per memory <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">feedback_codex_sustained_major_loop.md</code>, if round-3 also returns MAJOR I will surface the consensus-vs-minority decision rather than continuing to cycle.</p>\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2659#issuecomment-4414433089\", \"body\": \"## Round-3: APPROVE \\u2014 plan is approval-ready\\n\\nCodex round-3 returned **APPROVE** with no blockers. Artifact: `scripts/review/results/2026-05-09-plan-2659-codex-r3.md`.\\n\\n**Adversarial-review trail:**\\n- Round 1: MAJOR (7 findings, 5 blockers) \\u2192 revision-2\\n- Round 2: MAJOR (round-1 all RESOLVED + 1 new stale-count defect) \\u2192 revision-3\\n- Round 3: APPROVE (round-2 RESOLVED, no regression, no new blockers)\\n\\nThree minor observations from round-3, none requiring further revision:\\n1. `implementation comment` could be tightened to \\\"GitHub issue implementation comment\\\" (currently sufficiently actionable).\\n2. `gh api` snippet doesn't handle missing `sources/` directory (not a real risk; directory exists with 23 files).\\n3. No acceptance-criteria internal contradictions.\\n\\n**Open commit decision (separate from plan-approval):** the review artifacts at `scripts/review/results/2026-05-09-plan-2659-codex.md`, `*-r2.md`, `*-r3.md` are currently uncommitted on workspace-hub local. Codex round-3 noted that the artifact links in the issue body return GitHub 404 for that reason. Whether to commit them now (and on what branch given Hermes is active) is your call \\u2014 independent of the implementation plan-approval gate.\\n\\n**Approval gate status:** issue is at `status:plan-review`. Implementation will not begin until the user applies `status:plan-approved` AND creates `.planning/plan-approved/2659.md`. The implementing agent will not self-approve.\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"name\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4\", \"id\": 23155845}, \"id\": 4414433089, \"pull_request_review_id\": null, \"in_reply_to_id\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"review\": null, \"side\": null, \"line\": null, \"start_line\": null, \"path\": null, \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Round-3: APPROVE \\u2014 plan is approval-ready</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Codex round-3 returned <strong>APPROVE</strong> with no blockers. Artifact: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scripts/review/results/2026-05-09-plan-2659-codex-r3.md</code>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Adversarial-review trail:</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Round 1: MAJOR (7 findings, 5 blockers) \\u2192 revision-2</li>\\n<li>Round 2: MAJOR (round-1 all RESOLVED + 1 new stale-count defect) \\u2192 revision-3</li>\\n<li>Round 3: APPROVE (round-2 RESOLVED, no regression, no new blockers)</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Three minor observations from round-3, none requiring further revision:</p>\\n<ol dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">implementation comment</code> could be tightened to \\\"GitHub issue implementation comment\\\" (currently sufficiently actionable).</li>\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">gh api</code> snippet doesn't handle missing <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sources/</code> directory (not a real risk; directory exists with 23 files).</li>\\n<li>No acceptance-criteria internal contradictions.</li>\\n</ol>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Open commit decision (separate from plan-approval):</strong> the review artifacts at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scripts/review/results/2026-05-09-plan-2659-codex.md</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">*-r2.md</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">*-r3.md</code> are currently uncommitted on workspace-hub local. Codex round-3 noted that the artifact links in the issue body return GitHub 404 for that reason. Whether to commit them now (and on what branch given Hermes is active) is your call \\u2014 independent of the implementation plan-approval gate.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Approval gate status:</strong> issue is at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">status:plan-review</code>. Implementation will not begin until the user applies <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">status:plan-approved</code> AND creates <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.planning/plan-approved/2659.md</code>. The implementing agent will not self-approve.</p>\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2659#issuecomment-4415300111\", \"body\": \"## Implementation complete \\u2014 commit `f5e533d6` on llm-wiki/main (push deferred)\\n\\nPlan executed in full per revision-3 of the issue body. Below is the implementation record per the plan's acceptance criterion (write-time counter rule + branch decision + deferred push).\\n\\n### Counter rule (write-time computation)\\n\\n- Observed `N` at write time: **23** (verified via `gh api repos/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/contents/wikis/engineering/wiki/sources --jq '[.[] | select(.name | endswith(\\\".md\\\"))] | length'`)\\n- Resolved `N+1`: **24**\\n- Plan baseline expectation was `24` \\u2014 matches; no divergence to surface.\\n- Post-write file count in `wikis/engineering/wiki/sources/`: **24** (verified locally via `ls *.md | wc -l`).\\n\\n### Branch decision (Hermes mitigation)\\n\\n- Default path applied: **commit on `llm-wiki/main`**.\\n- Pre-commit `pgrep` flagged parallel git ops, but verification showed the ops were in **workspace-hub** (auto-sync + an unrelated provenance-commit session), not in llm-wiki. The plan's mitigation is scoped to llm-wiki collisions, so the false-positive was overridden after verification.\\n- Working tree clean post-commit; reflog shows no silent revert.\\n\\n### Files changed (3 paths, 62 insertions / 4 deletions)\\n\\n| Path | Operation |\\n|---|---|\\n| `wikis/engineering/wiki/sources/2026-05-09-anthropics-financial-services.md` | new (50 lines, Pattern B frontmatter) |\\n| `wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md` | frontmatter `page_count 107\\u2192108`, `source_count 16\\u219224`, `last_updated 2026-05-06\\u21922026-05-09`; he