er parallel-session contention; main session will push in serialization phase).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>v2 revision items from Claude:</strong></p>\\n<ol dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><strong>Forbidden-path scope (P1):</strong> plan proposes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scripts/knowledge/run-batch-pack-1.py</code> runner + <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tests/**</code> test module, both conflicting with batch-pack spec \\u00a73.1 forbidden-paths clause. Either cite a spec exemption, relocate the artifacts, or file an amendment micro-issue.</li>\\n<li>Enumerate classifier keyword sets (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">MARINE_TAGS</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NAVAL_ARCH_TAGS</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NAVAL_HOSTS</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">MARINE_TERMS</code>) \\u2014 currently underspecified.</li>\\n<li>Attach a dry-run count of how many of the 40 entries (31 data_api + 9 standard_portal) land as sufficient vs insufficient under the 120-char threshold.</li>\\n<li>Add an <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">unclassifiable</code> / <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">maritime-law</code> escape hatch, or explicit justification for accepting IMO into engineering wiki.</li>\\n<li>Tighten <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">noaa-ndbc</code> fixture reference.</li>\\n</ol>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Authoritative count verified: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">online-resource-registry.yaml</code> has exactly 40 entries matching <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">type in {data_api, standard_portal}</code>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not eligible for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">status:plan-review</code> until v2 addresses P1-1 + other findings. User approval required.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Artifacts: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2364-{claude,codex,gemini}.md</code></p>\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543164\", \"body\": \"## v2 adversarial review \\u2014 DOUBLE MAJOR\\n\\nv2 pushed at `5db2c0cbf` on branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1`. Fresh cross-review against fixed infra.\\n\\n### Verdicts\\n| Provider | Verdict |\\n|---|---|\\n| Claude | **MAJOR** (2 P2s + 7 P3s) |\\n| Gemini | **MAJOR** (1 P1) |\\n| Codex | UNAVAILABLE (#2479) |\\n\\n### v2 resolved r1 P1s + most P2s\\n- **Forbidden-path**: clause quoted verbatim (`config/**`, `.claude/**`, `tests/**`, `scripts/**`). Runner relocated to `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner.py`; tests to `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py`.\\n- **Planner rationalization deleted.**\\n- **Domain classifier**: all 40 entries have `tags: None` \\u2014 tag-based rules dead; v2 uses host-regex + notes-keywords only (enumerated).\\n- **120-char dry-run**: 25/40 pass, 15/40 insufficient \\u2014 split reasonable.\\n- **`noaa-ndbc` \\u2192 `noaa_ndbc`**: fixture id corrected (hyphen \\u2192 underscore, matching registry).\\n- **Maritime-law**: added as 4th allowed `target_wiki_domain` with `out-of-scope-for-promotion: true`.\\n\\n### Gemini's v2 finding (NEW P1)\\n\\n**Regex-based YAML patching is fragile (data-corruption risk).** v2 dropped `ruamel.yaml` (not in `pyproject.toml`) and substituted 'scoped two-key text-patch with structural-diff verification'. Gemini flags: anchored regex on YAML will corrupt the file if there are commented lines, multi-line strings, or unexpected whitespace. **Surgical fix:** two options \\u2014 (a) ADD `ruamel.yaml` as a new dep (small, standard lib for round-trip YAML), OR (b) write a companion `online-resource-registry.processed.yaml` overlay file that doesn't require in-place patching of the canonical registry.\\n\\n### Claude's v2 findings\\n\\n1. **[P2] Registry write-back idempotency tested only at report layer.** Anchored regex appends a second `processed: true` on re-run unless runner pre-checks. **Fix:** pre-write guard + byte-diff AC test.\\n2. **[P2] Wall-clock test flakes on CI.** `test_duplicate_check_wall_clock_under_budget` asserts <30s over 19,191 pages \\u2014 slow runners will flake. **Fix:** gate behind `@pytest.mark.perf` or env var.\\n3. **[P2] Test sys.path for hyphenated runner.** Tests at `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py` must import runner at hyphenated `batch-pack-1-runner.py`. Hyphen-path pattern AGAIN \\u2014 see `feedback_llm_wiki_hyphen_module_path_pattern`. **Fix:** rename to underscore OR specify `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` mechanism.\\n\\n### Claude P3s\\n- Registry patch atomicity (temp+rename)\\n- `processed_date` timezone unspecified (UTC+iso format needed)\\n- Classifier-precedence tests incomplete\\n- Stub frontmatter schema not enumerated\\n- Deliverable vs AC disagree on maritime-law counting\\n- Forbidden-path guard regex could be tightened\\n\\n### Next action\\n**v3 needed** \\u2014 Gemini's P1 (regex YAML) is the blocker; Claude's P2s are surgical. Recommend adding `ruamel.yaml` as a dep + keeping the structural verification approach.\\n\\nArtifacts: `scripts/review/results/2026042?T*-plan-2364-v2.md-plan-*.md`\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"name\": \"vamseeachanta\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4\", \"id\": 23155845}, \"id\": 4383543164, \"pull_request_review_id\": null, \"in_reply_to_id\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"review\": null, \"side\": null, \"line\": null, \"start_line\": null, \"path\": null, \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">v2 adversarial review \\u2014 DOUBLE MAJOR</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">v2 pushed at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">5db2c0cbf</code> on branch <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1</code>. Fresh cross-review against fixed infra.</p>\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Verdicts</h3>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Provider</th>\\n<th>Verdict</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Claude</td>\\n<td><strong>MAJOR</strong> (2 P2s + 7 P3s)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Gemini