": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"title\": \"vamseeachanta/llm-wiki Issue #25 comments\", \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"display_title\": \"vamseeachanta/llm-wiki Issue #25 comments\"}"}],"structured_content":{"comments":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543117","body":"R1 cross-review complete (2026-04-23):\n- **Claude: MAJOR** — 9 findings (P1 blockers include forbidden-path scope conflict)\n- **Codex: UNAVAILABLE** — `submit-to-codex.sh` stdin-hang (exit 124, same vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2406 regression hitting all plans in this batch)\n- **Gemini: UNAVAILABLE** — NO_OUTPUT response\n- **Net:** MAJOR (needs-revision; only 1 of 3 reviewers produced a verdict — signal is thin)\n\nPlan drafted: `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md`. Committed locally on `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` @ `882b834d8` but NOT pushed (pre-push hook stuck under parallel-session contention; main session will push in serialization phase).\n\n**v2 revision items from Claude:**\n1. **Forbidden-path scope (P1):** plan proposes `scripts/knowledge/run-batch-pack-1.py` runner + `tests/**` test module, both conflicting with batch-pack spec §3.1 forbidden-paths clause. Either cite a spec exemption, relocate the artifacts, or file an amendment micro-issue.\n2. Enumerate classifier keyword sets (`MARINE_TAGS`, `NAVAL_ARCH_TAGS`, `NAVAL_HOSTS`, `MARINE_TERMS`) — currently underspecified.\n3. Attach a dry-run count of how many of the 40 entries (31 data_api + 9 standard_portal) land as sufficient vs insufficient under the 120-char threshold.\n4. Add an `unclassifiable` / `maritime-law` escape hatch, or explicit justification for accepting IMO into engineering wiki.\n5. Tighten `noaa-ndbc` fixture reference.\n\nAuthoritative count verified: `online-resource-registry.yaml` has exactly 40 entries matching `type in {data_api, standard_portal}`.\n\nNot eligible for `status:plan-review` until v2 addresses P1-1 + other findings. User approval required.\n\nArtifacts: `scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2364-{claude,codex,gemini}.md`\n","user":{"login":"vamseeachanta","name":"vamseeachanta","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4","id":23155845},"id":4383543117,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<p dir=\"auto\">R1 cross-review complete (2026-04-23):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Claude: MAJOR</strong> — 9 findings (P1 blockers include forbidden-path scope conflict)</li>\n<li><strong>Codex: UNAVAILABLE</strong> — <code class=\"notranslate\">submit-to-codex.sh</code> stdin-hang (exit 124, same <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4297731336\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2406\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2406/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2406\">vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2406</a> regression hitting all plans in this batch)</li>\n<li><strong>Gemini: UNAVAILABLE</strong> — NO_OUTPUT response</li>\n<li><strong>Net:</strong> MAJOR (needs-revision; only 1 of 3 reviewers produced a verdict — signal is thin)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Plan drafted: <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md</code>. Committed locally on <code class=\"notranslate\">plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1</code> @ <code class=\"notranslate\">882b834d8</code> but NOT pushed (pre-push hook stuck under parallel-session contention; main session will push in serialization phase).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>v2 revision items from Claude:</strong></p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Forbidden-path scope (P1):</strong> plan proposes <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/knowledge/run-batch-pack-1.py</code> runner + <code class=\"notranslate\">tests/**</code> test module, both conflicting with batch-pack spec §3.1 forbidden-paths clause. Either cite a spec exemption, relocate the artifacts, or file an amendment micro-issue.</li>\n<li>Enumerate classifier keyword sets (<code class=\"notranslate\">MARINE_TAGS</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">NAVAL_ARCH_TAGS</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">NAVAL_HOSTS</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">MARINE_TERMS</code>) — currently underspecified.</li>\n<li>Attach a dry-run count of how many of the 40 entries (31 data_api + 9 standard_portal) land as sufficient vs insufficient under the 120-char threshold.</li>\n<li>Add an <code class=\"notranslate\">unclassifiable</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">maritime-law</code> escape hatch, or explicit justification for accepting IMO into engineering wiki.</li>\n<li>Tighten <code class=\"notranslate\">noaa-ndbc</code> fixture reference.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Authoritative count verified: <code class=\"notranslate\">online-resource-registry.yaml</code> has exactly 40 entries matching <code class=\"notranslate\">type in {data_api, standard_portal}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not eligible for <code class=\"notranslate\">status:plan-review</code> until v2 addresses P1-1 + other findings. User approval required.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Artifacts: <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2364-{claude,codex,gemini}.md</code></p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543164","body":"## v2 adversarial review — DOUBLE MAJOR\n\nv2 pushed at `5db2c0cbf` on branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1`. Fresh cross-review against fixed infra.\n\n### Verdicts\n| Provider | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Claude | **MAJOR** (2 P2s + 7 P3s) |\n| Gemini | **MAJOR** (1 P1) |\n| Codex | UNAVAILABLE (#2479) |\n\n### v2 resolved r1 P1s + most P2s\n- **Forbidden-path**: clause quoted verbatim (`config/**`, `.claude/**`, `tests/**`, `scripts/**`). Runner relocated to `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner.py`; tests to `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py`.\n- **Planner rationalization deleted.**\n- **Domain classifier**: all 40 entries have `tags: None` — tag-based rules dead; v2 uses host-regex + notes-keywords only (enumerated).\n- **120-char dry-run**: 25/40 pass, 15/40 insufficient — split reasonable.\n- **`noaa-ndbc` → `noaa_ndbc`**: fixture id corrected (hyphen → underscore, matching registry).\n- **Maritime-law**: added as 4th allowed `target_wiki_domain` with `out-of-scope-for-promotion: true`.\n\n### Gemini's v2 finding (NEW P1)\n\n**Regex-based YAML patching is fragile (data-corruption risk).** v2 dropped `ruamel.yaml` (not in `pyproject.toml`) and substituted 'scoped two-key text-patch with structural-diff verification'. Gemini flags: anchored regex on YAML will corrupt the file if there are commented lines, multi-line strings, or unexpected whitespace. **Surgical fix:** two options — (a) ADD `ruamel.yaml` as a new dep (small, standard lib for round-trip YAML), OR (b) write a companion `online-resource-registry.processed.yaml` overlay file that doesn't require in-place patching of the canonical registry.\n\n### Claude's v2 findings\n\n1. **[P2] Registry write-back idempotency tested only at report layer.** Anchored regex appends a second `processed: true` on re-run unless runner pre-checks. **Fix:** pre-write guard + byte-diff AC test.\n2. **[P2] Wall-clock test flakes on CI.** `test_duplicate_check_wall_clock_under_budget` asserts <30s over 19,191 pages — slow runners will flake. **Fix:** gate behind `@pytest.mark.perf` or env var.\n3. **[P2] Test sys.path for hyphenated runner.** Tests at `docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py` must import runner at hyphenated `batch-pack-1-runner.py`. Hyphen-path pattern AGAIN — see `feedback_llm_wiki_hyphen_module_path_pattern`. **Fix:** rename to underscore OR specify `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` mechanism.\n\n### Claude P3s\n- Registry patch atomicity (temp+rename)\n- `processed_date` timezone unspecified (UTC+iso format needed)\n- Classifier-precedence tests incomplete\n- Stub frontmatter schema not enumerated\n- Deliverable vs AC disagree on maritime-law counting\n- Forbidden-path guard regex could be tightened\n\n### Next action\n**v3 needed** — Gemini's P1 (regex YAML) is the blocker; Claude's P2s are surgical. Recommend adding `ruamel.yaml` as a dep + keeping the structural verification approach.\n\nArtifacts: `scripts/review/results/2026042?T*-plan-2364-v2.md-plan-*.md`","user":{"login":"vamseeachanta","name":"vamseeachanta","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4","id":23155845},"id":4383543164,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">v2 adversarial review — DOUBLE MAJOR</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">v2 pushed at <code class=\"notranslate\">5db2c0cbf</code> on branch <code class=\"notranslate\">plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1</code>. Fresh cross-review against fixed infra.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Verdicts</h3>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Provider</th>\n<th>Verdict</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Claude</td>\n<td><strong>MAJOR</strong> (2 P2s + 7 P3s)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gemini</td>\n<td><strong>MAJOR</strong> (1 P1)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Codex</td>\n<td>UNAVAILABLE (#2479)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">v2 resolved r1 P1s + most P2s</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Forbidden-path</strong>: clause quoted verbatim (<code class=\"notranslate\">config/**</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">.claude/**</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">tests/**</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/**</code>). Runner relocated to <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner.py</code>; tests to <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Planner rationalization deleted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Domain classifier</strong>: all 40 entries have <code class=\"notranslate\">tags: None</code> — tag-based rules dead; v2 uses host-regex + notes-keywords only (enumerated).</li>\n<li><strong>120-char dry-run</strong>: 25/40 pass, 15/40 insufficient — split reasonable.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"notranslate\">noaa-ndbc</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">noaa_ndbc</code></strong>: fixture id corrected (hyphen → underscore, matching registry).</li>\n<li><strong>Maritime-law</strong>: added as 4th allowed <code class=\"notranslate\">target_wiki_domain</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">out-of-scope-for-promotion: true</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Gemini's v2 finding (NEW P1)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Regex-based YAML patching is fragile (data-corruption risk).</strong> v2 dropped <code class=\"notranslate\">ruamel.yaml</code> (not in <code class=\"notranslate\">pyproject.toml</code>) and substituted 'scoped two-key text-patch with structural-diff verification'. Gemini flags: anchored regex on YAML will corrupt the file if there are commented lines, multi-line strings, or unexpected whitespace. <strong>Surgical fix:</strong> two options — (a) ADD <code class=\"notranslate\">ruamel.yaml</code> as a new dep (small, standard lib for round-trip YAML), OR (b) write a companion <code class=\"notranslate\">online-resource-registry.processed.yaml</code> overlay file that doesn't require in-place patching of the canonical registry.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Claude's v2 findings</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>[P2] Registry write-back idempotency tested only at report layer.</strong> Anchored regex appends a second <code class=\"notranslate\">processed: true</code> on re-run unless runner pre-checks. <strong>Fix:</strong> pre-write guard + byte-diff AC test.</li>\n<li><strong>[P2] Wall-clock test flakes on CI.</strong> <code class=\"notranslate\">test_duplicate_check_wall_clock_under_budget</code> asserts &lt;30s over 19,191 pages — slow runners will flake. <strong>Fix:</strong> gate behind <code class=\"notranslate\">@pytest.mark.perf</code> or env var.</li>\n<li><strong>[P2] Test sys.path for hyphenated runner.</strong> Tests at <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/reports/batch-pack-1-runner-tests.py</code> must import runner at hyphenated <code class=\"notranslate\">batch-pack-1-runner.py</code>. Hyphen-path pattern AGAIN — see <code class=\"notranslate\">feedback_llm_wiki_hyphen_module_path_pattern</code>. <strong>Fix:</strong> rename to underscore OR specify <code class=\"notranslate\">importlib.util.spec_from_file_location</code> mechanism.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Claude P3s</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Registry patch atomicity (temp+rename)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">processed_date</code> timezone unspecified (UTC+iso format needed)</li>\n<li>Classifier-precedence tests incomplete</li>\n<li>Stub frontmatter schema not enumerated</li>\n<li>Deliverable vs AC disagree on maritime-law counting</li>\n<li>Forbidden-path guard regex could be tightened</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Next action</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>v3 needed</strong> — Gemini's P1 (regex YAML) is the blocker; Claude's P2s are surgical. Recommend adding <code class=\"notranslate\">ruamel.yaml</code> as a dep + keeping the structural verification approach.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Artifacts: <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/review/results/2026042?T*-plan-2364-v2.md-plan-*.md</code></p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543220","body":"## v3 drafted — `de71883f0` (overlay file pivot per user decision)\n\nBranch: `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` @ `de71883f0`\nPlan path: `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md`\n\n**User decision (2026-04-25):** pivot to overlay file (option b) over adding ruamel.yaml dep (option a). Rationale: no in-place mutation, no new dep, fits existing project pattern (`provider-routing-scorecard.json` is regenerated, not patched).\n\n**Overlay design:**\n- Source `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` stays read-only\n- Runner emits sibling `online-resource-registry.processed.yaml` with `schema_version`, `generated_at`, `source_registry_sha256`, per-entry `processed/processed_date/source_checksum/target_wiki_domain`\n- Atomic write via `os.replace`\n- Determinism: `processed[]` sorted by `id`; `processed_date` carried forward so reruns are byte-identical (after stripping top-level `generated_at`)\n- Consumer fallback: missing overlay → return None + log warning; checksum mismatch → consult overlay best-effort\n- **Eliminates Gemini r2 P1 entirely** (no regex on YAML, no in-place mutation, no new dep)\n\n**r2 items addressed (top 5):**\n- Claude P2-1 idempotency-only-at-report-layer → `test_overlay_byte_identical_across_reruns` asserts file-layer sha256 equality\n- Claude P2-2 wall-clock test flakiness → `@pytest.mark.perf` opt-in via `RUN_PERF_TESTS=1`\n- Claude P2-3 hyphen-path import smell → renamed to `batch_pack_1_runner.py` + `_tests.py` (underscore); `docs/reports/conftest.py` shim\n- Claude P3 deliverable-vs-AC disagreement → three-bucket model: `sufficient(23) + insufficient(15) + catalog_only(2) == 40`\n- Gemini P3 shell pipeline → pure-Python `pathlib.Path.rglob`\n\nForward-adopts vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 v3 `code_id`/`publisher`/`revision` frontmatter when extractable.\n\nHyphen-path grep: 0 matches.\n\nCross-review of v3 dispatching.","user":{"login":"vamseeachanta","name":"vamseeachanta","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4","id":23155845},"id":4383543220,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">v3 drafted — <code class=\"notranslate\">de71883f0</code> (overlay file pivot per user decision)</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Branch: <code class=\"notranslate\">plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1</code> @ <code class=\"notranslate\">de71883f0</code><br>\nPlan path: <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>User decision (2026-04-25):</strong> pivot to overlay file (option b) over adding ruamel.yaml dep (option a). Rationale: no in-place mutation, no new dep, fits existing project pattern (<code class=\"notranslate\">provider-routing-scorecard.json</code> is regenerated, not patched).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Overlay design:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Source <code class=\"notranslate\">data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml</code> stays read-only</li>\n<li>Runner emits sibling <code class=\"notranslate\">online-resource-registry.processed.yaml</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">schema_version</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generated_at</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">source_registry_sha256</code>, per-entry <code class=\"notranslate\">processed/processed_date/source_checksum/target_wiki_domain</code></li>\n<li>Atomic write via <code class=\"notranslate\">os.replace</code></li>\n<li>Determinism: <code class=\"notranslate\">processed[]</code> sorted by <code class=\"notranslate\">id</code>; <code class=\"notranslate\">processed_date</code> carried forward so reruns are byte-identical (after stripping top-level <code class=\"notranslate\">generated_at</code>)</li>\n<li>Consumer fallback: missing overlay → return None + log warning; checksum mismatch → consult overlay best-effort</li>\n<li><strong>Eliminates Gemini r2 P1 entirely</strong> (no regex on YAML, no in-place mutation, no new dep)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>r2 items addressed (top 5):</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Claude P2-1 idempotency-only-at-report-layer → <code class=\"notranslate\">test_overlay_byte_identical_across_reruns</code> asserts file-layer sha256 equality</li>\n<li>Claude P2-2 wall-clock test flakiness → <code class=\"notranslate\">@pytest.mark.perf</code> opt-in via <code class=\"notranslate\">RUN_PERF_TESTS=1</code></li>\n<li>Claude P2-3 hyphen-path import smell → renamed to <code class=\"notranslate\">batch_pack_1_runner.py</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">_tests.py</code> (underscore); <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/reports/conftest.py</code> shim</li>\n<li>Claude P3 deliverable-vs-AC disagreement → three-bucket model: <code class=\"notranslate\">sufficient(23) + insufficient(15) + catalog_only(2) == 40</code></li>\n<li>Gemini P3 shell pipeline → pure-Python <code class=\"notranslate\">pathlib.Path.rglob</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Forward-adopts <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4318785728\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471\">vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471</a> v3 <code class=\"notranslate\">code_id</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">publisher</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">revision</code> frontmatter when extractable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hyphen-path grep: 0 matches.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Cross-review of v3 dispatching.</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543256","body":"## Cross-review v3 — `de71883f0`\n\n**Claude:** **MAJOR** — top: P2 partition/classify ordering ambiguity (`partition_three_bucket` calls `classify_domain` BEFORE? maritime-law detection unclear); P2 PyYAML availability not attested; P2 `optional_2471_fields` extraction heuristic unspecified; P2 stale-overlay consumer needs `is_stale` signal.\n**Gemini:** **MAJOR** — **P1: `yaml` is NOT in Python stdlib.** Plan claims 'no new dependencies' + 'stdlib yaml' but `import yaml` requires PyYAML. P3: missing CLAUDE.md paths in attestation; P3 quoted-source_id false-negative in duplicate check.\n**Codex:** UNAVAILABLE (#2479)\n\n**Cross-provider convergence:** Both flagged the PyYAML/stdlib false-claim — high-signal defect, must be addressed in v4.\n\nResult files:\n- `scripts/review/results/20260425T092133Z-2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md-plan-claude.md`\n- `scripts/review/results/20260425T093644Z-2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md-plan-gemini.md`","user":{"login":"vamseeachanta","name":"vamseeachanta","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4","id":23155845},"id":4383543256,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">Cross-review v3 — <code class=\"notranslate\">de71883f0</code></h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Claude:</strong> <strong>MAJOR</strong> — top: P2 partition/classify ordering ambiguity (<code class=\"notranslate\">partition_three_bucket</code> calls <code class=\"notranslate\">classify_domain</code> BEFORE? maritime-law detection unclear); P2 PyYAML availability not attested; P2 <code class=\"notranslate\">optional_2471_fields</code> extraction heuristic unspecified; P2 stale-overlay consumer needs <code class=\"notranslate\">is_stale</code> signal.<br>\n<strong>Gemini:</strong> <strong>MAJOR</strong> — <strong>P1: <code class=\"notranslate\">yaml</code> is NOT in Python stdlib.</strong> Plan claims 'no new dependencies' + 'stdlib yaml' but <code class=\"notranslate\">import yaml</code> requires PyYAML. P3: missing CLAUDE.md paths in attestation; P3 quoted-source_id false-negative in duplicate check.<br>\n<strong>Codex:</strong> UNAVAILABLE (#2479)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Cross-provider convergence:</strong> Both flagged the PyYAML/stdlib false-claim — high-signal defect, must be addressed in v4.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Result files:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/review/results/20260425T092133Z-2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md-plan-claude.md</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/review/results/20260425T093644Z-2026-04-23-issue-2364-batch-pack-1-api-standards-portal-promotion.md-plan-gemini.md</code></li>\n</ul>"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543277","body":"## v4 drafted — `5c6e6bed5` (PyYAML attestation, classify-before-partition, code_id heuristic, is_stale)\n\nBranch: `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` @ `5c6e6bed5`\n\n**Addresses cross-converged r3 MAJOR (Claude+Gemini both):**\n- **Gemini P1 (yaml stdlib false-claim) RESOLVED**: PyYAML 6.0.3 verified as direct dep — `pyproject.toml` has both `\"pyyaml>=6.0\"` AND `\"PyYAML>=6.0\"`; `uv pip list` confirms. Plan body changes 'stdlib yaml' → 'yaml.safe_load/safe_dump from PyYAML 6.0+ (already in pyproject.toml)'. New test `test_pyyaml_is_a_direct_dep` + AC.\n- **Claude P2 partition/classify ordering**: `classify_domain` runs FIRST per entry, then `partition_three_bucket` consumes (entry, domain) tuples. Maritime-law detection inside `classify_domain`. 2 new tests.\n- **Claude P2 optional_2471_fields heuristic**: `KNOWN_PUBLISHERS=(DNV,API,IMO,CSA,OCIMF,ABS)` + `PUBLISHER_RE`/`CODE_ID_RE`/`REVISION_RE`; gating requires both code_id AND publisher. Positive fixture: 'DNV-OS-E301 Rev 2024-04 mooring' → `{code_id:DNV-OS-E301, publisher:DNV, revision:2024-04}`. Negative: NOAA tide-gauge → `{}` (keys absent).\n- **Claude P2 stale-overlay signal**: consumer signature → `Tuple[Optional[ProcessedRecord], bool]`. `is_stale=True` iff source_registry_sha256 mismatches.\n- **Gemini P3 CLAUDE.md path reconciliation**: live `git ls-files` confirms flat path `knowledge/wikis/<domain>/CLAUDE.md` exists for all 4 domains; Gemini r3 attested wrong path (no `/wiki/` segment). Plan corrects.\n- **Gemini P3 quoted source_id**: regex tolerates optional quotes via `^source_id:\\\\s*\"?...\"?\\\\s*$`.\n\nHyphen-path grep: 0 matches.\n\nCross-review of v4 dispatching.","user":{"login":"vamseeachanta","name":"vamseeachanta","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23155845?v=4","id":23155845},"id":4383543277,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">v4 drafted — <code class=\"notranslate\">5c6e6bed5</code> (PyYAML attestation, classify-before-partition, code_id heuristic, is_stale)</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Branch: <code class=\"notranslate\">plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1</code> @ <code class=\"notranslate\">5c6e6bed5</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Addresses cross-converged r3 MAJOR (Claude+Gemini both):</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Gemini P1 (yaml stdlib false-claim) RESOLVED</strong>: PyYAML 6.0.3 verified as direct dep — <code class=\"notranslate\">pyproject.toml</code> has both <code class=\"notranslate\">\"pyyaml&gt;=6.0\"</code> AND <code class=\"notranslate\">\"PyYAML&gt;=6.0\"</code>; <code class=\"notranslate\">uv pip list</code> confirms. Plan body changes 'stdlib yaml' → 'yaml.safe_load/safe_dump from PyYAML 6.0+ (already in pyproject.toml)'. New test <code class=\"notranslate\">test_pyyaml_is_a_direct_dep</code> + AC.</li>\n<li><strong>Claude P2 partition/classify ordering</strong>: <code class=\"notranslate\">classify_domain</code> runs FIRST per entry, then <code class=\"notranslate\">partition_three_bucket</code> consumes (entry, domain) tuples. Maritime-law detection inside <code class=\"notranslate\">classify_domain</code>. 2 new tests.</li>\n<li><strong>Claude P2 optional_2471_fields heuristic</strong>: <code class=\"notranslate\">KNOWN_PUBLISHERS=(DNV,API,IMO,CSA,OCIMF,ABS)</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">PUBLISHER_RE</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">CODE_ID_RE</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">REVISION_RE</code>; gating requires both code_id AND publisher. Positive fixture: 'DNV-OS-E301 Rev 2024-04 mooring' → <code class=\"notranslate\">{code_id:DNV-OS-E301, publisher:DNV, revision:2024-04}</code>. Negative: NOAA tide-gauge → <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code> (keys absent).</li>\n<li><strong>Claude P2 stale-overlay signal</strong>: consumer signature → <code class=\"notranslate\">Tuple[Optional[ProcessedRecord], bool]</code>. <code class=\"notranslate\">is_stale=True</code> iff source_registry_sha256 mismatches.</li>\n<li><strong>Gemini P3 CLAUDE.md path reconciliation</strong>: live <code class=\"notranslate\">git ls-files</code> confirms flat path <code class=\"notranslate\">knowledge/wikis/&lt;domain&gt;/CLAUDE.md</code> exists for all 4 domains; Gemini r3 attested wrong path (no <code class=\"notranslate\">/wiki/</code> segment). Plan corrects.</li>\n<li><strong>Gemini P3 quoted source_id</strong>: regex tolerates optional quotes via <code class=\"notranslate\">^source_id:\\\\s*\"?...\"?\\\\s*$</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hyphen-path grep: 0 matches.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Cross-review of v4 dispatching.</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25#issuecomment-4383543297","body":"## House-cleaning note — `4aad18049`\n\nCross-branch contamination caused by a checkout-failure-then-add chain on 2026-04-25 (the v5 plan for vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 was accidentally committed to this branch as commit `5206282fe`). Reverted via `4aad18049` so the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 v5 plan no longer pollutes this branch's tree. The legitimate vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 v5 plan lives at branch `plan/issue-2369-batch-pack-2` @ `b24b3f2dc`. Adding this to memory: 'cp untracked file before failed checkout silently lands on wrong branch when commit happens before recovery.'","user"